\s1 Abishag Cares for David
\p \v 1 \rb Now King|וְהַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb was old|זָקֵ֔ן\rb* \rb and well along|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb in years|בַּיָּמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and though they covered him|וַיְכַסֻּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb with blankets|בַּבְּגָדִ֔ים\rb*, \rb he could not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb keep warm|יִחַ֖ם\rb*. \v 2 \rb So his servants|עֲבָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמְרוּ\rb* \rb to him|ל֣וֹ\rb*, “\rb Let us search for|יְבַקְשׁ֞וּ\rb* \rb a young|נַעֲרָ֣ה\rb* \rb virgin|בְתוּלָ֔ה\rb* \rb for our lord|לַאדֹנִ֤י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb to attend|וְעָֽמְדָה֙\rb* \rb to|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and|וּתְהִי־\rb* \rb care|סֹכֶ֑נֶת\rb* \rb for him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb and lie|וְשָׁכְבָ֣ה\rb* \rb by his side|בְחֵיקֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb to keep him|לַאדֹנִ֥י\rb*\rb |הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb warm|וְחַ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb Then they searched|וַיְבַקְשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb for a beautiful|יָפָ֔ה\rb* \rb girl|נַעֲרָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and they found|וַֽיִּמְצְא֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abishag|אֲבִישַׁג֙\rb* \rb the Shunammite|הַשּׁ֣וּנַמִּ֔ית\rb* \rb and brought|וַיָּבִ֥אוּ\rb* \rb her|אֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to the king|לַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb The girl|וְהַֽנַּעֲרָ֖ה\rb* \rb was unsurpassed|עַד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb in beauty|יָפָ֣ה\rb*; \rb she|וַתְּהִ֨י\rb* \rb cared|סֹכֶ֙נֶת֙\rb* \rb for the king|לַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb and served him|וַתְּשָׁ֣רְתֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb but he|וְהַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb had no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb relations with her|יְדָעָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\s1 Adonijah Usurps the Kingdom
\p \v 5 \rb At that time Adonijah|וַאֲדֹנִיָּ֧ה\rb*, \rb David’s son|בֶן־\rb* \rb by Haggith|חַגִּ֛ית\rb*, \rb began to exalt himself|מִתְנַשֵּׂ֥א\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb will be king|אֶמְלֹ֑ךְ\rb*!” \rb And he acquired|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb*\rb |ל֗וֹ\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֚כֶב\rb* \rb and horsemen|וּפָ֣רָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to run|רָצִ֥ים\rb* \rb ahead of him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 (\rb His father|אָבִ֤יו\rb* \rb had never|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |מִיָּמָיו֙\rb* \rb once reprimanded him|עֲצָב֨וֹ\rb* \rb by saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Why|מַדּ֖וּעַ\rb* \rb do you act|עָשִׂ֑יתָ\rb* \rb this way|כָּ֣כָה\rb*?” \rb Adonijah was|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְאֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb handsome|טֽוֹב־\rb*\rb |תֹּ֙אַר֙\rb*, \rb born|יָלְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb next after|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.)
\p \v 7 \rb So Adonijah|וַיִּהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb conferred|דְבָרָ֔יו\rb* \rb with|עִ֚ם\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֣ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֔ה\rb* \rb and with|וְעִ֖ם\rb* \rb Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb*, \rb who supported|וַֽיַּעְזְר֔וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb him|אֲדֹנִיָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb But Zadok|וְצָד֣וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַ֠כֹּהֵן\rb*, \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֜ע\rb*, \rb Nathan|וְנָתָ֤ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb*, \rb Shimei|וְשִׁמְעִ֣י\rb*, \rb Rei|וְרֵעִ֔י\rb*, \rb and David’s|לְדָוִ֑ד\rb* \rb mighty men|וְהַגִּבּוֹרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb would not|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb join|עִם־\rb* \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb And Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb sacrificed|וַיִּזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֤אן\rb*, \rb oxen|וּבָקָר֙\rb*, \rb and fattened calves|וּמְרִ֔יא\rb* \rb near|עִ֚ם\rb* \rb the stone|אֶ֣בֶן\rb* \rb of Zoheleth|הַזֹּחֶ֔לֶת\rb*,\f + \fr 1:9 \ft Or \fqa the Serpent’s Stone\f* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is next to|אֵ֖צֶל\rb*\rb |עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb En-rogel|רֹגֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb He invited|וַיִּקְרָ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb brothers|אֶחָיו֙\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb who were servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb But|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb he did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb invite|קָרָֽא׃\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָן֩\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֨יא\rb*, \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֜הוּ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the mighty men|הַגִּבּוֹרִ֛ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or his brother|אָחִ֖יו\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb*.
\s1 Nathan and Bathsheba before David
\p \v 11 \rb Then Nathan|נָתָ֗ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בַּת־\rb* \rb Bathsheba|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb the mother|אֵם־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Have you not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֔עַתְּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Haggith|חַגִּ֑ית\rb* \rb has become king|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb and our lord|וַאֲדֹנֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb does not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb know it|יָדָֽע׃\rb*? \v 12 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb please|נָ֖א\rb*, \rb come|לְכִ֛י\rb* \rb and let me advise|אִיעָצֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb you|עֵצָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Save|וּמַלְּטִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your own life|נַפְשֵׁ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the life|נֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of your son|בְּנֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Go|לְכִ֞י\rb* \rb at once|וּבֹ֣אִי׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַ֤רְתְּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb*, ‘\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*, \rb did you|אַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹֽא־\rb* \rb swear|נִשְׁבַּ֤עְתָּ\rb* \rb to your maidservant|לַאֲמָֽתְךָ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your son|בְנֵךְ֙\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֤ה\rb* \rb will reign|יִמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb after me|אַחֲרַ֔י\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb will sit|יֵשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my throne|כִּסְאִ֑י\rb*”? \rb Why then|וּמַדּ֖וּעַ\rb* \rb has Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb become king|מָלַ֥ךְ\rb*?’ \v 14 \rb Then|הִנֵּ֗ה\rb*, \rb while you are still|עוֹדָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֶּ֥רֶת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb I will|וַאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb come in|אָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb after you|אַחֲרַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb and confirm|וּמִלֵּאתִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your words|דְּבָרָֽיִךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb |בַת־\rb* \rb So Bathsheba|שֶׁ֤בֶע\rb* \rb went|וַתָּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb to see|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb in his bedroom|הַחַ֔דְרָה\rb*. \rb Since the king|וְהַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb was very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb old|זָקֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb Abishag|וַֽאֲבִישַׁג֙\rb* \rb the Shunammite|הַשּׁ֣וּנַמִּ֔ית\rb* \rb was serving|מְשָׁרַ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb |בַּת־\rb* \rb And Bathsheba|שֶׁ֔בַע\rb* \rb bowed down|וַתִּקֹּ֣ד\rb* \rb in homage|וַתִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb to the king|לַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb who|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is your desire|לָּֽךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 17 “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִי֙\rb*,” \rb she replied|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb you yourself|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb swore|נִשְׁבַּ֜עְתָּ\rb* \rb to your maidservant|לַֽאֲמָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*: ‘\rb Surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your son|בְנֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb* \rb will reign|יִמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb after me|אַחֲרָ֑י\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb will sit|יֵשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my throne|כִּסְאִֽי׃\rb*.’ \v 18 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb*, \rb behold|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb has become king|מָלָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and you|וְעַתָּ֛ה\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb know it|יָדָֽעְתָּ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And he has sacrificed|וַ֠יִּזְבַּח\rb* \rb an abundance|לָרֹב֒\rb* \rb of oxen|שׁ֥וֹר\rb*, \rb fattened calves|וּֽמְרִיא־\rb*, \rb and sheep|וְצֹאן֮\rb*, \rb and has invited|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb all the other|לְכָל־\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb as well as Abiathar|וּלְאֶבְיָתָר֙\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb and Joab|וּלְיֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the army|הַצָּבָ֑א\rb*. \rb But he has not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb invited|קָרָֽא׃\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb Solomon|וְלִשְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb*. \v 20 \rb And as for you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb the eyes|עֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb are upon you|עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb to tell|לְהַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb who|מִ֗י\rb* \rb will sit|יֵשֵׁ֛ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb after him|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb Otherwise, when my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb rests|כִּשְׁכַ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֑יו\rb*,\rb |וְהָיִ֗יתִי\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb and my son|וּבְנִ֥י\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb will be counted|וְהָיָ֕ה\rb* \rb as criminals|חַטָּאִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb And just then|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb*, \rb while Bathsheba was still|עוֹדֶ֥נָּה\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֶּ֖רֶת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb Nathan|וְנָתָ֥ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb arrived|בָּֽא׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb So the king|לַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb was told|וַיַּגִּ֤ידוּ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Nathan|נָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb* \rb is here|הִנֵּ֖ה\rb*.” \rb And Nathan went in|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb and bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֧חוּ\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |אַפָּ֖יו\rb*\rb |אָֽרְצָה׃\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 24 “\rb My lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָן֒\rb*, “\rb did you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb say|אָמַ֔רְתָּ\rb*, ‘\rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb will reign|יִמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb after me|אַחֲרָ֑י\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb will sit|יֵשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my throne|כִּסְאִֽי׃\rb*’? \v 25 \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb* \rb he has gone down|יָרַ֣ד\rb* \rb and sacrificed|וַ֠יִּזְבַּח\rb* \rb an abundance|לָרֹב֒\rb* \rb of oxen|שׁ֥וֹר\rb*, \rb fattened calves|וּֽמְרִיא־\rb*, \rb and sheep|וְצֹאן֮\rb*, \rb and has invited|וַיִּקְרָא֩\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*, \rb the commanders|וּלְשָׂרֵ֤י\rb*\f + \fr 1:25 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa Joab the commander\f* \rb of the army|הַצָּבָא֙\rb*, \rb and Abiathar|וּלְאֶבְיָתָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*. \rb And behold|וְהִנָּ֛ם\rb*, \rb they are eating|אֹכְלִ֥ים\rb* \rb and drinking|וְשֹׁתִ֖ים\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, ‘\rb Long live|יְחִ֖י\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*!’ \v 26 \rb But|וְלִ֣י\rb* \rb me|אֲנִֽי־\rb* \rb your servant|עַ֠בְדֶּךָ\rb* \rb he has not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb invited|קָרָֽא׃\rb*, \rb nor Zadok|וּלְצָדֹ֨ק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*, \rb nor Benaiah|וְלִבְנָיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֛ע\rb*, \rb nor your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb Solomon|וְלִשְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb*. \v 27 \rb Has|אִ֗ם\rb*\rb |מֵאֵת֙\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb let this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb happen|נִהְיָ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb informing|הוֹדַ֙עְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדֶּיךָ\rb* \rb who|מִ֗י\rb* \rb should sit|יֵשֵׁ֛ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרָֽיו׃ס\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִֽי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*?”
\s1 David Renews His Oath to Bathsheba
\p \v 28 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Call in|קִרְאוּ־\rb*\rb |לְבַת־\rb* \rb Bathsheba|שָׁ֑בַע\rb* \rb for me|לִ֖י\rb*.” \rb So she came|וַתָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb into the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽתַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb before him|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb swore an oath|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֥ע\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֕ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has redeemed|פָּדָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb distress|צָרָֽה׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I will carry out|אֶעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb this very|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb exactly|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb what|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb I swore|נִשְׁבַּ֨עְתִּי\rb* \rb to you|לָ֜ךְ\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַּיהוָ֨ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*: \rb Surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb your son|בְנֵךְ֙\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֤ה\rb* \rb will reign|יִמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb after me|אַחֲרַ֔י\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֛וּא\rb* \rb will sit|יֵשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my throne|כִּסְאִ֖י\rb* \rb in my place|תַּחְתָּ֑י\rb*.”
\p \v 31 \rb |בַּת־\rb* \rb Bathsheba|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb bowed|וַתִּקֹּ֨ד\rb* \rb facedown|אַפַּ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb in homage|וַתִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb to the king|לַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb May my lord|אֲדֹנִ֛י\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb live|יְחִ֗י\rb* \rb forever|לְעֹלָֽם׃פ\rb*!”
\s1 Solomon Anointed King
\r (1 Chronicles 29:21–25)
\p \v 32 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֗ד\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*, “\rb Call in|קִרְאוּ־\rb* \rb for me|לִ֞י\rb* \rb Zadok|לְצָד֤וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb*, \rb Nathan|וּלְנָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*, \rb and Benaiah|וְלִבְנָיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֑ע\rb*.” \rb So they came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 “\rb Take|קְח֤וּ\rb* \rb my servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אֲדֹנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּכֶם֙\rb*,”\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֗ם\rb*. “\rb Set|וְהִרְכַּבְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb my son|בְנִ֔י\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my own mule|הַפִּרְדָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb and take him down|וְהוֹרַדְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gihon|גִּחֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb There|שָׁ֠ם\rb* \rb Zadok|צָד֨וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb and Nathan|וְנָתָ֧ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֛יא\rb* \rb are to anoint|וּמָשַׁ֣ח\rb* \rb him|אֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb You are to blow|וּתְקַעְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb* \rb and declare|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֕ם\rb*, ‘\rb Long live|יְחִ֖י\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*!’ \v 35 \rb Then you shall go up|וַעֲלִיתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb with him|אַחֲרָ֗יו\rb*, \rb and he is to come|וּבָא֙\rb* \rb and sit|וְיָשַׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my throne|כִּסְאִ֔י\rb* \rb and|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb reign|יִמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in my place|תַּחְתָּ֑י\rb*. \rb For I have appointed|צִוִּ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb him|וְאֹת֤וֹ\rb*\rb |לִֽהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb ruler|נָגִ֔יד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 36 “\rb Amen|אָמֵ֑ן\rb*,”\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהֽוֹיָדָ֛ע\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*. “\rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֚ן\rb*\rb |יֹאמַ֣ר\rb* \rb declare it|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*. \v 37 \rb Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb may He be|יְהִי\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb* \rb and make his throne|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb* \rb even greater|וִֽיגַדֵּל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb than that|מִ֨כִּסֵּ֔א\rb* \rb of my lord|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*.”
\p \v 38 \rb Then Zadok|צָד֣וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַ֠כֹּהֵן\rb*, \rb Nathan|וְנָתָ֨ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֜יא\rb*, \rb and Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֗ע\rb*, \rb along with the Cherethites|וְהַכְּרֵתִי֙\rb* \rb and Pelethites|וְהַפְּלֵתִ֔י\rb*, \rb went down|וַיֵּ֣רֶד\rb* \rb and set|וַיַּרְכִּ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb mule|פִּרְדַּ֖ת\rb*, \rb and they escorted|וַיֹּלִ֥כוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb Gihon|גִּחֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 39 \rb Zadok|צָד֨וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb the horn|קֶ֤רֶן\rb* \rb of oil|הַשֶּׁ֙מֶן֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the tabernacle|הָאֹ֔הֶל\rb* \rb and anointed|וַיִּמְשַׁ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*. \rb Then they blew|וַֽיִּתְקְעוּ֙\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb proclaimed|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Long live|יְחִ֖י\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*!”
\p \v 40 \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אַֽחֲרָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְהָעָם֙\rb* \rb followed him|וַיַּעֲל֤וּ\rb*, \rb playing|מְחַלְּלִ֣ים\rb* \rb flutes|בַּחֲלִלִ֔ים\rb* \rb and rejoicing|וּשְׂמֵחִ֖ים\rb* \rb with such a great|גְדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb joy|שִׂמְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb that the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb was split|וַתִּבָּקַ֥ע\rb* \rb by the sound|בְּקוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.
\s1 Adonijah Learns of Solomon’s Kingship
\p \v 41 \rb Now|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his guests|הַקְּרֻאִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb were finishing|כִּלּ֣וּ\rb* \rb their feast|לֶאֱכֹ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb when they heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb the sound|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the ram’s horn|הַשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb*. “\rb Why is|מַדּ֥וּעַ\rb* \rb the city|הַקִּרְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb in such a loud|קֽוֹל־\rb* \rb uproar|הוֹמָֽה׃\rb*?” \rb asked|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.
\p \v 42 \rb As he was|עוֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּ֔ר\rb*, \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֛ן\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֥ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb arrived|בָּ֑א\rb*. “\rb Come in|בֹּ֔א\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַ֖תָּה\rb* \rb are a man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of valor|חַ֛יִל\rb*. \rb You must be bringing good|וְט֥וֹב\rb* \rb news|תְּבַשֵּֽׂר׃\rb*.”
\p \v 43 “\rb Not at all|אֲבָ֕ל\rb*,” \rb Jonathan|יוֹנָתָ֔ן\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֙עַן֙\rb*\rb |לַאֲדֹנִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*. “\rb Our lord|אֲדֹנֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb has made Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb* \rb king|הִמְלִ֥יךְ\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 44 \rb And with Solomon|אִתּֽוֹ־\rb*, \rb the king|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb Zadok|צָד֨וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Nathan|נָתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb*, \rb and Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְה֣וֹיָדָ֔ע\rb*, \rb along with the Cherethites|וְהַכְּרֵתִ֖י\rb* \rb and Pelethites|וְהַפְּלֵתִ֑י\rb*, \rb and they have set|וַיַּרְכִּ֣בוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb mule|פִּרְדַּ֥ת\rb*. \v 45 \rb Zadok|צָד֣וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb and Nathan|וְנָתָן֩\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֨יא\rb* \rb have anointed|וַיִּמְשְׁח֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֡וֹ\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb at Gihon|בְּגִח֗וֹן\rb*, \rb and they have gone up|וַיַּעֲל֤וּ\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁם֙\rb* \rb with rejoicing|שְׂמֵחִ֔ים\rb* \rb that rings out|וַתֵּהֹ֖ם\rb* \rb in the city|הַקִּרְיָ֑ה\rb*. \rb That is|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb the noise|הַקּ֖וֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you hear|שְׁמַעְתֶּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 46 \rb Moreover|וְגַם֙\rb*, \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb has taken his seat|יָשַׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the royal|הַמְּלוּכָֽה׃\rb* \rb throne|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 47 \rb The king’s|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb have also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb gone|בָּ֜אוּ\rb* \rb to congratulate|לְ֠בָרֵךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our lord|אֲדֹנֵ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֮\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹר֒\rb*, ‘\rb May your God|אֱלֹהֶיךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb make the name|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb more famous|יֵיטֵ֨ב\rb* \rb than your own name|מִשְּׁמֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and may He make his throne|כִּסְא֖וֹ\rb* \rb greater|וִֽיגַדֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb than your throne|מִכִּסְאֶ֑ךָ\rb*.’
\p \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb has bowed in worship|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֥חוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his bed|הַמִּשְׁכָּֽב׃\rb*, \v 48 \rb |וְגַם־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb saying|אָמַ֣ר\rb*\rb |כָּ֖כָה\rb*, ‘\rb Blessed be|בָּר֨וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*! \rb Today|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb He|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has provided one|נָתַ֥ן\rb*\f + \fr 1:48 \ft LXX \fqa one of my offspring\f* \rb to sit|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my throne|כִּסְאִ֖י\rb*, \rb and my eyes|וְעֵינַ֥י\rb* \rb have seen it|רֹאֽוֹת׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 49 \rb At this, all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the guests|הַ֨קְּרֻאִ֔ים\rb* \rb of Adonijah|לַאֲדֹנִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb arose|וַיָּקֻ֔מוּ\rb* \rb in terror|וַיֶּֽחֶרְדוּ֙\rb* \rb and scattered|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |לְדַרְכּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 50 \rb But Adonijah|וַאֲדֹ֣נִיָּ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb in fear|יָרֵ֖א\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb to take hold|וַֽיַּחֲזֵ֖ק\rb* \rb of the horns|בְּקַרְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 51 \rb It was reported|וַיֻּגַּ֤ד\rb* \rb to Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb*: “\rb Behold|הִנֵּה֙\rb*, \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹ֣נִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb fears|יָרֵ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*,\rb |וְ֠הִנֵּה\rb* \rb and he has taken hold|אָחַ֞ז\rb* \rb of the horns|בְּקַרְנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Let King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb first|כַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb swear|יִשָּֽׁבַֽע־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֤י\rb* \rb not|אִם־\rb* \rb to put|יָמִ֥ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his servant|עַבְדּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to the sword|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 52 \rb And Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb If|אִ֚ם\rb* \rb he is|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a man|לְבֶן־\rb* \rb of character|חַ֔יִל\rb*, \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb a single hair of his|מִשַּׂעֲרָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb will fall|יִפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb to the ground|אָ֑רְצָה\rb*. \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb evil|רָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb is found|תִמָּצֵא־\rb* \rb in him|ב֖וֹ\rb*, \rb he will die|וָמֵֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 53 \rb So King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb summoned Adonijah|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb down|וַיֹּרִדֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*, \rb and he came|וַיָּבֹ֕א\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb before King|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb who|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb to him|ל֥וֹ\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb to your home|לְבֵיתֶֽךָ׃פ\rb*.”
\c 2
\s1 David Instructs Solomon
\r (Psalm 37:1–40)
\p \v 1 \rb As the time|יְמֵֽי־\rb* \rb drew near|וַיִּקְרְב֥וּ\rb* \rb for David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb to die|לָמ֑וּת\rb*, \rb he charged|וַיְצַ֛ו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֥ה\rb*, \v 2 “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb am about to go|הֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb the way|בְּדֶ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb So be strong|וְחָזַקְתָּ֖\rb* \rb and prove yourself|וְהָיִ֥יתָֽ\rb* \rb a man|לְאִֽישׁ׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb And keep|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֞\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the charge|מִשְׁמֶ֣רֶת׀\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb to walk|לָלֶ֤כֶת\rb* \rb in His ways|בִּדְרָכָיו֙\rb* \rb and to keep|לִשְׁמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb His statutes|חֻקֹּתָ֤יו\rb*, \rb commandments|מִצְוֺתָיו֙\rb*, \rb ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֣יו\rb*, \rb and decrees|וְעֵדְוֺתָ֔יו\rb*, \rb as written|כַּכָּת֖וּב\rb* \rb in the Law|בְּתוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moses|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you may prosper|תַּשְׂכִּ֗יל\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb* \rb you do|תַּֽעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and wherever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you turn|תִּפְנֶ֖ה\rb*,\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 4 \rb and so that|לְמַעַן֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb may fulfill|יָקִ֨ים\rb* \rb His promise|דְּבָר֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb to me|עָלַי֮\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb* ‘\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb your descendants|בָנֶ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |דַּרְכָּ֗ם\rb* \rb take heed|יִשְׁמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to walk|לָלֶ֤כֶת\rb* \rb faithfully|בֶּאֱמֶ֔ת\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַי֙\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their heart|לְבָבָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb and soul|נַפְשָׁ֑ם\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֕ר\rb* \rb you will never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb fail|יִכָּרֵ֤ת\rb*\rb |לְךָ֙\rb* \rb to have a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb on|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’
\p \v 5 \rb Moreover|וְגַ֣ם\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֡עְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֣ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָ֗ה\rb* \rb did|עָ֨שָׂה\rb* \rb to me|לִ֜י\rb*— \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he did|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb to Abner|לְאַבְנֵ֨ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵ֜ר\rb* \rb and Amasa|וְלַעֲמָשָׂ֤א\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jether|יֶ֙תֶר֙\rb*,\f + \fr 2:5 \fqa Jether \ft is a variant of \fqa Ithra\ft ; also in verse 32; see 2 Samuel 17:25.\f* \rb the two|לִשְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the armies|צִבְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb*. \rb He killed them|וַיַּ֣הַרְגֵ֔ם\rb* \rb in peacetime|בְּשָׁלֹ֑ם\rb* \rb to avenge|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb* \rb the blood|דְּמֵֽי־\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*. \rb He stained|וַיִּתֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb with the blood|דְּמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb the belt|בַּחֲגֹֽרָתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb around his waist|בְּמָתְנָ֔יו\rb* \rb and the sandals|וּֽבְנַעֲל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on his feet|בְּרַגְלָֽיו׃\rb*.\f + \fr 2:5 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa He stained with innocent blood the belt around my waist and the sandals on my feet.\f* \v 6 \rb So act|וְעָשִׂ֖יתָ\rb* \rb according to your wisdom|כְּחָכְמָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb and do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb let his gray head|שֵׂיבָת֛וֹ\rb* \rb go down|תוֹרֵ֧ד\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁאֹֽל׃ס\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁלֹ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb But show|תַּֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֔סֶד\rb*\f + \fr 2:7 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb to the sons|וְלִבְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Barzillai|בַרְזִלַּ֤י\rb* \rb the Gileadite|הַגִּלְעָדִי֙\rb*, \rb and let them be|וְהָי֖וּ\rb* \rb among those who eat|בְּאֹכְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb at your table|שֻׁלְחָנֶ֑ךָ\rb*, \rb because|כִּי־\rb*\rb |כֵן֙\rb* \rb they stood by|קָרְב֣וּ\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb when I fled|בְּבָרְחִ֕י\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your brother|אָחִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Keep an eye on|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb Shimei|שִֽׁמְעִ֨י\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Gera|גֵּרָ֥א\rb*,\rb |בֶן־\rb* \rb the Benjamite|הַיְמִינִי֮\rb* \rb from Bahurim|מִבַּחֻרִים֒\rb* \rb who is with you|עִ֠מְּךָ\rb*. \rb He|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb called down bitter|נִמְרֶ֔צֶת\rb* \rb curses against me|קִֽלְלַ֙נִי֙\rb*\rb |קְלָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb I went|לֶכְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to Mahanaim|מַחֲנָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb but when|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb he came down|יָרַ֤ד\rb* \rb to meet me|לִקְרָאתִי֙\rb* \rb at the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*, \rb I swore|וָאֶשָּׁ֨בַֽע\rb* \rb to him|ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַֽיהוָה֙\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* ‘\rb I will never|אִם־\rb* \rb put you|אֲמִֽיתְךָ֖\rb* \rb to the sword|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃\rb*.’ \v 9 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb hold him guiltless|תְּנַקֵּ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb are a wise|חָכָ֖ם\rb* \rb man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*. \rb You know|וְיָֽדַעְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you ought to do|תַּֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb to him|לּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb to bring his gray head|שֵׂיבָת֛וֹ\rb* \rb down|וְהוֹרַדְתָּ֧\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁאֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb in blood|בְּדָ֖ם\rb*.”
\s1 David’s Reign and Death
\r (1 Chronicles 29:26–30)
\p \v 10 \rb Then David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִֽד׃פ\rb*. \v 11 \rb The length|וְהַיָּמִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb of David’s|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb reign|מָלַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb was forty|אַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* —\rb |מָלַךְ֙\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֤וֹן\rb* \rb and thirty-three|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׁלֹ֖שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|וּבִירוּשָׁלִַ֣ם\rb*\rb |מָלַ֔ךְ\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb So Solomon|וּשְׁלֹמֹ֕ה\rb* \rb sat|יָשַׁ֕ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֖א\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb and his kingdom|מַלְכֻת֖וֹ\rb* \rb was firmly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb established|וַתִּכֹּ֥ן\rb*.
\s1 The Execution of Adonijah
\p \v 13 \rb Now Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Haggith|חַגֵּ֗ית\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֞א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בַּת־\rb* \rb Bathsheba|שֶׁ֙בַע֙\rb* \rb the mother|אֵם־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb and she asked|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Do you come|בֹּאֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb in peace|הֲשָׁל֣וֹם\rb*?”
\p “\rb Yes, in peace|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*. \v 14 \rb Then he said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I|לִ֖י\rb* \rb have something to tell|דָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אֵלָ֑יִךְ\rb*.”
\p “\rb Say it|דַּבֵּֽר׃\rb*,” \rb she answered|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 15 “\rb You|אַ֤תְּ\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֙עַתְּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb the kingship|הַמְּלוּכָ֔ה\rb*\rb |לִי֙\rb* \rb was mine|הָיְתָ֣ה\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*. “\rb All|כָֽל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb expected|וְעָלַ֞י\rb*\rb |שָׂ֧מוּ\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb that I should reign|לִמְלֹ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb but the kingship|הַמְּלוּכָה֙\rb* \rb has turned|וַתִּסֹּ֤ב\rb* \rb to my brother|לְאָחִ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it has come|הָ֥יְתָה\rb* \rb to him|לּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb from the LORD|מֵיְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 16 \rb So now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb*\rb |שֹׁאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb have just one|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb request|שְׁאֵלָ֤ה\rb* \rb of you|מֵֽאִתָּ֔ךְ\rb*; \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb deny|תָּשִׁ֖בִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb me|פָּנָ֑י\rb*.”
\p “\rb State your request|דַּבֵּֽר׃\rb*,” \rb she told|וַתֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Adonijah replied|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Please|נָא֙\rb* \rb speak|אִמְרִי־\rb* \rb to King|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb turn you down|יָשִׁ֖יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֑יִךְ\rb*. \rb Let him give|וְיִתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abishag|אֲבִישַׁ֥ג\rb* \rb the Shunammite|הַשּׁוּנַמִּ֖ית\rb* \rb as my wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 “\rb Very well|ט֑וֹב\rb*,”\rb |בַּת־\rb* \rb Bathsheba|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb replied|וַתֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*. “\rb I|אָנֹכִ֕י\rb* \rb will speak|אֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb for you|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb |בַת־\rb* \rb So Bathsheba|שֶׁ֙בַע֙\rb* \rb went|וַתָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֶּר־\rb* \rb to him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb The king|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb stood up|וַיָּקָם֩\rb* \rb to greet her|לִקְרָאתָ֜הּ\rb*, \rb bowed|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֣חוּ\rb* \rb to her|לָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb and sat down|וַיֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his throne|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb*. \rb Then the king had a throne|כִּסֵּא֙\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb* \rb for his|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb mother|לְאֵ֣ם\rb*, \rb who sat down|וַתֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb at his right hand|לִֽימִינֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 “\rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb have just one|אַחַ֤ת\rb* \rb small|קְטַנָּה֙\rb* \rb request of you|שְׁאֵלָ֨ה\rb*,” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*. “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb deny|תָּ֖שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb me|פָּנָ֑י\rb*.”
\p “\rb Make your request|שֹׁאֶ֣לֶת\rb*,\rb |מֵֽאִתָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb my mother|אִמִּ֔י\rb*,” \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |שַׁאֲלִ֣י\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb deny|אָשִׁ֖יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you|פָּנָֽיִךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb So Bathsheba said|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Let Abishag|אֲבִישַׁ֣ג\rb* \rb the Shunammite|הַשֻּׁנַמִּ֑ית\rb* \rb be given|יֻתַּ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to your brother|אָחִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb Adonijah|לַאֲדֹנִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb as his wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּעַן֩\rb* \rb his mother|לְאִמּ֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Why|וְלָמָה֩\rb* \rb do you|אַ֨תְּ\rb* \rb request|שֹׁאֶ֜לֶת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abishag|אֲבִישַׁ֤ג\rb* \rb the Shunammite|הַשֻּׁנַמִּית֙\rb* \rb for Adonijah|לַאֲדֹ֣נִיָּ֔הוּ\rb*? \rb Since|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is my older|הַגָּד֣וֹל\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נִּי\rb* \rb brother|אָחִ֖י\rb*, \rb you might as well request|וְשַֽׁאֲלִי־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמְּלוּכָ֔ה\rb* \rb for him|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb and for Abiathar|וּלְאֶבְיָתָ֣ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb and for Joab|וּלְיוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Zeruiah|צְרוּיָֽה׃פ\rb*!”
\p \v 23 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb swore|וַיִּשָּׁבַע֙\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*:\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* “\rb May God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb punish|כֹּ֣ה\rb*\rb |יַֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֤י\rb*, \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely|יוֹסִ֔יף\rb*, \rb if|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹ֣נִיָּ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has not made|דִּבֶּר֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb request|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb at the expense of his life|בְנַפְשׁ֔וֹ\rb*. \v 24 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb*, \rb as surely as the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb* — \rb the One|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb who established me|הֱכִינַ֗נִי\rb*, \rb who set me|וַיּוֹשִׁיבִינִי\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּא֙\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb and who founded|עָֽשָׂה־\rb* \rb for me|לִ֛י\rb* \rb a dynasty|בַּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb as|וַאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb He promised|דִּבֵּ֑ר\rb*— \rb surely|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb shall be put to death|יוּמַ֖ת\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*!”
\p \v 25 \rb So King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb gave orders|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb to|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֑ע\rb*, \rb and he struck down|וַיִּפְגַּע־\rb* \rb Adonijah|בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to Abiathar|וּלְאֶבְיָתָ֨ר\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*, “\rb Go back|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb your fields|שָׂדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb in Anathoth|עֲנָתֹת֙\rb*. \rb Even though|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb you|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb deserve to die|מָ֖וֶת\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb put you to death|אֲמִיתֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb at this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb time|וּבַיּ֨וֹם\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you carried|נָשָׂ֜אתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֤י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִה֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֔י\rb*\rb |וְכִ֣י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb and you suffered|הִתְעַנִּ֔יתָ\rb* \rb through all|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb suffered|הִתְעַנָּ֖ה\rb*.” \v 27 \rb So Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb banished|וַיְגָ֤רֶשׁ\rb* \rb Abiathar|אֶבְיָתָ֔ר\rb* \rb from|מִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb the priesthood|כֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and thus fulfilled|לְמַלֵּא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֛ר\rb* \rb at Shiloh|בְּשִׁלֹֽה׃פ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Eli|עֵלִ֖י\rb*.
\s1 The Execution of Joab
\p \v 28 \rb When the news|וְהַשְּׁמֻעָה֙\rb* \rb reached|בָּ֣אָה\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb*,\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb who|יוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb had conspired|נָטָה֙\rb* \rb with|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Adonijah|אֲדֹנִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb but|וְאַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb with|נָטָ֑ה\rb* \rb Absalom|אַבְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb*, \rb he|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּ֤נָס\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and took hold|וַֽיַּחֲזֵ֖ק\rb* \rb of the horns|בְּקַרְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb It was reported|וַיֻּגַּ֞ד\rb* \rb to King|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb*:\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* “\rb Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb has fled|נָ֤ס\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and is now|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*.”
\p \rb So Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֛ע\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb strike him down|פְּגַע־\rb*\rb |בּֽוֹ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 30 \rb And Benaiah|בְנָיָ֜הוּ\rb* \rb entered|וַיָּבֹ֨א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Joab|אֵלָ֜יו\rb*, “\rb |כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb The king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֤ר\rb*, ‘\rb Come out|צֵ֔א\rb*!’”
\p \rb But Joab replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר׀\rb*, “\rb No|לֹ֖א\rb*,\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I will die|אָמ֑וּת\rb* \rb here|פֹ֣ה\rb*.”
\p \rb So Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֤הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb relayed the message|דָּבָ֣ר\rb*\rb |וַיָּ֨שֶׁב\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb This is how|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb*\rb |דִבֶּ֥ר\rb*\rb |וְכֹ֥ה\rb* \rb answered me|עָנָֽנִי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 31 \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*\rb |ל֣וֹ\rb*, “\rb Do|עֲשֵׂה֙\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he says|דִּבֶּ֔ר\rb*. \rb Strike him down|וּפְגַע־\rb*\rb |בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and bury him|וּקְבַרְתּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and so remove|וַהֲסִירֹ֣תָ׀\rb* \rb from me|מֵעָלַ֕י\rb* \rb and from|וּמֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb the innocent|חִנָּ֗ם\rb* \rb blood|דְּמֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb shed|שָׁפַ֣ךְ\rb*. \v 32 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will bring|וְהֵשִׁיב֩\rb* \rb his bloodshed|דָּמ֜וֹ\rb* \rb back upon|עַל־\rb* \rb his own head|רֹאשׁ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb for|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb without|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb the knowledge|יָדָ֑ע\rb* \rb of my father|וְאָבִ֥י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb he struck down|פָּגַ֣ע\rb* \rb two|בִּשְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb men|אֲ֠נָשִׁים\rb* \rb more righteous|צַדִּקִ֨ים\rb* \rb and better|וְטֹבִ֤ים\rb* \rb than he|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb when he put|וַיַּהַרְגֵ֣ם\rb* \rb to the sword|בַּחֶ֔רֶב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abner|אַבְנֵ֤ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ner|נֵר֙\rb*, \rb commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb army|צְבָ֣א\rb*, \rb and Amasa|עֲמָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jether|יֶ֖תֶר\rb*, \rb commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of Judah’s|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb army|צְבָ֥א\rb*. \v 33 \rb Their blood|דְמֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb will come back|וְשָׁ֤בוּ\rb* \rb upon the heads|בְּרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of Joab|יוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb and|וּבְרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb his descendants forever|זַרְע֖וֹ\rb*\rb |לְעֹלָ֑ם\rb*; \rb but for David|וּלְדָוִ֡ד\rb*, \rb his descendants|וּ֠לְזַרְעוֹ\rb*, \rb his house|וּלְבֵית֨וֹ\rb*, \rb and his throne|וּלְכִסְא֜וֹ\rb*, \rb there shall be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb peace|שָׁל֛וֹם\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֥ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֖ם\rb*.”
\p \v 34 \rb So Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְה֣וֹיָדָ֔ע\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֗עַל\rb*, \rb struck down Joab|וַיִּפְגַּע־\rb*, \rb and killed him|וַיְמִתֵ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb He was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb at his own home|בְּבֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb appointed|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֛ע\rb* \rb in Joab’s place|תַּחְתָּ֖יו\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the army|הַצָּבָ֑א\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and he appointed|נָתַ֣ן\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zadok|צָד֤וֹק\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb in Abiathar’s|אֶבְיָתָֽר׃\rb* \rb place|תַּ֖חַת\rb*.
\s1 The Execution of Shimei
\p \v 36 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb Shimei|לְשִׁמְעִ֔י\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|ל֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Build|בְּֽנֵה־\rb* \rb a house|בַ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and live|וְיָשַׁבְתָּ֖\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*, \rb but do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|תֵצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb anywhere else|אָ֥נֶה\rb*\rb |וָאָֽנָה׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb On the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb you go out|צֵאתְךָ֗\rb* \rb and cross|וְעָֽבַרְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Kidron|קִדְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb Valley|נַ֣חַל\rb*, \rb know for sure|יָדֹ֥עַ\rb*\rb |תֵּדַ֖ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you will die|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמ֑וּת\rb*; \rb your blood|דָּמְךָ֖\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb on your own head|בְרֹאשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 38 “\rb The sentence|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb is fair|ט֣וֹב\rb*,” \rb Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֤י\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |לַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*. “\rb Your servant|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֶּר֙\rb*.” \rb And Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֛י\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּ֧שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb for a long|רַבִּֽים׃ס\rb* \rb time|יָמִ֥ים\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb After|מִקֵּץ֙\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb however|וַיְהִ֗י\rb*, \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Shimei’s|לְשִׁמְעִ֔י\rb* \rb slaves|עֲבָדִים֙\rb* \rb ran away|וַיִּבְרְח֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Maacah|מַעֲכָ֖ה\rb*,\f + \fr 2:39 \fqa Maacah \ft is a variant of \fqa Maoch\ft ; see 1 Samuel 27:2.\f* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Gath|גַּ֑ת\rb*. \rb And Shimei|לְשִׁמְעִי֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb was told|וַיַּגִּ֤ידוּ\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb your slaves|עֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb are in Gath|בְּגַֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 40 \rb |וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb So Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֗י\rb* \rb saddled|וַֽיַּחֲבֹשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his donkey|חֲמֹר֔וֹ\rb* \rb and set out|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Achish|אָכִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb at Gath|גַּ֙תָה֙\rb* \rb in search of|לְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his slaves|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb*,\rb |שִׁמְעִ֔י\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and he brought them|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb back|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from Gath|מִגַּֽת׃\rb*.
\p \v 41 \rb When Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb* \rb was told|וַיֻּגַּ֖ד\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb Shimei|שִׁמְעִ֧י\rb* \rb had gone|הָלַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִירוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb to Gath|גַּ֖ת\rb* \rb and had returned|וַיָּשֹֽׁב׃\rb*, \v 42 \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb Shimei|לְשִׁמְעִ֗י\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb*, “\rb Did I not|הֲל֧וֹא\rb* \rb make you swear|הִשְׁבַּעְתִּ֣יךָ\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and warn|וָאָעִ֤ד\rb* \rb you|בְּךָ֙\rb*, ‘\rb On the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb you leave|צֵאתְךָ֗\rb* \rb and go|וְהָֽלַכְתָּ֙\rb* \rb elsewhere|אָ֣נֶה\rb*\rb |וָאָ֔נָה\rb*, \rb know for sure|יָדֹ֥עַ\rb*\rb |תֵּדַ֖ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you will die|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמ֑וּת\rb*’? \rb And you told|וַתֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֛י\rb*, ‘\rb The sentence|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb is fair|ט֥וֹב\rb*; \rb I will comply|שָׁמָֽעְתִּי׃\rb*.’ \v 43 \rb So why|וּמַדּ֕וּעַ\rb* \rb have you not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb kept|שָׁמַ֔רְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb your oath|שְׁבֻעַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the command|הַמִּצְוָ֖ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I gave you|צִוִּ֥יתִי\rb*?”\rb |עָלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 44 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |שִׁמְעִ֗י\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֙עְתָּ֙\rb* \rb in your heart|לְבָ֣בְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the evil|הָרָעָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |יָדַע֙\rb* \rb you did|עָשִׂ֖יתָ\rb* \rb to my father|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֣ד\rb*. \rb Therefore the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will bring|וְהֵשִׁ֧יב\rb* \rb your evil|רָעָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb back upon your head|בְּרֹאשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb*. \v 45 \rb But King|וְהַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb will be blessed|בָּר֑וּךְ\rb* \rb and David’s|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb throne|וְכִסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb will remain|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb secure|נָכ֛וֹן\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 46 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְה֣וֹיָדָ֔ע\rb*, \rb and he went out|וַיֵּצֵ֕א\rb* \rb and struck Shimei down|וַיִּפְגַּע־\rb*\rb |בּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and he died|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb*. \rb Thus the kingdom|וְהַמַּמְלָכָ֥ה\rb* \rb was firmly established|נָכ֖וֹנָה\rb* \rb in the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 Solomon’s Prayer for Wisdom
\r (2 Chronicles 1:1–13; Psalm 45:1–17; Psalm 72:1–20)
\p \v 1 \rb Later, Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb formed an alliance|וַיִּתְחַתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb by marrying|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb*. \rb Solomon brought her|וַיְבִיאֶ֙הָ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the City|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb he had finished|כַּלֹּת֗וֹ\rb* \rb building|לִבְנ֤וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his palace|בֵּיתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the wall|חוֹמַ֥ת\rb* \rb around|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb The people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb however|רַ֣ק\rb*, \rb were still sacrificing|מְזַבְּחִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the high places|בַּבָּמ֑וֹת\rb* \rb because|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb a house|בַ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb yet|עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |הָהֵֽם׃פ\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֥ים\rb* \rb been built|נִבְנָ֥ה\rb*. \v 3 \rb And Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb loved|וַיֶּאֱהַ֤ב\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and walked|לָלֶ֕כֶת\rb* \rb in the statutes|בְּחֻקּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb except that|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb sacrificed|מְזַבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb and burned incense|וּמַקְטִֽיר׃\rb* \rb on the high places|בַּבָּמ֔וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Now the king|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Gibeon|גִּבְעֹ֙נָה֙\rb* \rb to sacrifice|לִזְבֹּ֣חַ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it was|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb the great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֑ה\rb* \rb high place|הַבָּמָ֣ה\rb*. \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb offered|יַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֤לֶף\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the|הַהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb altar there|הַמִּזְבֵּ֥חַ\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb One night|הַלָּ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb at Gibeon|בְּגִבְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהֹוָ֛ה\rb* \rb appeared|נִרְאָ֧ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb in a dream|בַּחֲל֣וֹם\rb*, \rb and God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Ask|שְׁאַ֖ל\rb*\rb |מָ֥ה\rb*, \rb and I will give it|אֶתֶּן־\rb* \rb to you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 6 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb have shown|עָשִׂ֜יתָ\rb* \rb much|גָּדוֹל֒\rb* \rb loving devotion|חֶ֣סֶד\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb*, \rb my father|אָבִי֮\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb because|כַּאֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb he walked|הָלַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb in faithfulness|בֶּאֱמֶ֧ת\rb*, \rb righteousness|וּבִצְדָקָ֛ה\rb*, \rb and uprightness|וּבְיִשְׁרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of heart|לֵבָ֖ב\rb*\rb |עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb And You have maintained|וַתִּשְׁמָר־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb loving devotion|הַחֶ֤סֶד\rb* \rb by giving|וַתִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb a son|בֵ֛ן\rb* \rb to sit|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his throne|כִּסְא֖וֹ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb very day|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb And now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָ֔י\rb*, \rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb have made Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb king|הִמְלַ֣כְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb in my father|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb place|תַּ֖חַת\rb*. \rb But I am|וְאָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb only a little|קָטֹ֔ן\rb* \rb child|נַ֣עַר\rb*, \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb knowing how|אֵדַ֖ע\rb* \rb to go out|צֵ֥את\rb* \rb or come in|וָבֹֽא׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Your servant|וְעַ֨בְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb is here among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the people|עַמְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You have chosen|בָּחָ֑רְתָּ\rb*, \rb a people|עַם־\rb*\rb |רָ֕ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb too numerous|מֵרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb to count|יִמָּנֶ֛ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or number|יִסָּפֵ֖ר\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Therefore give|וְנָתַתָּ֨\rb* \rb Your servant|לְעַבְדְּךָ֜\rb* \rb an understanding|שֹׁמֵ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֤ב\rb* \rb to judge|לִשְׁפֹּ֣ט\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb and to discern|לְהָבִ֖ין\rb* \rb between|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb and evil|לְרָ֑ע\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb is able|יוּכַל֙\rb* \rb to govern|לִשְׁפֹּ֔ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb great|הַכָּבֵ֖ד\rb* \rb people of Yours|עַמְּךָ֥\rb*?”
\p \v 10 \rb Now it|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb pleased|וַיִּיטַ֥ב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb*\f + \fr 3:10 \ft Hebrew \fqa Adonai\ft ; also in verse 15\f* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb had made this request|שָׁאַ֣ל\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb So God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Since|יַעַן֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb you have asked for|שָׁאַ֜לְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb instead of|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb requesting|שָׁאַ֨לְתָּ\rb* \rb long|רַבִּ֗ים\rb* \rb life|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb wealth|עֹ֔שֶׁר\rb* \rb for yourself|לְּךָ֙\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |שָׁאַ֖לְתָּ\rb* \rb death|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb for your enemies|אֹיְבֶ֑יךָ\rb* — \rb but you have asked|וְשָׁאַ֧לְתָּ\rb* \rb for discernment|הָבִ֖ין\rb* \rb to administer|לִשְׁמֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb* — \v 12 \rb behold|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb I will do|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb what you have asked|כִּדְבָרֶ֑יךָ\rb*.\rb |הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb I will give|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֗\rb* \rb a wise|חָכָ֣ם\rb* \rb and discerning|וְנָב֔וֹן\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֚ב\rb*, \rb so that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb there will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb have been|הָיָ֣ה\rb*\rb |לְפָנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb another|וְאַחֲרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb like you|כָּמ֙וֹךָ֙\rb*, \rb nor|לֹא־\rb* \rb will there ever be|יָק֥וּם\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Moreover|וְגַ֨ם\rb*, \rb I will give|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb request|שָׁאַ֙לְתָּ֙\rb* — \rb both|גַּם־\rb* \rb riches|עֹ֖שֶׁר\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb honor|כָּב֑וֹד\rb* — \rb so that|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb during all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your days|יָמֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb in any kingdom|בַּמְּלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb will be|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb your equal|כָמ֥וֹךָ\rb*. \v 14 \rb So if|וְאִ֣ם׀\rb* \rb you walk|תֵּלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in My ways|בִּדְרָכַ֗י\rb* \rb and keep|לִשְׁמֹ֤ר\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקַּי֙\rb* \rb and commandments|וּמִצְוֺתַ֔י\rb*, \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣יד\rb* \rb did|הָלַ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb I will prolong|וְהַאַרַכְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb your days|יָמֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb Then Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb awoke|וַיִּקַ֥ץ\rb*, \rb and indeed it had been|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb a dream|חֲל֑וֹם\rb*. \rb So he returned|וַיָּב֨וֹא\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb*, \rb stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֣ד׀\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֗י\rb*, \rb and offered|וַיַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹלוֹת֙\rb* \rb and peace offerings|שְׁלָמִ֔ים\rb*.\rb |וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb Then he held|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb a feast|מִשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Solomon Judges Wisely
\p \v 16 \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb two|שְׁתַּ֛יִם\rb*\rb |נָשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb prostitutes|זֹנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb came|תָּבֹ֗אנָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽתַּעֲמֹ֖דְנָה\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb One|הָֽאַחַת֙\rb* \rb woman|הָאִשָּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֜אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Please|בִּ֣י\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*, \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb woman|וְהָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb live|יֹשְׁבֹ֖ת\rb* \rb in the same|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb house|בְּבַ֣יִת\rb*, \rb and I gave birth|וָאֵלֵ֥ד\rb* \rb while she was|עִמָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבָּֽיִת׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb On the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁי֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb after I gave birth|לְלִדְתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb this woman|הָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb had a baby|וַתֵּ֖לֶד\rb*. \rb We|וַאֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb were alone|יַחְדָּ֗ו\rb*, \rb with|אִתָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb one|זָ֤ר\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb but|זוּלָתִ֥י\rb* \rb the two|שְׁתַּֽיִם־\rb* \rb of us|אֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb*\rb |בַּבָּֽיִת׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb During the night|לָ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb woman’s|הָאִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֛מָת\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb she rolled over|שָׁכְבָ֖ה\rb* \rb on him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb So she got up|וַתָּקָם֩\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּת֨וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the night|הַלַּ֜יְלָה\rb* \rb and took|וַתִּקַּ֧ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֣י\rb* \rb from my side|מֵֽאֶצְלִ֗י\rb* \rb while|וַאֲמָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb I was asleep|יְשֵׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb She laid him|וַתַּשְׁכִּיבֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in her bosom|בְּחֵיקָ֑הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and put|הִשְׁכִּ֥יבָה\rb* \rb her dead|הַמֵּ֖ת\rb* \rb son|בְּנָ֥הּ\rb* \rb at my bosom|בְחֵיקִֽי׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb The next morning|בַּבֹּ֛קֶר\rb*, \rb when I got up|וָאָקֻ֥ם\rb* \rb to nurse|לְהֵינִ֥יק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֖י\rb*, \rb I discovered|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb he was dead|מֵ֑ת\rb*.\rb |בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb But when I examined him|וָאֶתְבּוֹנֵ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb*, \rb I realized|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb that he was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb the son|בְנִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had borne|יָלָֽדְתִּי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 “\rb No|לֹ֣א\rb*,”\rb |כִ֗י\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb the other|הָאַחֶ֜רֶת\rb* \rb woman|הָאִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*, “\rb the living one is|הַחַי֙\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֤י\rb* \rb and the dead one is|הַמֵּ֔ת\rb* \rb your son|וּבְנֵ֣ךְ\rb*.”
\p \rb But the first woman|וְזֹ֤את\rb* \rb insisted|אֹמֶ֙רֶת֙\rb*, “\rb No|לֹ֣א\rb*,\rb |כִ֔י\rb* \rb the dead one is|הַמֵּ֖ת\rb* \rb yours|בְּנֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and the living one is|הֶחָ֑י\rb* \rb mine|וּבְנִ֣י\rb*.” \rb So they argued|וַתְּדַבֵּ֖רְנָה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This|זֹ֣את\rb* \rb woman says|אֹמֶ֔רֶת\rb*, ‘\rb |זֶה־\rb* \rb My son|בְּנִ֥י\rb* \rb is alive|הַחַ֖י\rb* \rb and yours|וּבְנֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb is dead|הַמֵּ֑ת\rb*,’ \rb but that|וְזֹ֤את\rb* \rb woman says|אֹמֶ֙רֶת֙\rb*, ‘\rb No|לֹ֣א\rb*,\rb |כִ֔י\rb* \rb your son|בְּנֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb is dead|הַמֵּ֖ת\rb* \rb and mine|וּבְנִ֥י\rb* \rb is alive|הֶחָֽי׃פ\rb*.’”
\p \v 24 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb continued|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Bring|קְח֣וּ\rb* \rb me|לִי־\rb* \rb a sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb*.” \rb So they brought him|וַיָּבִ֥אוּ\rb* \rb a sword|הַחֶ֖רֶב\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*, \v 25 \rb and the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Cut|גִּזְר֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the living|הַחַ֖י\rb* \rb child|הַיֶּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb in two|לִשְׁנָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and give|וּתְנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb half|הַחֲצִי֙\rb* \rb to one|לְאַחַ֔ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and half|הַחֲצִ֖י\rb* \rb to the other|לְאֶחָֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb Then the woman|הָאִשָּׁה֩\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb son|בְּנָ֨הּ\rb* \rb was alive|הַחַ֜י\rb* \rb spoke|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb she yearned|נִכְמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb with compassion|רַחֲמֶיהָ֮\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb her son|בְּנָהּ֒\rb*. “\rb Please|בִּ֣י\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֗י\rb*,” \rb she said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*, “\rb give|תְּנוּ־\rb* \rb her|לָהּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the living|הַחַ֔י\rb* \rb baby|הַיָּל֣וּד\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb kill him|תְּמִיתֻ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |וְהָמֵ֖ת\rb*!”
\p \rb But the other|וְזֹ֣את\rb* \rb woman said|אֹמֶ֗רֶת\rb*, “\rb He will be|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb neither|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb mine|לִ֥י\rb* \rb nor|גַם־\rb* \rb yours|לָ֛ךְ\rb*. \rb Cut him in two|גְּזֹֽרוּ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 27 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb gave his ruling|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*\rb |וַיַּ֨עַן\rb*: “\rb Give|תְּנוּ־\rb* \rb the living|הַחַ֔י\rb* \rb baby|הַיָּל֣וּד\rb* \rb to the first woman|לָהּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*. \rb By no means|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb should you kill him|תְמִיתֻ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |וְהָמֵ֖ת\rb*; \rb she|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb is his mother|אִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb When all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb of the judgment|הַמִּשְׁפָּט֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb had given|שָׁפַ֣ט\rb*, \rb they stood in awe|וַיִּֽרְא֖וּ\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they saw|רָא֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the wisdom|חָכְמַ֧ת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb was in him|בְּקִרְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to administer|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃ס\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 Solomon’s Princes
\p \v 1 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb So King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb ruled|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*, \v 2 \rb and these|וְאֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb were his chief officials|הַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Azariah|עֲזַרְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָד֖וֹק\rb* \rb was the priest|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 3 \rb Elihoreph|אֱלִיחֹ֧רֶף\rb* \rb and Ahijah|וַאֲחִיָּ֛ה\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Shisha|שִׁישָׁ֖א\rb*,\f + \fr 4:3 \fqa Shisha \ft is also called \fqa Seraiah\ft , \fqa Sheva\ft , and \fqa Shavsha\ft ; see 2 Samuel 8:17, 2 Samuel 20:25, and 1 Chronicles 18:16.\f* \rb were secretaries|סֹפְרִ֑ים\rb*;
\li1 \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahilud|אֲחִיל֖וּד\rb* \rb was the recorder|הַמַּזְכִּֽיר׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 4 \rb Benaiah|וּבְנָיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֖ע\rb* \rb was in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the army|הַצָּבָ֑א\rb*;
\li1 \rb Zadok|וְצָד֥וֹק\rb* \rb and Abiathar|וְאֶבְיָתָ֖ר\rb* \rb were priests|כֹּהֲנִֽים׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 5 \rb Azariah|וַעֲזַרְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Nathan|נָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb was in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the governors|הַנִּצָּבִ֑ים\rb*;
\li1 \rb Zabud|וְזָב֧וּד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nathan|נָתָ֛ן\rb* \rb was a priest|כֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb and adviser|רֵעֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 6 \rb Ahishar|וַאֲחִישָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb was in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the palace|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*;
\li1 \rb and Adoniram|וַאֲדֹנִירָ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 4:6 \fqa Adoniram \ft is a variant of \fqa Adoram \ft and \fqa Hadoram\ft ; see 2 Samuel 20:24 and 2 Chronicles 10:18.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abda|עַבְדָּ֖א\rb* \rb was in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the forced labor|הַמַּֽס׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Solomon’s Twelve Officers
\p \v 7 \rb Solomon|וְלִשְׁלֹמֹ֞ה\rb* \rb had twelve|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֤ר\rb* \rb governors|נִצָּבִים֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to provide food|וְכִלְכְּל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his household|בֵּית֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Each one|אֶחָד\rb* \rb would arrange provisions|לְכַלְכֵּֽל׃ס\rb* \rb for one month|חֹ֧דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the year|בַּשָּׁנָ֛ה\rb*,\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \v 8 \rb and these|וְאֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb were their names|שְׁמוֹתָ֔ם\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-hur|ח֖וּר\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 9 \rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-deker|דֶּ֛קֶר\rb* \rb in Makaz|בְּמָקַ֥ץ\rb*, \rb in Shaalbim|וּבְשַֽׁעַלְבִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb in Beth-shemesh|שָׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb*,\rb |וְאֵיל֖וֹן\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb and in Elon-beth-hanan|חָנָֽן׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 10 \rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-hesed|חֶ֖סֶד\rb* \rb in Arubboth|בָּֽאֲרֻבּ֑וֹת\rb* (\rb Socoh|שֹׂכֹ֖ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Hepher|חֵֽפֶר׃ס\rb* \rb belonged to him|ל֥וֹ\rb*);
\li1 \v 11 \rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-abinadab|אֲבִֽינָדָ֖ב\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |נָ֣פַת\rb* \rb in Naphath-dor|דֹּ֑אר\rb*\f + \fr 4:11 \ft Or \fqa in all the heights of Dor\ft ; \fqa Naphath-dor \ft is a variant of \fqa Naphoth-dor\ft ; see Joshua 11:2.\f* \rb (Taphath|טָפַת֙\rb*, \rb a daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb was|הָ֥יְתָה\rb* \rb his|לּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb wife|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃ס\rb*);
\li1 \v 12 \rb Baana|בַּֽעֲנָא֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahilud|אֲחִיל֔וּד\rb* \rb in Taanach|תַּעְנַ֖ךְ\rb*, \rb in Megiddo|וּמְגִדּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and in all|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Beth-shean|שְׁאָ֡ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb next to|אֵ֨צֶל\rb* \rb Zarethan|צָרְתַ֜נָה\rb* \rb below|מִתַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb Jezreel|לְיִזְרְעֶ֗אל\rb*, \rb from|מִבֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb Beth-shean|שְׁאָן֙\rb* \rb to|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אָבֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Abel-meholah|מְחוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb and on past|מֵעֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb Jokmeam|לְיָקְמֳעָֽם׃ס\rb*;
\li1 \v 13 \rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-geber|גֶּ֖בֶר\rb* \rb in Ramoth-gilead|בְּרָמֹ֣ת\rb* (\rb the villages|חַוֺּת֩\rb* \rb of Jair|יָאִ֨יר\rb* \rb son of|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |בַּגִּלְעָ֗ד\rb* \rb in Gilead|גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb* \rb belonged to him|ל֡וֹ\rb*, \rb as well as the region|חֶ֤בֶל\rb* \rb of Argob|אַרְגֹּב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Bashan|בַּבָּשָׁ֔ן\rb* \rb with its sixty|שִׁשִּׁים֙\rb* \rb great|גְּדֹל֔וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb with walls|חוֹמָ֖ה\rb* \rb and bronze|נְחֹֽשֶׁת׃ס\rb* \rb bars|וּבְרִ֥יחַ\rb*);
\li1 \v 14 \rb Ahinadab|אֲחִֽינָדָ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Iddo|עִדֹּ֖א\rb* \rb in Mahanaim|מַחֲנָֽיְמָה׃\rb*;
