\s1 Solomon’s Prosperity
\p \v 20 \rb The people of Judah|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb were as numerous|לָרֹ֑ב\rb* \rb as the sand|כַּח֥וֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the seashore|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*, \rb and they were eating|אֹכְלִ֥ים\rb* \rb and drinking|וְשֹׁתִ֖ים\rb* \rb and rejoicing|וּשְׂמֵחִֽים׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And Solomon|וּשְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb*\rb |הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb reigned|מוֹשֵׁל֙\rb* \rb over all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the kingdoms|הַמַּמְלָכ֔וֹת\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Euphrates|הַנָּהָר֙\rb*\f + \fr 4:21 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\ft ; also in verse 24\f* \rb to the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb as far as|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb These kingdoms offered|מַגִּשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb tribute|מִנְחָ֛ה\rb* \rb and served|וְעֹבְדִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his life|חַיָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb provisions|לֶֽחֶם־\rb* \rb for a single|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb day|לְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb were|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cors|כֹּר֙\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֔לֶת\rb*,\f + \fr 4:22 \fqa 30 cors \ft is approximately 187 bushels or 6,600 liters (probably about 5.5 tons or 5 metric tons of flour).\f* \rb sixty|וְשִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cors|כֹּ֖ר\rb* \rb of meal|קָֽמַח׃\rb*,\f + \fr 4:22 \fqa 60 cors \ft is approximately 375 bushels or 13,200 liters (probably about 11 tons or 10 metric tons of meal).\f* \v 23 \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֨ה\rb* \rb fat|בְּרִאִ֗ים\rb* \rb oxen|בָקָ֜ר\rb*, \rb twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb range|רְעִ֖י\rb* \rb oxen|בָּקָ֛ר\rb*, \rb and a hundred|וּמֵ֣אָה\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֑אן\rb*, \rb as well as|לְ֠בַד\rb* \rb deer|מֵֽאַיָּ֤ל\rb*, \rb gazelles|וּצְבִי֙\rb*, \rb roebucks|וְיַחְמ֔וּר\rb*, \rb and fattened|אֲבוּסִֽים׃\rb* \rb poultry|וּבַרְבֻּרִ֖ים\rb*. \v 24 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb Solomon|ה֞וּא\rb* \rb had dominion|רֹדֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb over everything|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb west|עֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb of the Euphrates|הַנָּהָ֗ר\rb*\f + \fr 4:24 \ft Or \fqa beyond the River\f* — \rb over all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַלְכֵ֖י\rb*\rb |עֵ֣בֶר\rb*\rb |הַנָּהָ֑ר\rb* \rb from Tiphsah|מִתִּפְסַח֙\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb Gaza|עַזָּ֔ה\rb* — \rb and he had|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb peace|וְשָׁל֗וֹם\rb* \rb on all|מִכָּל־\rb*\rb |מִסָּבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb sides|עֲבָרָ֖יו\rb*. \v 25 \rb Throughout|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃ס\rb*, \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֨ה\rb* \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb dwelt|וַיֵּשֶׁב֩\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶ֗טַח\rb* \rb from Dan|מִדָּ֖ן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שָׁ֑בַע\rb*, \rb each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb under|תַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb his own vine|גַּפְנוֹ֙\rb* \rb and|וְתַ֣חַת\rb* \rb his own fig tree|תְּאֵֽנָת֔וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb had|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb 4,000|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb*\f + \fr 4:26 \ft Some LXX manuscripts (see also 2 Chronicles 9:25); Hebrew \fqa 40,000 \ft \f* \rb stalls|אֻרְוֺ֥ת\rb* \rb for his chariot|לְמֶרְכָּב֑וֹ\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִ֖ים\rb* \rb and 12,000|וּשְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb horses|פָּרָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 4:26 \ft Or \fqa horsemen \ft or \fqa charioteers\f* \v 27 \rb Each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb month|חָדְשׁ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֜לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the governors|הַנִּצָּבִ֨ים\rb* \rb in turn provided food|וְכִלְכְּלוּ֩\rb* \rb for King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֧ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who came|הַקָּרֵ֛ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ־\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb table|שֻׁלְחַ֥ן\rb*. \rb They saw to it that|יְעַדְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb nothing was lacking|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb Each one|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb also brought|יָבִ֗אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the required place|הַמָּקוֹם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶה־\rb*\rb |שָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb their quotas|כְּמִשְׁפָּטֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb of barley|וְהַשְּׂעֹרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and straw|וְהַתֶּ֔בֶן\rb* \rb for the chariot horses|וְלָרָ֑כֶשׁ\rb* \rb and other horses|לַסּוּסִ֖ים\rb*.
\s1 Solomon’s Wisdom
\p \v 29 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֨ים\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּן֩\rb* \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֧ה\rb*, \rb exceedingly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb deep|הַרְבֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb insight|וּתְבוּנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and understanding|לֵ֔ב\rb* \rb beyond measure|וְרֹ֣חַב\rb*, \rb like the sand|כַּח֕וֹל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the seashore|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַיָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb was greater than|וַתֵּ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb that|מֵֽחָכְמַ֖ת\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of the East|קֶ֑דֶם\rb*, \rb greater than all|וּמִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the wisdom|חָכְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb He was wiser|וַיֶּחְכַּם֮\rb* \rb than all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb men|הָֽאָדָם֒\rb*— \rb wiser than Ethan|מֵאֵיתָ֣ן\rb* \rb the Ezrahite|הָאֶזְרָחִ֗י\rb*, \rb and wiser than Heman|וְהֵימָ֧ן\rb*, \rb Calcol|וְכַלְכֹּ֛ל\rb*, \rb and Darda|וְדַרְדַּ֖ע\rb*, \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Mahol|מָח֑וֹל\rb*. \rb And his fame|שְׁמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb spread|וַיְהִֽי־\rb* \rb throughout|בְכָֽל־\rb* \rb the surrounding|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb Solomon composed|וַיְדַבֵּ֕ר\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb proverbs|מָשָׁ֑ל\rb*, \rb and his songs|שִׁיר֖וֹ\rb* \rb numbered|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb a thousand|וָאָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb and five|חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*. \v 33 \rb He spoke|וַיְדַבֵּר֮\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb trees|הָֽעֵצִים֒\rb*, \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the cedar|הָאֶ֙רֶז֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Lebanon|בַּלְּבָנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד֙\rb* \rb the hyssop|הָאֵז֔וֹב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb growing|יֹצֵ֖א\rb* \rb in the wall|בַּקִּ֑יר\rb*, \rb and he taught|וַיְדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb animals|הַבְּהֵמָ֣ה\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb birds|הָע֔וֹף\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb reptiles|הָרֶ֖מֶשׂ\rb*,\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and fish|הַדָּגִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb So men of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb nations|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to listen|שָׁמְע֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*\rb |מֵאֵת֙\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*, \rb sent by all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had heard|לִשְׁמֹ֕עַ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb of his wisdom|חָכְמַ֣ת\rb*.
\c 5
\s1 Preparations for the Temple
\r (2 Chronicles 2:1–10)
\p \v 1 \rb Now when Hiram|חִירָ֨ם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Tyre|צ֤וֹר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb Solomon had been anointed|מָשְׁח֥וּ\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in his father’s|אָבִ֑יהוּ\rb* \rb place|תַּ֣חַת\rb*, \rb he sent|וַ֠יִּשְׁלַח\rb* \rb envoys|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*;\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Hiram|חִירָ֛ם\rb* \rb had always|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃ס\rb* \rb been|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb a friend|אֹהֵ֗ב\rb* \rb of David|לְדָוִ֖ד\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb And Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb relayed|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb this message|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hiram|חִירָ֖ם\rb*:
\pmo \v 3 “\rb As you|אַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb are well aware|יָדַ֜עְתָּ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb due to|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the wars waged|הַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on all sides|סְבָבֻ֑הוּ\rb* \rb against my father|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb he could|יָכֹל֙\rb* \rb not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb build|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁם֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֔יו\rb* \rb until|עַ֤ד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb had put|תֵּת־\rb* \rb his enemies under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb his feet|כַּפּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |רַגְלוֹ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהַ֛י\rb*\rb |לִ֖י\rb* \rb has given me rest|הֵנִ֨יחַ\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִ֑יב\rb*, \rb and there is no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb adversary|שָׂטָ֔ן\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ין\rb* \rb or crisis|פֶּ֥גַע\rb*\rb |רָֽע׃\rb*.
\b 
\pmo \v 5 \rb So behold|וְהִנְנִ֣י\rb*, \rb I plan|אֹמֵ֔ר\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb*, \rb according to what|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִי֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb*: ‘\rb I will put|אֶתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb your son|בִּנְךָ֗\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your throne|כִּסְאֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb in your place|תַּחְתֶּ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb and he|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb will build|יִבְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִֽי׃\rb*.’
\b 
\pmo \v 6 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֡ה\rb*, \rb order|צַוֵּה֩\rb* \rb that cedars|אֲרָזִ֜ים\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֗וֹן\rb* \rb be cut down|וְיִכְרְתוּ־\rb* \rb for me|לִ֨י\rb*. \rb My servants|וַֽעֲבָדַי֙\rb* \rb will be|יִהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb and I will pay|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֔\rb* \rb servants|עֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb whatever wages|וּשְׂכַ֤ר\rb*\rb |כְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you set|תֹּאמֵ֑ר\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֗עְתָּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there are none|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb among us|בָּ֛נוּ\rb* \rb as skilled|יֹדֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb in logging|לִכְרָת־\rb*\rb |עֵצִ֖ים\rb* \rb as the Sidonians|כַּצִּדֹנִֽים׃\rb*.”
\s1 Hiram’s Reply to Solomon
\r (2 Chronicles 2:11–18)
\p \v 7 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb When Hiram|חִירָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb received|כִּשְׁמֹ֧עַ\rb* \rb Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb message|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*, \rb he rejoiced|וַיִּשְׂמַ֣ח\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Blessed be|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*! \rb He|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִד֙\rb* \rb a wise|חָכָ֔ם\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb great|הָרָ֖ב\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֥ם\rb*!” \v 8 \rb Then Hiram|חִירָם֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb a reply to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*:
\pmo “\rb I have received|שָׁמַ֕עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb your message|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |שָׁלַ֖חְתָּ\rb*;\rb |אֵלָ֑י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb will do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb you desire|חֶפְצְךָ֔\rb* \rb regarding the cedar|אֲרָזִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּבַעֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb and cypress|בְרוֹשִֽׁים׃\rb*\f + \fr 5:8 \ft Or \fqa pine \ft or \fqa juniper \ft or \fqa fir\ft ; also in verse 10\f* \rb timber|בַּעֲצֵ֥י\rb*. \v 9 \rb My servants|עֲ֠בָדַי\rb* \rb will haul the logs|יֹרִ֨דוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֜וֹן\rb* \rb to the Sea|יָ֗מָּה\rb*,\f + \fr 5:9 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea\f* \rb and I|וַ֠אֲנִי\rb* \rb will float them|אֲשִׂימֵ֨ם\rb* \rb as rafts|דֹּבְר֤וֹת\rb* \rb by sea|בַּיָּם֙\rb* \rb to|עַֽד־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֞וֹם\rb* \rb you specify|תִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֛י\rb*. \rb There|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb I will separate the logs|וְנִפַּצְתִּ֥ים\rb*, \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb can take them away|תִשָּׂ֑א\rb*. \rb And in exchange, you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb can meet|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my needs|חֶפְצִ֔י\rb* \rb by providing|לָתֵ֖ת\rb* \rb my household|בֵּיתִֽי׃\rb* \rb with food|לֶ֥חֶם\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb So|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb Hiram|חִיר֜וֹם\rb* \rb provided|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb* \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the cedar|אֲרָזִ֛ים\rb*\rb |וַעֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb and cypress|בְרוֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb timber|עֲצֵ֧י\rb* \rb he wanted|חֶפְצֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb |שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb*\rb |יִתֵּ֧ן\rb*\rb |כֹּֽה־\rb*\rb |לְחִירָ֖ם\rb* \rb and year|שָׁנָ֥ה\rb* \rb after year|בְשָׁנָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb Solomon|וּשְׁלֹמֹה֩\rb* \rb would provide|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb Hiram|לְחִירָ֜ם\rb* \rb with 20,000|עֶשְׂרִים֩\rb*\rb |אֶ֨לֶף\rb* \rb cors|כֹּ֤ר\rb* \rb of wheat|חִטִּים֙\rb*\f + \fr 5:11 \fqa 20,000 cors \ft is approximately 124,800 bushels or 4.4 million liters (probably about 3,800 tons or 3,400 metric tons of wheat).\f* \rb as food|מַכֹּ֣לֶת\rb* \rb for his household|לְבֵית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb as well as 20,000|וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb baths|כֹּ֖ר\rb* \rb of pure olive oil|שֶׁ֣מֶן\rb*\rb |כָּתִ֑ית\rb*.\f + \fr 5:11 \ft LXX (see also 2 Chronicles 2:10); \fqa 20,000 baths \ft is approximately 116,000 gallons or 440,000 liters of olive oil; Hebrew \fqa twenty cors of pure oil \ft or \fqa twenty cors of pressed oil\f*
\p \v 12 \rb And the LORD|וַיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָה֙\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb He had promised|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb him|ל֑וֹ\rb*. \rb There was|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb peace|שָׁלֹ֗ם\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֤ין\rb* \rb Hiram|חִירָם֙\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb and the two|שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb of them made|וַיִּכְרְת֥וּ\rb* \rb a treaty|בְרִ֖ית\rb*.\f + \fr 5:12 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft .\f*
\s1 Solomon’s Labor Force
\p \v 13 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb conscripted|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb a labor force|מַ֖ס\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמַּ֔ס\rb* \rb of 30,000|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \v 14 \rb He sent them|וַיִּשְׁלָחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb to Lebanon|לְבָנ֗וֹנָה\rb* \rb in monthly|בַּחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb shifts|חֲלִיפ֔וֹת\rb* \rb of 10,000 men|עֲשֶׂ֨רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֤ים\rb*, \rb so that they would spend|יִהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb one month|חֹ֚דֶשׁ\rb* \rb in Lebanon|בַלְּבָנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and two|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb at home|בְּבֵית֑וֹ\rb*. \rb And Adoniram was|וַאֲדֹנִירָ֖ם\rb* \rb in charge|עַל־\rb* \rb of the forced labor|הַמַּֽס׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb had|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb 70,000|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb porters|נֹשֵׂ֣א\rb*\rb |סַבָּ֑ל\rb* \rb and 80,000|וּשְׁמֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb stonecutters|חֹצֵ֥ב\rb* \rb in the mountains|בָּהָֽר׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb not including|לְ֠בַד\rb* \rb his|לִשְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb 3,300|שְׁלֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֑וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 5:16 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa 3,600\ft ; see 2 Chronicles 2:18.\f* \rb foremen|מִשָּׂרֵ֨י\rb*\rb |הַנִּצָּבִ֤ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb who supervised|הָרֹדִ֣ים\rb* \rb the workers|בָּעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |הָעֹשִׂ֖ים\rb*\rb |בַּמְּלָאכָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb* \rb commanded them|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb to quarry|וַיַּסִּעוּ֩\rb* \rb large|גְּדֹל֜וֹת\rb*, \rb costly|יְקָר֛וֹת\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֨ים\rb* \rb to lay the foundation|לְיַסֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |אַבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb with dressed|גָזִֽית׃\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֧ים\rb*. \v 18 \rb So Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb*\rb |בֹּנֵ֧י\rb* \rb and Hiram’s|חִיר֖וֹם\rb* \rb builders|וּבֹנֵ֥י\rb*, \rb along with the Gebalites|וְהַגִּבְלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb quarried the stone|וַֽיִּפְסְל֞וּ\rb* \rb and prepared|וַיָּכִ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb the timber|הָעֵצִ֥ים\rb* \rb and stone|וְהָאֲבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb for the construction|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃פ\rb*.
\c 6
\s1 Temple Construction Begins
\r (2 Chronicles 3:1–2)
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb In the four|וְאַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb and eightieth|בִשְׁמוֹנִ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 6:1 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa four hundred and fortieth\f* \rb year|שָׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb after the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb had come|לְצֵ֣את\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַיִם֩\rb*, \rb in the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֜ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Solomon’s reign|לִמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*,\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb in the month|הַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of Ziv|זִ֗ו\rb*,\f + \fr 6:1 \fqa Ziv \ft was the second month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of April and May; also in verse 37.\f* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb month|בְּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb he|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb began to build|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb The house|וְהַבַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb built|בָּנָ֜ה\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb was sixty|שִׁשִּֽׁים־\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb twenty cubits|וְעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb wide|רָחְבּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and thirty|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb high|קוֹמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 6:2 \ft The house was approximately 90 feet long, 30 feet wide, and 45 feet high (27.4 meters long, 9.1 meters wide, and 13.7 meters high).\f* \v 3 \rb The portico|וְהָאוּלָ֗ם\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the front|פְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the main hall|הֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb was twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb*\f + \fr 6:3 \fqa 20 cubits \ft is approximately 30 feet or 9.1 meters; also in verses 16 and 20.\f* \rb long|אָרְכּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb extending across|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the width|רֹ֣חַב\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb and projecting out|רָחְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֧שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|בָּאַמָּ֛ה\rb*\f + \fr 6:3 \fqa 10 cubits \ft is approximately 15 feet or 4.6 meters; also in verses 23–26.\f* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb front|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb He also had|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb narrow|אֲטֻמִֽים׃\rb* \rb windows|חַלּוֹנֵ֖י\rb* \rb framed high|שְׁקֻפִ֥ים\rb* \rb in the temple|לַבָּ֔יִת\rb*.
\s1 The Chambers
\p \v 5 \rb Against|עַל־\rb* \rb the walls|קִ֨יר\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֤יִת\rb*\rb |לַֽהֵיכָ֖ל\rb* \rb and the inner sanctuary|וְלַדְּבִ֑יר\rb*, \rb Solomon built|וַיִּבֶן֩\rb* \rb a chambered structure|יָצוֹעַ\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֔יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |קִיר֤וֹת\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb*, \rb in which|סָבִ֔יב\rb* \rb he constructed|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb the side rooms|צְלָע֖וֹת\rb*\rb |סָבִֽיב׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb The bottom|הַתַּחְתֹּנָ֜ה\rb* \rb floor was|הַיָּצוֹעַ\rb* \rb five|חָמֵ֧שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|בָּאַמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb wide|רָחְבָּ֗הּ\rb*,\f + \fr 6:6 \fqa 5 cubits \ft is approximately 7.5 feet or 2.3 meters; also in verses 10 and 24.\f* \rb the middle floor|וְהַתִּֽיכֹנָה֙\rb* \rb six|שֵׁ֤שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּה֙\rb*\rb |רָחְבָּ֔הּ\rb*,\f + \fr 6:6 \fqa 6 cubits \ft is approximately 9 feet or 2.7 meters.\f* \rb and the third floor|וְהַ֨שְּׁלִישִׁ֔ית\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb cubits|בָּאַמָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |רָחְבָּ֑הּ\rb*.\f + \fr 6:6 \fqa 7 cubits \ft is approximately 10.5 feet or 3.2 meters.\f*\rb |כִּ֡י\rb* \rb He also placed|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb offset ledges|מִגְרָעוֹת֩\rb* \rb around|סָבִיב֙\rb* \rb the outside|ח֔וּצָה\rb* \rb of the temple|לַבַּ֤יִת\rb*, \rb so that nothing|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb would be inserted|אֲחֹ֥ז\rb* \rb into its|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \rb walls|בְּקִֽירוֹת־\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb The temple|וְהַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb was constructed|בְּהִבָּ֣נֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb using|נִבְנָ֑ה\rb* \rb finished|שְׁלֵמָ֥ה\rb* \rb stones|אֶֽבֶן־\rb* \rb cut at the quarry|מַסָּ֖ע\rb*, \rb so that no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb hammer|וּמַקָּב֤וֹת\rb* \rb or chisel|וְהַגַּרְזֶן֙\rb* \rb or any other|כָּל־\rb* \rb iron|בַרְזֶ֔ל\rb* \rb tool|כְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb was heard|נִשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb in the temple|בַּבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb while it was being built|בְּהִבָּנֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb The entrance|פֶּ֗תַח\rb* \rb to the bottom|הַתִּ֣יכֹנָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 6:8 \ft LXX and Targum; Hebrew \fqa middle\f* \rb floor|הַצֵּלָע֙\rb* \rb was on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the south|הַיְמָנִ֑ית\rb* \rb side|כֶּ֥תֶף\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*. \rb A stairway|וּבְלוּלִּ֗ים\rb* \rb led up|יַֽעֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the middle level|הַתִּ֣יכֹנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb there|הַתִּֽיכֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the third floor|הַשְּׁלִשִֽׁים׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb So Solomon built|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb and finished it|וַיְכַלֵּ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb roofing|וַיִּסְפֹּ֤ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb it|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb with beams|גֵּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb and planks|וּשְׂדֵרֹ֖ת\rb* \rb of cedar|בָּאֲרָזִֽים׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb He built|וַיִּ֤בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb chambers|הַיָּצוֹעַ\rb* \rb all along|עַל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb*, \rb each five|חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb high|קֽוֹמָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb and attached|וַיֶּאֱחֹ֥ז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb with beams|בַּעֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb of cedar|אֲרָזִֽים׃פ\rb*.
\s1 God’s Promise to Solomon
\p \v 11 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 12 “\rb As for this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb temple|הַבַּ֨יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are building|בֹנֶ֗ה\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you walk|תֵּלֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb in My statutes|בְּחֻקֹּתַי֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb carry out|תַּֽעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֣י\rb*, \rb and keep|וְשָׁמַרְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֖י\rb* \rb by walking|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb in them|בָּהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb I will fulfill|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb through you|אִתָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb the promise|דְּבָרִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I made|דִּבַּ֖רְתִּי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb*. \v 13 \rb And I will dwell|וְשָׁ֣כַנְתִּ֔י\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb abandon|אֶעֱזֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 The Temple’s Interior
\r (2 Chronicles 3:5–9)
\p \v 14 \rb So Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb built|וַיִּ֧בֶן\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb and finished|וַיְכַלֵּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb it|אֶת־\rb*. \v 15 \rb He lined|וַיִּבֶן֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the interior|הַבַּ֤יִת\rb*\rb |מִבַּ֙יְתָה֙\rb* \rb walls|קִיר֨וֹת\rb* \rb with cedar|אֲרָזִ֔ים\rb* \rb paneling|בְּצַלְע֣וֹת\rb* \rb from the floor|מִקַּרְקַ֤ע\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the ceiling|הַסִּפֻּ֔ן\rb*,\rb |צִפָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מִבָּ֑יִת\rb*\rb |עֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb and he covered|וַיְצַ֛ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the floor|קַרְקַ֥ע\rb*\rb |הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb with cypress|בְּרוֹשִֽׁים׃\rb*\f + \fr 6:15 \ft Or \fqa pine \ft or \fqa juniper \ft or \fqa fir\ft ; also in verse 34\f* \rb boards|בְּצַלְע֥וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb He partitioned off|וַיִּבֶן֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֜ה\rb* \rb at|מִן־\rb* \rb the rear|מִיַּרְכּוֹתֵי\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb with cedar|אֲרָזִ֔ים\rb* \rb boards|בְּצַלְע֣וֹת\rb* \rb from floor|הַקַּרְקַ֖ע\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb ceiling|הַקִּיר֑וֹת\rb* \rb to form|וַיִּ֤בֶן\rb* \rb within the temple|מִבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb an inner sanctuary|לִדְבִ֔יר\rb*, \rb the Most Holy Place|לְקֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 6:16 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies\f* \v 17 \rb |הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb And the main hall|הַהֵיכָ֥ל\rb* \rb in front of this room|לִפְנָֽי׃\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits long|בָּאַמָּ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 6:17 \fqa 40 cubits \ft is approximately 60 feet or 18.3 meters.\f*
\p \v 18 \rb The cedar|וְאֶ֤רֶז\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb paneling inside|פְּנִ֔ימָה\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb was carved|מִקְלַ֣עַת\rb* \rb with gourds|פְּקָעִ֔ים\rb* \rb and open|וּפְטוּרֵ֖י\rb* \rb flowers|צִצִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb Everything|הַכֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb was cedar|אֶ֔רֶז\rb*; \rb not|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb a stone|אֶ֖בֶן\rb* \rb could be seen|נִרְאָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Solomon also prepared|הֵכִ֑ין\rb* \rb the inner sanctuary|וּדְבִ֧יר\rb* \rb within|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֛יִת\rb*\rb |מִפְּנִ֖ימָה\rb* \rb to set|לְתִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֖וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 20 \rb The inner|וְלִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb sanctuary|הַדְּבִ֡יר\rb* \rb was twenty|עֶשְׂרִים֩\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֨ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֜רֶךְ\rb*, \rb twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֧ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֗חַב\rb*, \rb and twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb high|קֽוֹמָת֔וֹ\rb*. \rb He overlaid the inside|וַיְצַפֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with pure|סָג֑וּר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*, \rb and he also overlaid|וַיְצַ֥ף\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb of cedar|אָֽרֶז׃\rb*.\f + \fr 6:20 \ft Or \fqa with cedar\f*
\p \v 21 \rb So Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֧ה\rb* \rb overlaid|וַיְצַ֨ף\rb* \rb the inside|מִפְּנִ֖ימָה\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֛יִת\rb* \rb with pure|סָג֑וּר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*, \rb and he extended|וַיְעַבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָב֙\rb* \rb chains|בְּרַתִּיקוֹת\rb*\f + \fr 6:21 \ft Or \fqa made gold chains to draw (the curtains)\f* \rb across the front|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the inner sanctuary|הַדְּבִ֔יר\rb*, \rb which was overlaid|וַיְצַפֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb So he overlaid|צִפָּ֥ה\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb the whole interior|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֛יִת\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb was completely finished|תֹּ֣ם\rb*. \rb He also overlaid|צִפָּ֥ה\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb* \rb the entire|וְכָל־\rb* \rb altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֥חַ\rb* \rb that belonged to|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the inner sanctuary|לַדְּבִ֖יר\rb*.
\s1 The Cherubim
\r (2 Chronicles 3:10–13)
\p \v 23 \rb In the inner sanctuary|בַּדְּבִ֔יר\rb* \rb he made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb cherubim|כְרוּבִ֖ים\rb*, \rb each ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb high|קוֹמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*, \rb out of olive|שָׁ֑מֶן\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵי־\rb*. \v 24 \rb One wing|כְּנַ֤ף\rb* \rb of the first|הָֽאֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb cherub|הַכְּרוּב֙\rb* \rb was five|וְחָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits long|אַמּ֗וֹת\rb*, \rb and the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֑ית\rb* \rb wing|כְּנַ֥ף\rb*\rb |הַכְּר֖וּב\rb* \rb was five|וְחָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits long as well|אַמּ֔וֹת\rb*. \rb So the full|מִקְצ֥וֹת\rb* \rb wingspan|כְּנָפָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb*\rb |קְצ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |כְּנָפָֽיו׃\rb* \rb was ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֔וֹת\rb*. \v 25 \rb The second|הַשֵּׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb cherub|הַכְּר֖וּב\rb* \rb also measured ten|וְעֶ֙שֶׂר֙\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb*; \rb both|לִשְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִֽים׃\rb* \rb had the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb size|מִדָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb and shape|וְקֶ֥צֶב\rb*, \v 26 \rb and the height|קוֹמַת֙\rb* \rb of each|הָֽאֶחָ֔ד\rb*\rb |הַכְּר֣וּב\rb*\rb |וְכֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |הַשֵּׁנִֽי׃\rb* \rb cherub|הַכְּר֥וּב\rb* \rb was ten|עֶ֖שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֑ה\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb And he placed|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֜ים\rb* \rb inside|בְּת֣וֹךְ׀\rb* \rb the innermost room|הַפְּנִימִ֗י\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֣יִת\rb*. \rb Since their|הַכְּרֻבִים֒\rb* \rb wings|כַּנְפֵ֣י\rb* \rb were spread out|וַֽיִּפְרְשׂוּ֮\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wing|כְּנַף־\rb* \rb of the first cherub|הָֽאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb touched|וַתִּגַּ֤ע\rb* \rb one wall|בַּקִּ֔יר\rb*, \rb while the wing|וּכְנַף֙\rb* \rb of the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb cherub|הַכְּר֣וּב\rb* \rb touched|נֹגַ֖עַת\rb* \rb the other|הַשֵּׁנִ֑י\rb* \rb wall|בַּקִּ֣יר\rb*, \rb and in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the middle|תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the room|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb their wingtips|וְכַנְפֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |כָּנָ֥ף\rb* \rb touched|נֹגְעֹ֖ת\rb*. \v 28 \rb He also overlaid|וַיְצַ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָֽב׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb |וְאֵת֩\rb* \rb Then he carved|קָלַ֗ע\rb* \rb the walls|קִיר֨וֹת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb around|מֵסַ֣ב׀\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֜יִת\rb*, \rb in both the inner|מִלִּפְנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and outer sanctuaries|וְלַחִיצֽוֹן׃\rb*, \rb with carved|מִקְלְעוֹת֙\rb* \rb engravings|פִּתּוּחֵי֙\rb* \rb of cherubim|כְּרוּבִ֣ים\rb*, \rb palm trees|וְתִֽמֹרֹ֔ת\rb*, \rb and open|וּפְטוּרֵ֖י\rb* \rb flowers|צִצִּ֑ים\rb*. \v 30 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb he overlaid|צִפָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb floor|קַרְקַ֥ע\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb in both the inner|לִפְנִ֖ימָה\rb* \rb and outer sanctuaries|וְלַחִיצֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\s1 The Doors
\p \v 31 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb For the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the inner sanctuary|הַדְּבִ֔יר\rb*, \rb Solomon constructed|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb doors|דַּלְת֣וֹת\rb* \rb of olive|שָׁ֑מֶן\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵי־\rb* \rb with five-sided|חֲמִשִֽׁית׃\rb*\rb |הָאַ֥יִל\rb* \rb doorposts|מְזוּז֖וֹת\rb*. \v 32 \rb The double|וּשְׁתֵּי֮\rb* \rb doors|דַּלְת֣וֹת\rb* \rb were made of olive|שֶׁמֶן֒\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵי־\rb*, \rb and he carved|וְקָלַ֣ע\rb*\rb |מִקְלְע֨וֹת\rb* \rb into them|עֲ֠לֵיהֶם\rb* \rb cherubim|כְּרוּבִ֧ים\rb*, \rb palm trees|וְתִמֹר֛וֹת\rb*, \rb and open|וּפְטוּרֵ֥י\rb* \rb flowers|צִצִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and overlaid|וְצִפָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and palm trees|הַתִּֽמֹר֖וֹת\rb* \rb with hammered gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb*\rb |וַיָּ֛רֶד\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb In the same way|וְכֵ֥ן\rb* \rb he made|עָשָׂ֛ה\rb* \rb four-sided|רְבִעִֽית׃\rb* \rb doorposts|מְזוּז֣וֹת\rb* \rb of olive|שָׁ֑מֶן\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵי־\rb* \rb for the sanctuary|הַֽהֵיכָ֖ל\rb* \rb entrance|לְפֶ֥תַח\rb*. \v 34 \rb The two|וּשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb doors|דַלְת֖וֹת\rb* \rb were made of cypress|בְרוֹשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and each had|הָֽאַחַת֙\rb*\rb |הַדֶּ֤לֶת\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb folding|גְּלִילִ֔ים\rb* \rb panels|צְלָעִ֜ים\rb*\rb |הַשֵּׁנִ֖ית\rb*\rb |הַדֶּ֥לֶת\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |גְּלִילִֽים׃\rb*\rb |קְלָעִ֛ים\rb*. \v 35 \rb He carved into them|וְקָלַ֤ע\rb* \rb cherubim|כְּרוּבִים֙\rb*, \rb palm trees|וְתִ֣מֹר֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and open|וּפְטֻרֵ֖י\rb* \rb flowers|צִצִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb and he overlaid them|וְצִפָּ֣ה\rb* \rb with gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb hammered evenly|מְיֻשָּׁ֖ר\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the carvings|הַמְּחֻקֶּֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Courtyard
\p \v 36 \rb Solomon built|וַיִּ֙בֶן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֔ית\rb* \rb courtyard|הֶחָצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb rows|טוּרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of dressed stone|גָזִ֑ית\rb* \rb and one row|וְט֖וּר\rb* \rb of trimmed cedar|אֲרָזִֽים׃\rb* \rb beams|כְּרֻתֹ֥ת\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb The foundation of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb was laid|יֻסַּ֖ד\rb* \rb in the fourth|הָֽרְבִיעִ֔ית\rb* \rb year of Solomon’s reign|בַּשָּׁנָה֙\rb*, \rb in the month|בְּיֶ֖רַח\rb* \rb of Ziv|זִֽו׃\rb*. \v 38 \rb In the eleventh|הָאַחַ֨ת\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֜ה\rb* \rb year|וּבַשָּׁנָה֩\rb*, \rb in the month|בְּיֶ֣רַח\rb* \rb of Bul|בּ֗וּל\rb*,\f + \fr 6:38 \fqa Bul \ft was the eighth month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of October and November.\f*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֔י\rb* \rb month|הַחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the temple|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb was finished|כָּלָ֣ה\rb* \rb in every|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb detail|דְּבָרָ֖יו\rb* \rb and according to every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb specification|מִשְׁפָּטוֹ\rb*. \rb So he built the temple|וַיִּבְנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb*.
\c 7
\s1 Solomon’s Palace Complex
\p \v 1 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb however|וְאֶת־\rb*, \rb took thirteen|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb to complete|וַיְכַ֖ל\rb* \rb the construction|בָּנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of his entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb palace|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb He built|וַיִּ֜בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the House|בֵּ֣ית׀\rb* \rb of the Forest|יַ֣עַר\rb* \rb of Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֗וֹן\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֨ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֤ה\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּוֹ֙\rb*, \rb fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb wide|רָחְבּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and thirty|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb high|קוֹמָת֑וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 7:2 \ft The house was approximately 150 feet long, 75 feet wide, and 45 feet high (45.7 meters long, 22.9 meters wide, and 13.7 meters high).\f* \rb with|עַ֗ל\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָה֙\rb* \rb rows|טוּרֵי֙\rb* \rb of cedar|אֲרָזִ֔ים\rb* \rb pillars|עַמּוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb supporting|עַל־\rb*\rb |הָעַמּוּדִֽים׃\rb* \rb the cedar|אֲרָזִ֖ים\rb* \rb beams|וּכְרֻת֥וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb The house was roofed|וְסָפֻ֣ן\rb* \rb with cedar|בָּאֶ֗רֶז\rb* \rb above|מִמַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb the beams|הַצְּלָעֹת֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb rested on|עַל־\rb* \rb the pillars|הָֽעַמּוּדִ֔ים\rb* — \rb forty-five beams|אַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֑ה\rb*, \rb fifteen|חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb per row|הַטּֽוּר׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb There were three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb rows|טוּרִ֑ים\rb* \rb of high windows|וּשְׁקֻפִ֖ים\rb* \rb facing one another|וּמֶחֱזָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |מֶחֱזָ֖ה\rb* \rb in three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb tiers|פְּעָמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the doorways|הַפְּתָחִ֥ים\rb*\f + \fr 7:5 \ft Literally \fqa doorways and doorposts\f* \rb had rectangular|רְבֻעִ֣ים\rb* \rb frames|שָׁ֑קֶף\rb*, \rb with|וּמ֧וּל\rb* \rb the openings|מֶחֱזָ֛ה\rb* \rb facing one another|אֶל־\rb*\rb |מֶחֱזָ֖ה\rb* \rb in three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb tiers|פְּעָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Solomon made|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb his colonnade|אוּלָ֤ם\rb*\rb |הָֽעַמּוּדִים֙\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and thirty|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb wide|רָחְבּ֑וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 7:6 \ft The colonnade was approximately 75 feet long and 45 feet wide (22.9 meters long and 13.7 meters wide).\f* \rb with a portico|וְאוּלָם֙\rb* \rb in front of it|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and a canopy|וְעָ֖ב\rb* \rb with pillars|וְעַמֻּדִ֥ים\rb* \rb in front of|עַל־\rb* \rb the portico|פְּנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb In addition, he built|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb* \rb a hall|וְאוּלָ֤ם\rb* \rb for the throne|הַכִּסֵּא֙\rb*, \rb the Hall|אֻלָ֥ם\rb* \rb of Justice|הַמִּשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he was to judge|יִשְׁפָּט־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb*. \rb It was paneled|וְסָפ֣וּן\rb* \rb with cedar|בָּאֶ֔רֶז\rb* \rb from floor|מֵהַקַּרְקַ֖ע\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb ceiling|הַקַּרְקָֽע׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:7 \ft Syriac and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa from floor to floor\f*
\p \v 8 \rb And the palace|וּבֵיתוֹ֩\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Solomon would live|יֵ֨שֶׁב\rb*,\rb |שָׁ֜ם\rb* \rb set further back|הָאַחֶ֗רֶת\rb*\rb |חָצֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |לָֽאוּלָ֔ם\rb*, \rb was|הָיָ֑ה\rb* \rb of similar|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb construction|כַּמַּֽעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*. \rb He also made|יַעֲשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb a palace|וּבַ֜יִת\rb* \rb like this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb hall|כָּאוּלָ֖ם\rb* \rb for Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb daughter|לְבַת־\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb had married|לָקַ֣ח\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb these buildings|אֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb were constructed with costly|יְקָרֹת֙\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֤ים\rb*, \rb cut|גָּזִ֔ית\rb* \rb to size|כְּמִדֹּ֣ת\rb* \rb and trimmed|מְגֹרָר֥וֹת\rb* \rb with saws|בַּמְּגֵרָ֖ה\rb* \rb inside|מִבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb and out|וּמִח֑וּץ\rb* \rb from the foundation|וּמִמַּסָּד֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the eaves|הַטְּפָח֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and from the outside|וּמִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the great|הַגְּדוֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb courtyard|הֶחָצֵ֥ר\rb*. \v 10 \rb The foundations|וּמְיֻסָּ֕ד\rb* \rb were laid with large|גְּדֹל֑וֹת\rb*,\rb |אַבְנֵי֙\rb* \rb costly|יְקָר֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲבָנִ֣ים\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֥ים\rb*, \rb some ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits long|אַמּ֔וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 7:10 \fqa 10 cubits \ft is approximately 15 feet or 4.6 meters.\f* \rb and some|וְאַבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb eight|שְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb cubits long|אַמּֽוֹת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:10 \fqa 8 cubits \ft is approximately 12 feet or 3.7 meters.\f* \v 11 \rb Above these|וּמִלְמַ֗עְלָה\rb* \rb were costly|יְקָר֛וֹת\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֧ים\rb*, \rb cut|גָּזִ֖ית\rb* \rb to size|כְּמִדּ֥וֹת\rb*, \rb and cedar beams|וָאָֽרֶז׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb The great|הַגְּדוֹלָ֜ה\rb* \rb courtyard|וְחָצֵ֨ר\rb* \rb was surrounded by|סָבִ֗יב\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb* \rb rows|טוּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb of dressed stone|גָּזִ֔ית\rb* \rb and a row|וְט֖וּר\rb* \rb of trimmed cedar|אֲרָזִ֑ים\rb* \rb beams|כְּרֻתֹ֣ת\rb*, \rb as were the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֖ית\rb* \rb courtyard|וְלַחֲצַ֧ר\rb* \rb and portico|וּלְאֻלָ֥ם\rb* \rb of the house of|בֵּית־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |הַבָּֽיִת׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Pillars and Capitals
\r (2 Chronicles 3:14–17)
\p \v 13 \rb Now King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb to bring|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb Huram|חִירָ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 7:13 \ft Hebrew \fqa Hiram\ft , a variant of \fqa Huram\ft ; also in verses 40 and 45; see 2 Chronicles 4:11. Note that this is not Hiram king of Tyre mentioned in 1 Kings 5:1.\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from Tyre|מִצֹּֽר׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb He was|ה֜וּא\rb* \rb the son of|בֶּן־\rb* \rb a widow|אַלְמָנָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁה֩\rb* \rb from the tribe|מִמַּטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֗י\rb*, \rb and his father|וְאָבִ֣יו\rb* \rb was a man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹרִי֮\rb*, \rb a craftsman|חֹרֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb in bronze|נְחֹשֶׁת֒\rb*. \rb Huram had great|וַ֠יִּמָּלֵא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb skill|הַחָכְמָ֤ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb understanding|הַתְּבוּנָה֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and knowledge|הַדַּ֔עַת\rb*\rb |לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb for every kind|כָּל־\rb* \rb of bronze|בַּנְּחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb work|מְלָאכָ֖ה\rb*. \rb So he came|וַיָּבוֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb and carried out|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his work|מְלַאכְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb He cast|וַיָּ֛צַר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb pillars|הָעַמּוּדִ֖ים\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb*\rb |הָעַמּ֣וּד\rb*, \rb each|הָאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb eighteen|שְׁמֹנֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֜ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb high|קוֹמַת֙\rb* \rb and twelve|שְׁתֵּים־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb in circumference|וְחוּט֙\rb*\rb |יָסֹ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָעַמּ֥וּד\rb*\rb |הַשֵּׁנִֽי׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:15 \ft Each pillar was approximately 27 feet high and 18 feet in circumference (8.2 meters high and 5.5 meters in circumference).\f* \v 16 \rb He also made|עָשָׂ֗ה\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁתֵּ֨י\rb* \rb capitals|כֹתָרֹ֜ת\rb* \rb of cast|מֻצַ֣ק\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb to set|לָתֵ֛ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb top|רָאשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the pillars|הָֽעַמּוּדִ֖ים\rb*, \rb each|הָאֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb capital|הַכֹּתֶ֣רֶת\rb*\rb |קוֹמַ֖ת\rb*\rb |הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb*\rb |הַכֹּתֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb five|חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb high|קוֹמַת֙\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אַמּ֔וֹת\rb*.\f + \fr 7:16 \fqa 5 cubits \ft is approximately 7.5 feet or 2.3 meters.\f* \v 17 \rb For the capitals|לַכֹּ֣תָרֹ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb top|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the pillars|הָעַמּוּדִ֑ים\rb* \rb he made|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb a network|שְׂבָכִ֞ים\rb* \rb of lattice|שְׂבָכָ֗ה\rb*, \rb with wreaths|גְּדִלִים֙\rb* \rb of|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb chainwork|שַׁרְשְׁר֔וֹת\rb*, \rb seven|שִׁבְעָה֙\rb* \rb for each|הָאֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb capital|לַכֹּתֶ֣רֶת\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לַכֹּתֶ֥רֶת\rb*\rb |הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:17 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa one for each capital\f*
\p \v 18 \rb Likewise, he made|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the pillars|הָעַמּוּדִ֑ים\rb* \rb with two|וּשְׁנֵי֩\rb* \rb rows|טוּרִ֨ים\rb* \rb of pomegranates|הָֽרִמֹּנִ֔ים\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֜יב\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb each|הָאֶחָ֗ת\rb* \rb grating|הַשְּׂבָכָ֣ה\rb* \rb to cover|לְכַסּ֤וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb each capital|הַכֹּֽתָרֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb atop the pillars|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְכֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb*\rb |לַכֹּתֶ֖רֶת\rb*. \v 19 \rb And the capitals|וְכֹֽתָרֹ֗ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb atop|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb the pillars|הָעַמּוּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb in the portico|בָּֽאוּלָ֑ם\rb* \rb were shaped|מַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb like lilies|שׁוּשַׁ֣ן\rb*, \rb four|אַרְבַּ֖ע\rb* \rb cubits high|אַמּֽוֹת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:19 \fqa 4 cubits \ft is approximately 6 feet or 1.8 meters; also in verse 38.\f* \v 20 \rb On|עַל־\rb* \rb the capitals|וְכֹתָרֹ֗ת\rb* \rb of both|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb pillars|הָֽעַמּוּדִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb just|מִלְּעֻמַּ֣ת\rb* \rb above|מִמַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb the rounded projection|הַבֶּ֔טֶן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb next to|לְעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the network|שְׂבָכָה\rb*, \rb were the two hundred|מָאתַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb pomegranates|וְהָרִמּוֹנִ֤ים\rb* \rb in rows|טֻרִ֣ים\rb* \rb encircling|סָבִ֔יב\rb*\rb |עַ֖ל\rb* \rb each capital|הַכֹּתֶ֥רֶת\rb*\rb |הַשֵּׁנִֽית׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Thus he set up|וַיָּ֙קֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the pillars|הָֽעַמֻּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb at the portico|לְאֻלָ֖ם\rb* \rb of the temple|הַֽהֵיכָ֑ל\rb*. \rb The pillar|הָעַמּ֣וּד\rb*\rb |וַיָּ֜קֶם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the south|הַיְמָנִ֗י\rb* \rb he named|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁמוֹ֙\rb* \rb Jachin|יָכִ֔ין\rb*,\f + \fr 7:21 \fqa Jachin \ft probably means \fqa He establishes\ft .\f* \rb and the pillar|הָעַמּ֣וּד\rb*\rb |וַיָּ֙קֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the north|הַשְּׂמָאלִ֔י\rb* \rb he named|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Boaz|בֹּֽעַז׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:21 \fqa Boaz \ft probably means \fqa in Him is strength\ft .\f* \v 22 \rb And|וְעַ֛ל\rb* \rb the tops|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of the pillars|הָעַמּוּדִ֖ים\rb* \rb were shaped|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb like lilies|שׁוֹשָׁ֑ן\rb*. \rb So the work|מְלֶ֥אכֶת\rb* \rb of the pillars|הָעַמּוּדִֽים׃\rb* \rb was completed|וַתִּתֹּ֖ם\rb*.
\s1 The Molten Sea
\r (2 Chronicles 4:1–5)
\p \v 23 \rb He also made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb of cast metal|מוּצָ֑ק\rb*. \rb It was circular in shape|עָגֹ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֗יב\rb*, \rb measuring ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|בָּ֠אַמָּה\rb* \rb from rim|מִשְּׂפָת֨וֹ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb rim|שְׂפָת֜וֹ\rb*, \rb five|וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּה֙\rb* \rb in height|קוֹמָת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb in circumference|וּקְוֵה\rb*\rb |יָסֹ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |סָבִֽיב׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:23 \ft The Sea was approximately 15 feet from rim to rim, 7.5 feet in height, and 45 feet in circumference (4.6 meters from rim to rim, 2.3 meters in height, and 13.7 meters in circumference).\f* \v 24 \rb Below|מִתַּ֨חַת\rb* \rb the rim|לִשְׂפָת֤וֹ׀\rb*, \rb ornamental buds|וּפְקָעִים֩\rb* \rb encircled|סָבִיב֙\rb*\rb |סֹבְבִ֣ים\rb* \rb it|אֹת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb ten|עֶ֚שֶׂר\rb* \rb per cubit|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb all the way|מַקִּפִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb the Sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*,\rb |הַפְּקָעִ֔ים\rb* \rb cast|יְצֻקִ֖ים\rb* \rb in two|שְׁנֵ֤י\rb* \rb rows|טוּרִים֙\rb* \rb as a part of the Sea|בִּיצֻקָתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb The Sea stood|עֹמֵ֞ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb oxen|בָּקָ֗ר\rb*, \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb facing|פֹנִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb north|צָפ֡וֹנָה\rb*, \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁה֩\rb* \rb facing|פֹנִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb west|יָ֜מָּה\rb*, \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה׀\rb* \rb facing|פֹּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb south|נֶ֗גְבָּה\rb*, \rb and three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁה֙\rb* \rb facing|פֹּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb east|מִזְרָ֔חָה\rb*. \rb The Sea|וְהַיָּ֥ם\rb* \rb rested on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |מִלְמָ֑עְלָה\rb*, \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb their hindquarters|אֲחֹֽרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb toward the center|בָּֽיְתָה׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb It was a handbreadth|טֶ֔פַח\rb* \rb thick|וְעָבְי֣וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 7:26 \fqa A handbreadth \ft is approximately 2.9 inches or 7.4 centimeters.\f* \rb and its rim|וּשְׂפָת֛וֹ\rb* \rb was fashioned|כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb like the brim|שְׂפַת־\rb* \rb of a cup|כּ֖וֹס\rb*, \rb like a lily|שׁוֹשָׁ֑ן\rb* \rb blossom|פֶּ֣רַח\rb*. \rb It could hold|יָכִֽיל׃פ\rb* \rb two thousand|אַלְפַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb baths|בַּ֖ת\rb*.\f + \fr 7:26 \fqa 2,000 baths \ft is approximately 11,600 gallons or 44,000 liters; LXX does not include this sentence.\f*
\s1 The Ten Bronze Stands
\p \v 27 \rb In addition, he made|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֖שֶׂר\rb* \rb movable stands|הַמְּכֹנ֛וֹת\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb*, \rb each|הָֽאֶחָ֔ת\rb*\rb |הַמְּכוֹנָ֣ה\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb cubits|בָּאַמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֚רֶךְ\rb*, \rb four|וְאַרְבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּה֙\rb* \rb wide|רָחְבָּ֔הּ\rb*, \rb and three|וְשָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|בָּאַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb high|קוֹמָתָֽהּ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:27 \ft The stands were approximately 6 feet in length and width, and 4.5 feet high (1.8 meters in length and width, and 1.4 meters high).\f*
\p \v 28 \rb This|וְזֶ֛ה\rb* \rb was the design|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb of the stands|הַמְּכוֹנָ֖ה\rb*: \rb They had side panels|מִסְגְּרֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |וּמִסְגְּרֹ֖ת\rb* \rb attached|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb to uprights|הַשְׁלַבִּֽים׃\rb*, \v 29 \rb and on|וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb the panels|הַמִּסְגְּר֞וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the uprights|הַשְׁלַבִּ֗ים\rb* \rb were lions|אֲרָי֤וֹת׀\rb*, \rb oxen|בָּקָר֙\rb*, \rb and cherubim|וּכְרוּבִ֔ים\rb*. \rb On|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the uprights|הַשְׁלַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb was a pedestal|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb above|מִמָּ֑עַל\rb*, \rb and below|וּמִתַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb the lions|לַאֲרָי֣וֹת\rb* \rb and oxen|וְלַבָּקָ֔ר\rb* \rb were wreaths|לֹי֖וֹת\rb* \rb of beveled|מוֹרָֽד׃\rb* \rb work|מַעֲשֵׂ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb Each|הָֽאַחַת֙\rb* \rb stand|לַמְּכוֹנָ֤ה\rb* \rb had four|וְאַרְבָּעָה֩\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֜שֶׁת\rb* \rb wheels|אוֹפַנֵּ֨י\rb* \rb with bronze|נְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb* \rb axles|וְסַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and a basin|לַכִּיֹּר֙\rb* \rb resting on|הַכְּתֵפֹ֣ת\rb* \rb four|וְאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |פַעֲמֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb supports|כְּתֵפֹ֣ת\rb*, \rb with wreaths|לֹיֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb at each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb side|מֵעֵ֥בֶר\rb*. \v 31 \rb The opening to each stand|וּ֠פִיהוּ\rb* \rb inside|מִבֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb the crown|לַכֹּתֶ֤רֶת\rb* \rb at the top|וָמַ֙עְלָה֙\rb* \rb was one cubit deep|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb*,\f + \fr 7:31 \fqa One cubit \ft is approximately 18 inches or 45.7 centimeters.\f* \rb with a round|עָגֹ֣ל\rb* \rb opening|וּפִ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb like the design|מַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb of a pedestal|כֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb a cubit|אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and a half wide|וַחֲצִ֣י\rb*.\f + \fr 7:31 \fqa A cubit and a half \ft is approximately 2.25 feet or 68.6 centimeters wide; similarly in verse 32.\f* \rb And|וְגַם־\rb* \rb around|עַל־\rb* \rb its opening|פִּ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb were engravings|מִקְלָע֔וֹת\rb*, \rb but the panels of the stands were|וּמִסְגְּרֹתֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb square|מְרֻבָּע֖וֹת\rb*, \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb round|עֲגֻלּֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb There were four|וְאַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb* \rb wheels|הָאֽוֹפַנִּ֗ים\rb* \rb under|לְמִתַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb the panels|לַֽמִּסְגְּר֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and the axles|וִיד֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the wheels|הָאֽוֹפַנִּ֖ים\rb* \rb were attached to the stand|בַּמְּכוֹנָ֑ה\rb*; \rb each|הָאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb wheel|הָאוֹפַ֣ן\rb* \rb was a cubit|אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and a half|וַחֲצִ֥י\rb*\rb |הָאַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb in diameter|וְקוֹמַת֙\rb*. \v 33 \rb The wheels|הָא֣וֹפַנִּ֔ים\rb* \rb were made|וּמַֽעֲשֵׂה֙\rb* \rb like|כְּמַעֲשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb chariot|הַמֶּרְכָּבָ֑ה\rb* \rb wheels|אוֹפַ֣ן\rb*; \rb their axles|יְדוֹתָ֣ם\rb*, \rb rims|וְגַבֵּיהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb spokes|וְחִשֻּׁקֵיהֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb and hubs|וְחִשֻּׁרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb were all|הַכֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb of cast metal|מוּצָֽק׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb Each|הָֽאֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb stand|הַמְּכֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb had|אֶ֚ל\rb* \rb four|וְאַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb handles|כְּתֵפ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb one for each|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb corner|פִּנּ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb projecting|כְּתֵפֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the stand|הַמְּכֹנָ֖ה\rb*. \v 35 \rb At the top|וּבְרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of each stand|הַמְּכוֹנָ֗ה\rb* \rb was a circular|עָגֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb band|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֧י\rb* \rb a cubit|הָאַמָּ֛ה\rb* \rb high|קוֹמָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 7:35 \fqa Half a cubit \ft is approximately 9 inches or 22.9 centimeters high.\f* \rb The supports|יְדֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and panels|וּמִסְגְּרֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb were cast as a unit|מִמֶּֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb with|וְעַ֨ל\rb* \rb the top|רֹ֤אשׁ\rb* \rb of the stand|הַמְּכֹנָה֙\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb He engraved|וַיְפַתַּ֤ח\rb* \rb cherubim|כְּרוּבִ֖ים\rb*, \rb lions|אֲרָי֣וֹת\rb*, \rb and palm trees|וְתִמֹרֹ֑ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the surfaces|הַלֻּחֹת֙\rb* \rb of the supports|יְדֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb panels|וּמִסְגְּרֹתֶיהָ\rb*, \rb wherever each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb had space|כְּמַֽעַר־\rb*, \rb with wreaths|וְלֹי֖וֹת\rb* \rb all around|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb In this way|כָּזֹ֣את\rb* \rb he made|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb stands|הַמְּכֹנ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb each|לְכֻלָּֽהְנָה׃ס\rb* \rb with the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb casting|מוּצָ֨ק\rb*,\rb |אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb dimensions|מִדָּ֥ה\rb*,\rb |אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb and shape|קֶ֥צֶב\rb*.
\s1 The Ten Bronze Basins
