\p \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the articles|הַכֵּלִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָאֹהֶל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Huram|חִירָ֛ם\rb* \rb made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for King|לַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb were made of burnished|מְמֹרָֽט׃\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb*. \v 46 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb had them cast|יְצָקָ֣ם\rb* \rb in clay|בְּמַעֲבֵ֖ה\rb* \rb molds|הָאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb in the plain|בְּכִכַּ֤ר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Succoth|סֻכּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Zarethan|צָרְתָֽן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 7:46 \fqa Zarethan \ft is a variant of \fqa Zeredah\ft ; see 2 Chronicles 4:17.\f* \v 47 \rb Solomon left|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these articles|הַכֵּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb unweighed|וַיַּנַּ֤ח\rb*, \rb because there were so|מְאֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb many|מֵרֹ֖ב\rb*. \rb The weight|מִשְׁקַ֥ל\rb* \rb of the bronze|הַנְּחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb* \rb could not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be determined|נֶחְקַ֖ר\rb*.
\s1 Completion of the Gold Furnishings
