\s1 The Ark Enters the Temple
\r (2 Chronicles 5:1–14)
\p \v 1 \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb assembled|יַקְהֵ֣ל\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb* —\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the tribal|הַמַּטּוֹת֩\rb* \rb heads|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb and family leaders|נְשִׂיאֵ֨י\rb*\rb |הָאָב֜וֹת\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* — \rb to bring up|לְֽהַעֲל֞וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֧וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |הִ֥יא\rb* \rb from Zion|צִיּֽוֹן׃\rb*, \rb the City|מֵעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb*. \v 2 \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb came together|וַיִּקָּ֨הֲל֜וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb at the feast|בֶּחָ֑ג\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb in the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִֽי׃\rb* \rb month|הַחֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 8:2 \ft That is, the Feast of Tabernacles (or Booths or Shelters); similarly in verse 65; see Leviticus 23:33–36.\f* \rb the month|בְּיֶ֥רַח\rb* \rb of Ethanim|הָאֵֽתָנִ֖ים\rb*.\f + \fr 8:2 \fqa Ethanim \ft was the seventh month of the ancient Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of September and October.\f*
\p \v 3 \rb When all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb had arrived|וַיָּבֹ֕אוּ\rb*, \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took up|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb the ark|הָאָרֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb and they brought up|וַֽיַּעֲל֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Meeting|מוֹעֵ֔ד\rb* \rb with|וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb its|בָּאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb sacred|הַקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb furnishings|כְּלֵ֥י\rb*. \rb So the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb* \rb carried them up|וַיַּעֲל֣וּ\rb*.\rb |אֹתָ֔ם\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb There, before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the ark|הָֽאָר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb King|וְהַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb and the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb congregation|עֲדַ֤ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb who had assembled|הַנּוֹעָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb with him|עָלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb sacrificed|מְזַבְּחִים֙\rb* \rb so many|מֵרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֣אן\rb* \rb and oxen|וּבָקָ֔ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb they could not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be counted|יִסָּפְר֛וּ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or numbered|יִמָּנ֖וּ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then the priests|הַ֠כֹּהֲנִים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבִ֣אוּ\rb* \rb the ark|אֲר֨וֹן\rb* \rb of the covenant|בְּרִית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb its place|מְקוֹמ֛וֹ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inner sanctuary|דְּבִ֥יר\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*,\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Most Holy Place|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 8:6 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies\f*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb beneath|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the wings|כַּנְפֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִֽים׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִים֙\rb* \rb spread|פֹּרְשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb their wings|כְּנָפַ֔יִם\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb the place|מְק֖וֹם\rb* \rb of the ark|הָאָר֥וֹן\rb*\rb |הַכְּרֻבִ֛ים\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb and overshadowed|וַיָּסֹ֧כּוּ\rb*\rb |מִלְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb the ark|הָֽאָר֑וֹן\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb its poles|בַּדָּ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb The poles|הַבַּדִּ֤ים\rb* \rb extended far enough|וַֽיַּאֲרִכוּ֮\rb* \rb that their|הַבַּדִּים֒\rb* \rb ends|רָאשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb were visible|וַיֵּרָאוּ֩\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Holy Place|הַקֹּ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb front|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the inner sanctuary|הַדְּבִ֔יר\rb*, \rb but not|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |יֵרָא֖וּ\rb* \rb from outside the Holy Place|הַח֑וּצָה\rb*;\f + \fr 8:8 \ft Literally \fqa not from outside\f* \rb and they are|וַיִּ֣הְיוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb There was nothing|אֵ֚ין\rb* \rb in the ark|בָּֽאָר֔וֹן\rb* \rb except|רַ֗ק\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb stone|הָאֲבָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb tablets|לֻח֣וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb had placed|הִנִּ֥חַ\rb* \rb in it|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb at Horeb|בְּחֹרֵ֑ב\rb*,\f + \fr 8:9 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had made a covenant|כָּרַ֤ת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb after they had come out|בְּצֵאתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb And|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb when the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb* \rb came out|בְּצֵ֥את\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the Holy Place|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the cloud|וְהֶעָנָ֥ן\rb* \rb filled|מָלֵ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb so that the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֛ים\rb* \rb could|יָכְל֧וּ\rb* \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb stand there|לַעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb to minister|לְשָׁרֵ֖ת\rb* \rb because|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the cloud|הֶֽעָנָ֑ן\rb*. \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb the glory|כְבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb filled|מָלֵ֥א\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Solomon Blesses the LORD
\r (2 Chronicles 6:1–11)
\p \v 12 \rb Then|אָ֖ז\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb* \rb declared|אָמַ֣ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*\f + \fr 8:12 \ft Some LXX manuscripts \fqa The Lord has set the sun in the heavens, but\f* \rb has said|אָמַ֔ר\rb* \rb that He would dwell|לִשְׁכֹּ֖ן\rb*
\q2 \rb in the thick cloud|בָּעֲרָפֶֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb I have indeed built|בָּנֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |בָנִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb You|לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb an exalted|זְבֻ֖ל\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*,
\q2 \rb a place|מָכ֥וֹן\rb* \rb for You to dwell|לְשִׁבְתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb forever|עוֹלָמִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb And as the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֥ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb stood there|עֹמֵֽד׃\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb turned around|וַיַּסֵּ֤ב\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb and blessed|וַיְבָ֕רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb them all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |קְהַ֣ל\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \v 15 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*:
\pmo “\rb Blessed be|בָּר֤וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb has fulfilled|מִלֵּ֖א\rb* \rb with His own hand|וּבְיָד֥וֹ\rb* \rb what He spoke|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb with His mouth|בְּפִ֔יו\rb* \rb to|אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 16 ‘\rb Since|מִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I brought My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֮\rb* \rb out|הוֹצֵ֜אתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַיִם֒\rb*, \rb I have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb chosen|בָחַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb a city|בְעִ֗יר\rb* \rb from any|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb tribe|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in which to build|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb so that My Name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb would be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*. \rb But I have chosen|וָאֶבְחַ֣ר\rb* \rb David|בְּדָוִ֔ד\rb* \rb to be|לִֽהְי֖וֹת\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’
\pmo \v 17 \rb Now it was|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb the heart|לְבַ֖ב\rb* \rb of my father|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*, ‘\rb Since|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb it was|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָ֣בְךָ֔\rb* \rb to build|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb a house|בַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִ֑י\rb*, \rb you have done well|הֱטִיבֹ֔תָ\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb to have this|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb in|עִם־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Nevertheless|רַ֣ק\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb are not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the one to build it|תִבְנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*; \rb but|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb your son|בִּנְךָ֙\rb*, \rb your own offspring|הַיֹּצֵ֣א\rb*\rb |מֵחֲלָצֶ֔יךָ\rb*,\rb |הֽוּא־\rb* \rb will build|יִבְנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִֽי׃\rb*.’
\pmo \v 20 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has fulfilled|וַיָּ֣קֶם\rb* \rb the word|דְּבָר֖וֹ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He spoke|דִּבֵּ֑ר\rb*. \rb I have succeeded|וָאָקֻ֡ם\rb*\rb |תַּחַת֩\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֜י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֨ד\rb*, \rb and I sit|וָאֵשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb promised|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb*. \rb I have built|וָאֶבְנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb for the Name|לְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb And there I have provided|וָאָשִׂ֨ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb a place|מָקוֹם֙\rb* \rb for the ark|לָֽאָר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb which contains|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb He made|כָּרַת֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb when He brought them out|בְּהוֹצִיא֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 Solomon’s Prayer of Dedication
\r (2 Chronicles 6:12–42)
\p \v 22 \rb Then Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in front of|נֶ֖גֶד\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb spread out|וַיִּפְרֹ֥שׂ\rb* \rb his hands|כַּפָּ֖יו\rb* \rb toward heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*, \v 23 \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֗ר\rb*:
\pmo “\rb O LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb there is no|אֵין־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb like You|כָּמ֣וֹךָ\rb* \rb in heaven|בַּשָּׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb above|מִמַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb or on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb below|מִתָּ֑חַת\rb*, \rb keeping|שֹׁמֵ֤ר\rb* \rb Your covenant|הַבְּרִית֙\rb* \rb of loving devotion|וְֽהַחֶ֔סֶד\rb* \rb with Your servants|לַעֲבָדֶ֕יךָ\rb* \rb who walk|הַהֹלְכִ֥ים\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their hearts|לִבָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb You have kept|שָׁמַ֗רְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Your promise|דִּבַּ֖רְתָּ\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb to Your servant|לְעַבְדְּךָ֙\rb*, \rb my father|אָבִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*. \rb What You spoke|וַתְּדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with Your mouth|בְּפִ֛יךָ\rb* \rb You have fulfilled|מִלֵּ֖אתָ\rb* \rb with Your hand|וּבְיָדְךָ֥\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*.
\pmo \v 25 \rb Therefore now|וְעַתָּ֞ה\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb keep|שְׁ֠מֹר\rb* \rb for Your servant|לְעַבְדְּךָ֨\rb*, \rb my father|אָבִי֙\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֤ד\rb*, \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb You promised|דִּבַּ֤רְתָּ\rb* \rb when You said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*: ‘\rb You will never|לֹא־\rb* \rb fail|יִכָּרֵ֨ת\rb*\rb |לְךָ֥\rb* \rb to have a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb to sit|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb before Me|מִלְּפָנַ֔י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb only|רַ֠ק\rb* \rb your descendants|בָנֶ֤יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb guard|יִשְׁמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb their way|דַּרְכָּם֙\rb* \rb to walk|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֔י\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have done|הָלַ֖כְתָּ\rb*\rb |לְפָנָֽי׃\rb*.’ \v 26 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb*, \rb O God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb please|נָא֙\rb* \rb confirm|יֵאָ֤מֶן\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You promised|דְּבָרֶיךָ\rb*\rb |דִּבַּ֔רְתָּ\rb* \rb to Your servant|לְעַבְדְּךָ֖\rb*, \rb my father|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb*.
\pmo \v 27 \rb But|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb will God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb indeed|הַֽאֻמְנָ֔ם\rb* \rb dwell|יֵשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*?\rb |הִ֠נֵּה\rb* \rb The heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֜יִם\rb*, \rb even the highest heavens|וּשְׁמֵ֤י\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb cannot|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb contain You|יְכַלְכְּל֔וּךָ\rb*, \rb much less|אַ֕ף\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb temple|הַבַּ֥יִת\rb* \rb I have built|בָּנִֽיתִי׃\rb*. \v 28 \rb Yet regard|וּפָנִ֜יתָ\rb* \rb the prayer|תְּפִלַּ֧ת\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb plea|תְּחִנָּת֖וֹ\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֛\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb*, \rb so that You may hear|לִשְׁמֹ֤עַ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the cry|הָֽרִנָּה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and the prayer|הַתְּפִלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֛\rb* \rb is praying|מִתְפַּלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb today|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*.
