\pmo \v 31 \rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb When|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb sins|יֶחֱטָ֥א\rb* \rb against his neighbor|לְרֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and is required|וְנָֽשָׁא־\rb* \rb to take an oath|אָלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְהַֽאֲלֹת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and he comes|וּבָ֗א\rb* \rb to take an oath|אָלָ֛ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Your altar|מִֽזְבַּחֲךָ֖\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb temple|בַּבַּ֥יִת\rb*, \v 32 \rb then may You|וְאַתָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb hear|תִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb from heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֗יִם\rb* \rb and act|וְעָשִׂ֙יתָ֙\rb*. \rb May You judge|וְשָׁפַטְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb condemning|לְהַרְשִׁ֣יעַ\rb* \rb the wicked man|רָשָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb by bringing|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb down on his own head|בְּרֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb what he has done|דַּרְכּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and justifying|וּלְהַצְדִּ֣יק\rb* \rb the righteous man|צַדִּ֔יק\rb* \rb by rewarding|לָ֥תֶת\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb according to his righteousness|כְּצִדְקָתֽוֹ׃ס\rb*.
