\pmo \v 51 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֑ם\rb* \rb are Your people|עַמְּךָ֥\rb* \rb and Your inheritance|וְנַחֲלָתְךָ֖\rb*; \rb You brought them|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb out|הוֹצֵ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb out|מִתּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the furnace|כּ֥וּר\rb* \rb for iron|הַבַּרְזֶֽל׃\rb*. \v 52 \rb May Your eyes|עֵינֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb be|לִהְי֨וֹת\rb* \rb open|פְתֻחוֹת֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the pleas|תְּחִנַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb of|תְּחִנַּ֖ת\rb* \rb Your people|עַמְּךָ֣\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and may You listen|לִשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb whenever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb they call|קָרְאָ֥ם\rb* \rb to You|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 53 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֞ה\rb*, \rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*, \rb have set them apart|הִבְדַּלְתָּ֤ם\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the peoples|עַמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb as Your inheritance|לְֽנַחֲלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb You spoke|דִּבַּ֜רְתָּ\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדֶּ֗ךָ\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb when You brought|בְּהוֹצִיאֲךָ֧\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֛ינוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֖יִם\rb*.”
\s1 Solomon’s Benediction
\p \v 54 \rb Now when|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb* \rb had finished|כְּכַלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb praying|לְהִתְפַּלֵּל֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb prayer|הַתְּפִלָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and petition|וְהַתְּחִנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb*, \rb he got up|קָ֞ם\rb* \rb before|מִלִּפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֤ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb where he had been kneeling|מִכְּרֹ֣עַ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בִּרְכָּ֔יו\rb* \rb with his hands|וְכַפָּ֖יו\rb* \rb spread out|פְּרֻשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb toward heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 55 \rb And he stood|וַֽיַּעְמֹ֕ד\rb* \rb and blessed|וַיְבָ֕רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb in a loud|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb voice|ק֥וֹל\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*:
\pmo \v 56 “\rb Blessed be|בָּר֣וּךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb has given|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb rest|מְנוּחָה֙\rb* \rb to His people|לְעַמּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb according to all|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He promised|דִּבֵּ֑ר\rb*. \rb Not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb word|דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb has failed|נָפַ֞ל\rb* \rb of all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the good|הַטּ֔וֹב\rb* \rb promises|דְּבָר֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He made|דִּבֶּ֔ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֥ה\rb*.
\pmo \v 57 \rb May the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֨י\rb* \rb with us|עִמָּ֔נוּ\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He was|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb*. \rb May He never|אַל־\rb* \rb leave us|יַעַזְבֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb or|וְאַֽל־\rb* \rb forsake us|יִטְּשֵֽׁנוּ׃\rb*. \v 58 \rb May He incline|לְהַטּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb our hearts|לְבָבֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to Himself|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb to walk|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb His ways|דְּרָכָ֗יו\rb* \rb and to keep|וְלִשְׁמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺתָ֤יו\rb* \rb and statutes|וְחֻקָּיו֙\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He commanded|צִוָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבֹתֵֽינוּ׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 59 \rb And may|וְיִֽהְי֨וּ\rb* \rb these|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb words|דְבָרַ֜י\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I have made my petition|הִתְחַנַּ֙נְתִּי֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb be near|קְרֹבִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֣ם\rb* \rb and night|וָלָ֑יְלָה\rb*, \rb so that He may uphold|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת׀\rb* \rb the cause|מִשְׁפַּ֣ט\rb* \rb of His servant|עַבְדּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and|וּמִשְׁפַּ֛ט\rb* \rb of His people|עַמּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb as each day|י֥וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּיוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb requires|דְּבַר־\rb*, \v 60 \rb so that|לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the peoples|עַמֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb may know|דַּ֚עַת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb There is no|אֵ֖ין\rb* \rb other|עֽוֹד׃\rb*!
\pmo \v 61 \rb So let your heart|לְבַבְכֶם֙\rb* \rb be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb fully devoted|שָׁלֵ֔ם\rb* \rb to|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ\rb*, \rb as it is|כַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb this day|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*, \rb to walk|לָלֶ֧כֶת\rb* \rb in His statutes|בְּחֻקָּ֛יו\rb* \rb and to keep|וְלִשְׁמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb His commandments|מִצְוֺתָ֖יו\rb*.”
\s1 Sacrifices of Dedication
\r (2 Chronicles 7:4–10)
\p \v 62 \rb Then the king|וְֽהַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb offered|זֹבְחִ֥ים\rb* \rb sacrifices|זֶ֖בַח\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 63 \rb And Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb offered as|וַיִּזְבַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb peace offerings|הַשְּׁלָמִים֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |זָבַ֣ח\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָה֒\rb* \rb 22,000|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb oxen|בָּקָ֗ר\rb* \rb and 120,000|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb sheep|וְצֹ֕אן\rb*. \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb dedicated|וַֽיַּחְנְכוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*.
\p \v 64 \rb On that same|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb consecrated|קִדַּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb the middle|תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the courtyard|הֶחָצֵ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and|כִּי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he offered|עָ֣שָׂה\rb* \rb the burnt offerings|הָֽעֹלָה֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the grain offerings|הַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the fat|חֶלְבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the peace offerings|הַשְּׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבַּ֤ח\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb was too small|קָטֹ֗ן\rb* \rb to contain|מֵֽהָכִיל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all these offerings|הָעֹלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |הַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |חֶלְבֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַשְּׁלָמִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 65 \rb So at that|הַהִ֣יא׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb time|בָֽעֵת־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb with him|עִמּוֹ֩\rb*— \rb a great|גָּד֜וֹל\rb* \rb assembly of people|קָהָ֨ל\rb*\rb |מִלְּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb from Lebo-hamath|חֲמָ֣ת׀\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Brook|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb*— \rb kept|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb the feast|הֶחָ֡ג\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and seven more|וְשִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb*— \rb fourteen|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb days in all|יֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\p \v 66 \rb On the fifteenth|הַשְּׁמִינִי֙\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֤וֹם\rb*\f + \fr 8:66 \ft Hebrew \fqa On the eighth day\ft , probably referring to the day following the seven-day feast; see 2 Chronicles 7:9–10.\f* \rb Solomon sent the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb away|שִׁלַּ֣ח\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb So they blessed|וַֽיְבָרֲכ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb home|לְאָהֳלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb joyful|שְׂמֵחִים֙\rb* \rb and glad|וְט֣וֹבֵי\rb* \rb in heart|לֵ֔ב\rb* \rb for|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the good things|הַטּוֹבָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb for His servant|עַבְדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb David|לְדָוִ֣ד\rb* \rb and for His people|עַמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Israel|וּלְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.
\c 9
\s1 The LORD’s Response to Solomon
\r (2 Chronicles 7:11–22)
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb when Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb had finished|כְּכַלּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb building|לִבְנ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and had achieved|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃פ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb had desired|חֵ֣שֶׁק\rb* \rb to do|חָפֵ֖ץ\rb*, \v 2 \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֧א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb a second time|שֵׁנִ֑ית\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb He had appeared|נִרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb at Gibeon|בְּגִבְעֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*:
\pmo “\rb I have heard|שָׁמַ֖עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your prayer|תְּפִלָּתְךָ֣\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and petition|תְּחִנָּתְךָ֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |הִתְחַנַּ֣נְתָּה\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַי֒\rb*. \rb I have consecrated|הִקְדַּ֗שְׁתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb temple|הַבַּ֤יִת\rb*, \rb which you have built|בָּנִ֔תָה\rb*, \rb by putting|לָשֽׂוּם־\rb* \rb My Name|שְׁמִ֥י\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֑ם\rb*; \rb My eyes|עֵינַ֧י\rb* \rb and My heart|וְלִבִּ֛י\rb* \rb will be|וְהָי֨וּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb for all|כָּל־\rb* \rb time|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*.
\pmo \v 4 \rb And as for you|וְאַתָּ֞ה\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you walk|תֵּלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֗י\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb walked|הָלַ֜ךְ\rb*, \rb with a heart|לֵבָ֣ב\rb* \rb of integrity|בְּתָם־\rb* \rb and uprightness|וּבְיֹ֔שֶׁר\rb*, \rb doing|לַעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have commanded you|צִוִּיתִ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb and if you keep|תִּשְׁמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקַּ֥י\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטַ֖י\rb*, \v 5 \rb then I will establish|וַהֲקִ֨מֹתִ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your royal|מַֽמְלַכְתְּךָ֛\rb* \rb throne|כִּסֵּ֧א\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel forever|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לְעֹלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I promised|דִּבַּ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb when I said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb You will never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb fail|יִכָּרֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to have a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb on|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’
\pmo \v 6 \rb But if|אִם־\rb* \rb indeed|שׁ֨וֹב\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb or your sons|וּבְנֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb turn away|תְּשֻׁב֜וּן\rb* \rb from following Me|מֵֽאַחֲרַ֔י\rb* \rb and do not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb keep|תִשְׁמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֣י\rb* \rb and statutes|חֻקֹּתַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have set|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb before you|לִפְנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and if you go off|וַהֲלַכְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb to serve|וַעֲבַדְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb and worship|וְהִשְׁתַּחֲוִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*\rb |לָהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 7 \rb then I will cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֨ל\rb* \rb the land|הָאֲדָמָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and I will banish|אֲשַׁלַּ֖ח\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb My presence|פָּנָ֑י\rb* \rb this|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have sanctified|הִקְדַּ֣שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb for My Name|לִשְׁמִ֔י\rb*. \rb Then Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb will become|וְהָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb an object of scorn|לְמָשָׁ֥ל\rb* \rb and ridicule|וְלִשְׁנִינָ֖ה\rb* \rb among all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb peoples|הָעַמִּֽים׃\rb*.
