\p \v 24 \rb As soon as|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb had come up|עָֽלְתָה֙\rb* \rb from the City|מֵעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the palace|בֵּיתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Solomon had built|בָּֽנָה־\rb* \rb for her|לָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb he|אָ֖ז\rb* \rb built|בָּנָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the supporting terraces|הַמִּלּֽוֹא׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Three|שָׁלֹשׁ֩\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֨ים\rb* \rb a year|בַּשָּׁנָ֜ה\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֡ה\rb* \rb offered|וְהֶעֱלָ֣ה\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֣וֹת\rb* \rb and peace offerings|וּשְׁלָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had built|בָּנָ֣ה\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb burning incense|וְהַקְטֵ֣יר\rb* \rb with them|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb So he completed|וְשִׁלַּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb* \rb also assembled|עָשָׂה֩\rb* \rb a fleet of ships|וָאֳנִ֡י\rb*\rb |בְּעֶצְיֽוֹן־\rb* \rb at Ezion-geber|גֶּ֨בֶר\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb is near|אֶת־\rb* \rb Eloth|אֵל֛וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 9:26 \fqa Eloth \ft is a variant of \fqa Elath\ft ; see LXX, 2 Kings 14:22, and 2 Kings 16:6.\f* \rb in|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb Edom|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*, \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the shore|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Red|ס֖וּף\rb* \rb Sea|יַם־\rb*.\f + \fr 9:26 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \v 27 \rb And Hiram|חִירָ֤ם\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb sailors|אֳנִיּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb who knew|יֹדְעֵ֖י\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb to serve in the fleet|בָּֽאֳנִי֙\rb* \rb with|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb*. \v 28 \rb They sailed|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to Ophir|אוֹפִ֔ירָה\rb* \rb and imported|וַיִּקְח֤וּ\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁם֙\rb*— \rb 420|אַרְבַּע־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכָּ֑ר\rb*\f + \fr 9:28 \fqa 420 talents \ft is approximately 15.8 tons or 14.4 metric tons of gold.\f*— \rb and delivered|וַיָּבִ֖אוּ\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 The Queen of Sheba
\r (2 Chronicles 9:1–12)
\p \v 1 \rb Now when the queen|וּמַֽלְכַּת־\rb* \rb of Sheba|שְׁבָ֗א\rb* \rb heard|שֹׁמַ֛עַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb about the fame|שֵׁ֥מַע\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb concerning the name|לְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb she came|וַתָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to test him|לְנַסֹּת֖וֹ\rb* \rb with difficult questions|בְּחִידֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb She arrived|וַתָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלְַ֗מָה\rb* \rb with a very|מְאֹד֒\rb* \rb large|כָּבֵ֣ד\rb* \rb caravan|בְּחַיִל֮\rb*— \rb with camels|גְּ֠מַלִּים\rb* \rb bearing|נֹשְׂאִ֨ים\rb* \rb spices|בְּשָׂמִ֧ים\rb*, \rb gold|וְזָהָ֛ב\rb* \rb in great|מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb abundance|רַב־\rb*, \rb and precious|יְקָרָ֑ה\rb* \rb stones|וְאֶ֣בֶן\rb*.
\p \rb And she came|וַתָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb and spoke|וַתְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to him|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb on|עִם־\rb* \rb her mind|לְבָבָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb And Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her questions|דְּבָרֶ֑יהָ\rb*; \rb nothing|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |דָּבָר֙\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb too difficult|נֶעְלָ֣ם\rb* \rb for|מִן־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb*\rb |לֹ֦א\rb* \rb to explain|הִגִּ֖יד\rb*\rb |לָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb When the queen|מַֽלְכַּת־\rb* \rb of Sheba|שְׁבָ֔א\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb saw|וַתֵּ֙רֶא֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the wisdom|חָכְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb the palace|וְהַבַּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had built|בָּנָֽה׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb the food|וּמַאֲכַ֣ל\rb* \rb at his table|שֻׁלְחָנ֡וֹ\rb*, \rb the seating|וּמוֹשַׁ֣ב\rb* \rb of his servants|עֲבָדָיו֩\rb*, \rb the service|וּמַעֲמַ֨ד\rb* \rb and attire|וּמַלְבֻּֽשֵׁיהֶם֙\rb* \rb of his attendants|מְשָׁרְתוֹ\rb*, \rb his cupbearers|וּמַשְׁקָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and the burnt offerings|וְעֹ֣לָת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he presented|יַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb at the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb it took her breath|רֽוּחַ׃\rb* \rb away|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |הָ֥יָה\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb She said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*, “\rb The report|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I heard|שָׁמַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb in my own country|בְּאַרְצִ֑י\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb your words|דְּבָרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb is|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb true|אֱמֶת֙\rb*. \v 7 \rb But I did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb believe|הֶאֱמַ֣נְתִּי\rb* \rb these things|לַדְּבָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb until|עַ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I came|בָּ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb and saw|וַתִּרְאֶ֣ינָה\rb* \rb with my own eyes|עֵינַ֔י\rb*. \rb Indeed|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb not even|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb half|הַחֵ֑צִי\rb* \rb was told|הֻגַּד־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֖י\rb*. \rb Your wisdom|חָכְמָה֙\rb* \rb and prosperity|וָט֔וֹב\rb* \rb have far|אֶל־\rb* \rb exceeded|הוֹסַ֤פְתָּ\rb* \rb the report|הַשְּׁמוּעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I heard|שָׁמָֽעְתִּי׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb How blessed|אַשְׁרֵ֣י\rb* \rb are your men|אֲנָשֶׁ֔יךָ\rb*!\f + \fr 10:8 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate \fqa your wives\f* \rb How blessed|אַשְׁרֵ֖י\rb* \rb are these|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb servants of yours|עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb who stand|הָֽעֹמְדִ֤ים\rb* \rb continually|תָּמִ֔יד\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and hear|הַשֹּׁמְעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your wisdom|חָכְמָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*! \v 9 \rb Blessed|בָּר֔וּךְ\rb* \rb be|יְהִ֨י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb has delighted|חָפֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb in you|בְּךָ֔\rb* \rb to set|לְתִתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb you on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Because of the LORD’s|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb eternal|לְעֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb love|בְּאַהֲבַ֨ת\rb* \rb for Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb He has made you|וַיְשִֽׂימְךָ֣\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb to carry out|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb and righteousness|וּצְדָקָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Then she gave|וַתִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb 120|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֗ב\rb*,\f + \fr 10:10 \fqa 120 talents \ft is approximately 4.52 tons or 4.1 metric tons of gold.\f* \rb a great quantity of|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb spices|וּבְשָׂמִ֛ים\rb*, \rb and precious|יְקָרָ֑ה\rb* \rb stones|וְאֶ֣בֶן\rb*. \rb Never|לֹא־\rb* \rb again|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb were spices|כַבֹּ֨שֶׂם\rb* \rb in such|הַה֥וּא\rb* \rb abundance|לָרֹ֔ב\rb* \rb brought in|בָא֩\rb* \rb as those|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the queen|מַֽלְכַּת־\rb* \rb of Sheba|שְׁבָ֖א\rb* \rb gave|נָתְנָ֥ה\rb* \rb to King|לַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 (\rb The fleet|אֳנִ֣י\rb* \rb of Hiram|חִירָ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb brought|נָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb from Ophir|מֵאוֹפִ֑יר\rb* \rb also|וְגַם֙\rb* \rb brought|הֵבִ֨יא\rb* \rb from Ophir|מֵאֹפִ֜יר\rb* \rb a great cargo|הַרְבֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb of almug|אַלְמֻגִּ֛ים\rb*\f + \fr 10:11 \fqa Almug \ft is probably a variant of \fqa algum\ft ; also in verse 12; see 2 Chronicles 2:8.\f* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֧י\rb* \rb and precious|יְקָרָֽה׃\rb* \rb stones|וְאֶ֥בֶן\rb*. \v 12 \rb The king|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb the almug|הָאַלְמֻגִּ֜ים\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֨י\rb* \rb into steps|מִסְעָ֤ד\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and for the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|וּלְבֵ֣ית\rb*, \rb and into lyres|וְכִנֹּר֥וֹת\rb* \rb and harps|וּנְבָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb for the singers|לַשָּׁרִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb before had such|כֵ֞ן\rb* \rb almug|אַלְמֻגִּים֙\rb* \rb wood|עֲצֵ֤י\rb* \rb been brought in|בָֽא־\rb*, \rb nor has such|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb been seen again|נִרְאָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*.)
\p \v 13 \rb King|וְהַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb the queen|לְמַֽלְכַּת־\rb* \rb of Sheba|שְׁבָ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb she desired|חֶפְצָהּ֙\rb* — \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb she asked|שָׁאָ֔לָה\rb* — \rb besides|מִלְּבַד֙\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb her|לָ֔הּ\rb* \rb out of his|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb* \rb royal|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb bounty|כְּיַ֖ד\rb*. \rb Then she left|וַתֵּ֛פֶן\rb* \rb and returned|וַתֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to her own country|לְאַרְצָ֖הּ\rb*, \rb along with her servants|וַעֲבָדֶֽיהָ׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Solomon’s Wealth and Splendor
\r (2 Chronicles 1:14–17; 2 Chronicles 9:13–28)
\p \v 14 \rb The weight|מִשְׁקַ֣ל\rb* \rb of gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb each year|בְּשָׁנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb was|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb 666|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֛וֹת\rb*\rb |שִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וָשֵׁ֖שׁ\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּ֥ר\rb*\rb |זָהָֽב׃\rb*,\f + \fr 10:14 \fqa 666 talents \ft is approximately 25.1 tons or 22.8 metric tons of gold.\f* \v 15 \rb not including|לְבַד֙\rb* \rb the revenue|וּמִסְחַ֖ר\rb* \rb from the merchants|מֵאַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |הַתָּרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb traders|הָרֹכְלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Arabian|הָעֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb and governors|וּפַח֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb two hundred|מָאתַ֥יִם\rb* \rb large shields|צִנָּ֖ה\rb* \rb of hammered|שָׁח֑וּט\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*; \rb six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred shekels|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb*\f + \fr 10:16 \fqa 600 shekels \ft is approximately 15.1 pounds or 6.8 kilograms of gold.\f* \rb went|יַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb each|הָאֶחָֽת׃\rb* \rb shield|הַצִּנָּ֥ה\rb*. \v 17 \rb He also made three|וּשְׁלֹשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֤וֹת\rb* \rb small shields|מָֽגִנִּים֙\rb* \rb of hammered|שָׁח֔וּט\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*; \rb three|שְׁלֹ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb minas|מָנִים֙\rb* \rb of gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb*\f + \fr 10:17 \fqa 3 minas \ft is approximately 3.77 pounds or 1.71 kilograms of gold; possibly a reference to double minas, that is, approximately 7.54 pounds or 3.42 kilograms.\f* \rb went|יַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb each|הָאֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb shield|הַמָּגֵ֣ן\rb*. \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb put them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֣ם\rb* \rb in the House|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of the Forest|יַ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Lebanon|הַלְּבָנֽוֹן׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Additionally, the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb throne|כִּסֵּא־\rb* \rb of ivory|שֵׁ֖ן\rb* \rb and overlaid it|וַיְצַפֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with pure|מוּפָֽז׃\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֥ב\rb*. \v 19 \rb The throne|לַכִּסֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb had six|שֵׁ֧שׁ\rb* \rb steps|מַעֲל֣וֹת\rb*, \rb and its back|מֵאַֽחֲרָ֔יו\rb*\rb |לַכִּסֵּה֙\rb* \rb had a rounded|עָגֹ֤ל\rb* \rb top|וְרֹאשׁ־\rb*. \rb There were armrests|וְיָדֹ֛ת\rb* \rb on both sides|וּמִזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |מִזֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the seat|מְק֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁ֑בֶת\rb*, \rb with a|וּשְׁנַ֣יִם\rb* \rb lion|אֲרָי֔וֹת\rb* \rb standing|עֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֥צֶל\rb* \rb each armrest|הַיָּדֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb Twelve|וּשְׁנֵ֧ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb lions|אֲרָיִ֗ים\rb* \rb stood|עֹמְדִ֥ים\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the six|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb steps|הַֽמַּעֲל֖וֹת\rb*, \rb one at either end|מִזֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb of each step|וּמִזֶּ֑ה\rb*. \rb Nothing|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb like this|כֵ֖ן\rb* \rb had ever been made|נַעֲשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for any|לְכָל־\rb* \rb kingdom|מַמְלָכֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb All|וְ֠כֹל\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon’s|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb drinking|מַשְׁקֵ֨ה\rb* \rb cups|כְּלֵ֞י\rb* \rb were gold|זָהָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb the utensils|כְּלֵ֛י\rb* \rb of the House|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of the Forest|יַ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֖וֹן\rb* \rb were pure|סָג֑וּר\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*. \rb There was no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֗סֶף\rb*, \rb because it was accounted|נֶחְשָׁ֛ב\rb* \rb as nothing|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |לִמְאֽוּמָה׃\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb*. \v 22 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the king had|לַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb the ships|אֳנִ֨י\rb* \rb of Tarshish|תַרְשִׁ֤ישׁ\rb*\f + \fr 10:22 \ft Or \fqa a fleet of trading ships\ft ; twice in this verse\f* \rb at sea|בַּיָּ֔ם\rb* \rb with|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb Hiram’s|חִירָ֑ם\rb* \rb fleet|אֳנִ֣י\rb*, \rb and once|אַחַת֩\rb* \rb every three years|לְשָׁלֹ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֜ים\rb* \rb the ships|אֳנִ֣י\rb* \rb of Tarshish|תַרְשִׁ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb would arrive|תָּב֣וֹא׀\rb* \rb bearing|נֹֽשְׂאֵת֙\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֣ב\rb*, \rb silver|וָכֶ֔סֶף\rb*, \rb ivory|שֶׁנְהַבִּ֥ים\rb*, \rb apes|וְקֹפִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and peacocks|וְתֻכִּיִּֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 10:22 \ft Or \fqa baboons\f*
\p \v 23 \rb So King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb surpassed|וַיִּגְדַּל֙\rb* \rb all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb in riches|לְעֹ֖שֶׁר\rb* \rb and wisdom|וּלְחָכְמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb The whole|וְכָ֨ל־\rb* \rb world|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb sought|מְבַקְשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an audience|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb with Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb* \rb to hear|לִשְׁמֹ֙עַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wisdom|חָכְמָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb had put|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb in his heart|בְּלִבּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb |דְּבַר־\rb* \rb Year|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb after year|בְּשָׁנָֽה׃ס\rb*,\rb |וְהֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb each visitor|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb would bring|מְבִאִ֣ים\rb* \rb his tribute|מִנְחָת֡וֹ\rb*: \rb articles|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of silver|כֶסֶף֩\rb*\rb |וּכְלֵ֨י\rb* \rb and gold|זָהָ֤ב\rb*, \rb clothing|וּשְׂלָמוֹת֙\rb*, \rb weapons|וְנֵ֣שֶׁק\rb*, \rb spices|וּבְשָׂמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb horses|סוּסִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and mules|וּפְרָדִ֑ים\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֮\rb* \rb accumulated|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֣ף\rb*\rb |רֶ֣כֶב\rb*\rb |וּפָרָשִׁים֒\rb*\rb |וַיְהִי־\rb*\f + \fr 10:26 \ft Literally \fqa Solomon accumulated chariots and horses; he had\f* \rb 1,400|אֶ֤לֶף\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּע־\rb*\rb |מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb and 12,000|וּשְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb horses|פָּֽרָשִׁ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 10:26 \ft Or \fqa horsemen \ft or \fqa charioteers\f* \rb which he stationed|וַיַּנְחֵם֙\rb* \rb in the chariot|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and also with|וְעִם־\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb silver|הַכֶּ֛סֶף\rb* \rb as common in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb as stones|כָּאֲבָנִ֑ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and|נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb cedar|הָאֲרָזִ֗ים\rb* \rb as abundant|לָרֹֽב׃\rb* \rb as sycamore|כַּשִּׁקְמִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the foothills|בַּשְּׁפֵלָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 10:27 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f*
\p \v 28 \rb Solomon’s|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |לִשְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb horses|הַסּוּסִ֛ים\rb* \rb were imported|וּמוֹצָ֧א\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and Kue|וּמִקְוֵ֕ה\rb*;\f + \fr 10:28 \ft Probably an area in Cilicia, a province in the southeast of Asia Minor\f* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb merchants|סֹחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb purchased them|יִקְח֥וּ\rb*\rb |בִּמְחִֽיר׃\rb* \rb from Kue|מִקְוֵ֖ה\rb*. \v 29 \rb A chariot|מֶרְכָּבָ֤ה\rb* \rb could be imported|וַֽ֠תַּעֲלֶה\rb*\rb |וַתֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb for six|בְּשֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb hundred shekels|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 10:29 \fqa 600 shekels \ft is approximately 15.1 pounds or 6.8 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb and a horse|וְס֖וּס\rb* \rb for a hundred|וּמֵאָ֑ה\rb* \rb and fifty|בַּחֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*.\f + \fr 10:29 \fqa 150 shekels \ft is approximately 3.8 pounds or 1.7 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb Likewise|וְ֠כֵן\rb*, \rb they|בְּיָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb exported them|יֹצִֽאוּ׃פ\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the Hittites|הַחִתִּ֛ים\rb* \rb and to the kings|וּלְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb*.
\c 11
\s1 Solomon’s Foreign Wives
\p \v 1 \rb King|וְהַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon, however|שְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb*, \rb loved|אָהַ֞ב\rb* \rb many|רַבּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb foreign|נָכְרִיּ֛וֹת\rb* \rb women|נָשִׁ֧ים\rb* \rb along with the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* — \rb women of Moab|מוֹאֲבִיּ֤וֹת\rb*, \rb Ammon|עַמֳּנִיּוֹת֙\rb*, \rb Edom|אֲדֹ֣מִיֹּ֔ת\rb*, \rb and Sidon|צֵדְנִיֹּ֖ת\rb*, \rb as well as Hittite women|חִתִּיֹּֽת׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb These women were from|מִן־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb* \rb about which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb* \rb had told|אָֽמַר־\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*, “\rb You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb intermarry|תָבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb with them|בָהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְהֵם֙\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb*\rb |יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |בָכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb for surely|אָכֵן֙\rb* \rb they will turn|יַטּ֣וּ\rb* \rb your hearts|לְבַבְכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb their gods|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*.” \rb Yet Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb clung|דָּבַ֥ק\rb* \rb to these women|בָּהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb in love|לְאַהֲבָֽה׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb He had|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb seven|שְׁבַ֣ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb wives|נָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb of royal birth|שָׂרוֹת֙\rb* \rb and three|שְׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֑וֹת\rb* \rb concubines|וּפִֽלַגְשִׁ֖ים\rb* — \rb and his wives|נָשָׁ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb turned his heart|לִבּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb away|וַיַּטּ֥וּ\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb For when|לְעֵת֙\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb grew|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb old|זִקְנַ֣ת\rb*, \rb his wives|נָשָׁיו֙\rb* \rb turned|הִטּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֔וֹ\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*, \rb and he was|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb wholeheartedly|לְבָב֤וֹ\rb* \rb devoted|שָׁלֵם֙\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |כִּלְבַ֖ב\rb* \rb as his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb David had been|דָּוִ֥יד\rb*. \v 5 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb followed|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Ashtoreth|עַשְׁתֹּ֔רֶת\rb* \rb the goddess|אֱלֹהֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the Sidonians|צִדֹנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and Milcom|מִלְכֹּ֔ם\rb*\f + \fr 11:5 \fqa Milcom \ft is a variant of \fqa Molech\ft ; also in verse 33; see verse 7 and Leviticus 18:21.\f* \rb the abomination|שִׁקֻּ֖ץ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|עַמֹּנִֽים׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb So Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb unlike his father|אָבִֽיו׃ס\rb* \rb David|כְּדָוִ֥ד\rb*, \rb he did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb follow|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb completely|מִלֵּ֛א\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb At that time|אָז֩\rb* \rb on a hill|בָּהָ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb east|עַל־\rb* \rb of|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*, \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb* \rb built|יִבְנֶ֨ה\rb* \rb a high place|בָּמָ֗ה\rb* \rb for Chemosh|לִכְמוֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb the abomination|שִׁקֻּ֣ץ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb and for Molech|וּלְמֹ֕לֶךְ\rb* \rb the abomination|שִׁקֻּ֖ץ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb He did|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb the same|וְכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb his foreign|הַנָּכְרִיּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb wives|נָשָׁ֖יו\rb*, \rb who burned incense|מַקְטִיר֥וֹת\rb* \rb and sacrificed|וּֽמְזַבְּח֖וֹת\rb* \rb to their gods|לֵאלֹהֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\s1 God’s Anger against Solomon
\p \v 9 \rb Now the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb grew angry|וַיִּתְאַנַּ֥ף\rb* \rb with Solomon|בִּשְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֗וֹ\rb* \rb had turned away|נָטָ֣ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֤ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb who had appeared|הַנִּרְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb twice|פַּעֲמָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb Although He had warned Solomon|וְצִוָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb explicitly|עַל־\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb not|לְבִ֨לְתִּי־\rb* \rb to follow|לֶ֔כֶת\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*, \rb Solomon did not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb keep|שָׁמַ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb* \rb command|צִוָּ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֗ה\rb*, “\rb Because|יַ֚עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have done|הָֽיְתָה־\rb*\rb |עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb this|זֹּ֣את\rb* \rb and have not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb kept|שָׁמַ֙רְתָּ֙\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֣י\rb* \rb and My statutes|וְחֻקֹּתַ֔י\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have commanded|צִוִּ֖יתִי\rb* \rb you|עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb I will tear|אֶקְרַ֤ע\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָה֙\rb* \rb away|קָרֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb from you|מֵֽעָלֶ֔יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and give it|וּנְתַתִּ֖יהָ\rb* \rb to your servant|לְעַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Nevertheless|אַךְ־\rb*, \rb for the sake|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֔נָּה\rb* \rb it during your lifetime|בְּיָמֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*; \rb I will tear it|אֶקְרָעֶֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb out of the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of your son|בִּנְךָ֖\rb*. \v 13 \rb Yet|רַ֤ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb tear the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָה֙\rb* \rb away from him|אֶקְרָ֔ע\rb*. \rb I will give|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb tribe|שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb to your son|לִבְנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb for the sake|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb of My servant|עַבְדִּ֔י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb and for the sake|וּלְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have chosen|בָּחָֽרְתִּי׃\rb*.”
\s1 Hadad’s Return
\p \v 14 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb raised up|וַיָּ֨קֶם\rb* \rb against Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb an adversary|שָׂטָן֙\rb*, \rb Hadad|הֲדַ֣ד\rb* \rb the Edomite|הָאֲדֹמִ֑י\rb*,\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb from the royal|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb line|מִזֶּ֧רַע\rb* \rb of Edom|בֶּאֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Earlier|וַיְהִ֗י\rb*, \rb when David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb was|בִּֽהְי֤וֹת\rb* \rb in Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb*, \rb Joab|יוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the army|הַצָּבָ֔א\rb* \rb had gone|בַּעֲל֗וֹת\rb* \rb to bury|לְקַבֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the dead|הַחֲלָלִ֑ים\rb* \rb and had struck down|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֖ר\rb* \rb in Edom|בֶּאֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb had stayed|יָֽשַׁב־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb six|שֵׁ֧שֶׁת\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁ֛ים\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he had killed|הִכְרִ֥ית\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male|זָכָ֖ר\rb* \rb in Edom|בֶּאֱדֽוֹם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb But Hadad|אֲדַ֡ד\rb*,\rb |הוּא֩\rb* \rb still just|וַאֲנָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb a young|קָטָֽן׃\rb* \rb boy|נַ֥עַר\rb*, \rb had fled|וַיִּבְרַ֣ח\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*,\rb |וַהֲדַ֖ד\rb* \rb along with|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb some Edomites|אֲדֹמִיִּ֜ים\rb* \rb who were servants|מֵעַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֛יו\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Hadad and his men set out|וַיָּקֻ֙מוּ֙\rb* \rb from Midian|מִמִּדְיָ֔ן\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Paran|פָּארָ֑ן\rb*. \rb They took|וַיִּקְחוּ֩\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb from Paran|מִפָּארָ֗ן\rb* \rb with them|עִמָּ֜ם\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb who gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb Hadad|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb a house|בַ֗יִת\rb*\rb |נָ֥תַן\rb*\rb |לֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb and land|וְאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb and provided|אָ֣מַר\rb* \rb him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb with food|וְלֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb There Hadad|הֲדַ֥ד\rb* \rb found|וַיִּמְצָא֙\rb* \rb such great|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֛ן\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb that he gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb to him|ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb in marriage|אִשָּׁה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sister|אֲח֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲח֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Queen|הַגְּבִירָֽה׃\rb* \rb Tahpenes|תַּחְפְּנֵ֥יס\rb*, \rb his own wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb*. \v 20 \rb And the sister|אֲח֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Tahpenes|תַּחְפְּנֵ֗יס\rb* \rb bore|וַתֵּ֨לֶד\rb* \rb Hadad|ל֜וֹ\rb* \rb a son|בְּנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb named Genubath|גְּנֻבַ֣ת\rb*. \rb Tahpenes herself|תַחְפְּנֵ֔ס\rb* \rb weaned him|וַתִּגְמְלֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb in|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and Genubath|גְנֻבַת֙\rb* \rb lived|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb there|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַרְעֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb When Hadad|וַהֲדַ֞ד\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb* \rb had rested|שָׁכַ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and that|וְכִי־\rb* \rb Joab|יוֹאָ֣ב\rb*, \rb the commander|שַֽׂר־\rb* \rb of the army|הַצָּבָ֑א\rb*, \rb was dead|מֵ֖ת\rb*, \rb he|הֲדַד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb*, “\rb Let me go|שַׁלְּחֵ֖נִי\rb*, \rb that I may return|וְאֵלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my own country|אַרְצִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb But Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֗ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb*, “\rb |כִּ֠י\rb* \rb What|מָה־\rb* \rb have you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb lacked|חָסֵר֙\rb* \rb here with me|עִמִּ֔י\rb* \rb that you suddenly|וְהִנְּךָ֥\rb* \rb want|מְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb to go back|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your own country|אַרְצֶ֑ךָ\rb*?”
\p “\rb Nothing|לֹ֔א\rb*,” \rb Hadad replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*, “\rb but|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb please let me go|שַׁלֵּ֖חַ\rb*\rb |תְּשַׁלְּחֵֽנִי׃\rb*.”
\s1 Rezon’s Hostility
\p \v 23 \rb And God|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb raised up|וַיָּ֨קֶם\rb* \rb against Solomon|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb another adversary|שָׂטָ֔ן\rb*, \rb Rezon|רְז֖וֹן\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Eliada|אֶלְיָדָ֑ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had fled|בָּרַ֗ח\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָֽיו׃\rb*, \rb Hadadezer|הֲדַדְעֶ֥זֶר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Zobah|צוֹבָ֖ה\rb*, \v 24 \rb and had gathered|וַיִּקְבֹּ֤ץ\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb to himself|עָלָיו֙\rb*. \rb When David|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb killed|בַּהֲרֹ֥ג\rb* \rb the Zobaites|אֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb Rezon captained|וַיְהִ֣י\rb*\rb |שַׂר־\rb* \rb a band of raiders|גְּד֔וּד\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּלְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb to Damascus|דַמֶּ֙שֶׂק֙\rb*, \rb where they settled|וַיֵּ֣שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb and gained control|וַֽיִּמְלְכ֖וּ\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Rezon was|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb Israel’s|לְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb enemy|שָׂטָ֤ן\rb* \rb throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb adding to|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the trouble|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb caused by|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Hadad|הֲדָ֑ד\rb*. \rb So Rezon ruled|וַיִּמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Aram|אֲרָֽם׃פ\rb* \rb with hostility|וַיָּ֙קָץ֙\rb* \rb toward Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*.
\s1 Jeroboam’s Rebellion
\p \v 26 \rb Now Jeroboam|וְיָרָבְעָם֩\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֨ט\rb* \rb was an Ephraimite|אֶפְרָתִ֜י\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Zeredah|הַצְּרֵדָ֗ה\rb* \rb whose mother|אִמּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb was a widow|אַלְמָנָ֔ה\rb* \rb named|וְשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb Zeruah|צְרוּעָה֙\rb*. \rb Jeroboam was a servant|עֶ֖בֶד\rb* \rb of Solomon|לִשְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb but he rebelled|וַיָּ֥רֶם\rb*\rb |יָ֖ד\rb* \rb against the king|בַּמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*, \v 27 \rb and this|וְזֶ֣ה\rb* \rb is the account|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of his rebellion|הֵרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |יָ֖ד\rb* \rb against the king|בַּמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb had built|בָּנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the supporting terraces|הַמִּלּ֔וֹא\rb*\f + \fr 11:27 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Millo\f* \rb and repaired|סָגַ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gap in the wall|פֶּ֕רֶץ\rb* \rb of the city|עִ֖יר\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb*. \v 28 \rb Now Jeroboam was|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb a mighty|גִּבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb man|וְהָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of valor|חָ֑יִל\rb*. \rb So when Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb noticed|וַיַּ֨רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the young man|הַנַּ֗עַר\rb* \rb was|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb industrious|מְלָאכָה֙\rb*\rb |עֹשֵׂ֤ה\rb*, \rb he put him in charge|וַיַּפְקֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb of the whole|לְכָל־\rb* \rb labor force|סֵ֖בֶל\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵֽף׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb During|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֜יא\rb* \rb Ahijah|אֲחִיָּה֩\rb* \rb the Shilonite|הַשִּׁילֹנִ֨י\rb* \rb met|וַיִּמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb Jeroboam|אֹת֡וֹ\rb* \rb on the road|בַּדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb as he|וְיָֽרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb was going out|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|מִירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Now Ahijah|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb had wrapped himself|מִתְכַּסֶּה֙\rb* \rb in a new|חֲדָשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb cloak|בְּשַׂלְמָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and the two|וּשְׁנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb of them were alone|לְבַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb in the open field|בַּשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb And Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb took hold|וַיִּתְפֹּ֣שׂ\rb* \rb of the new|הַחֲדָשָׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb cloak|בַּשַּׂלְמָ֥ה\rb* \rb he was wearing|עָלָ֑יו\rb*, \rb tore it|וַיִּ֨קְרָעֶ֔הָ\rb* \rb into twelve|שְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb pieces|קְרָעִֽים׃\rb*, \v 31 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to Jeroboam|לְיָֽרָבְעָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb Take|קַח־\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֣ה\rb* \rb pieces|קְרָעִ֑ים\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֖\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹה֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֨ר\rb*: ‘\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I will tear|קֹרֵ֤עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָה֙\rb* \rb out of the hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb and I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֥ה\rb* \rb tribes|הַשְּׁבָטִֽים׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb But one|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb tribe|וְהַשֵּׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb will remain|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb for the sake|לְמַ֣עַן׀\rb* \rb of My servant|עַבְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֗ד\rb* \rb and for the sake|וּלְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have chosen|בָּחַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb out of all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb For|יַ֣עַן׀\rb* \rb they have|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\f + \fr 11:33 \ft Hebrew; LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate \fqa he has\ft ; twice in this verse\f* \rb forsaken Me|עֲזָב֗וּנִי\rb* \rb to worship|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲווּ֮\rb* \rb Ashtoreth|לְעַשְׁתֹּרֶת֮\rb* \rb the goddess|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Sidonians|צִֽדֹנִין֒\rb*, \rb Chemosh|לִכְמוֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb the god|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Moabites|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and Milcom|וּלְמִלְכֹּ֖ם\rb* \rb the god|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb*. \rb They have not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb walked|הָלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb in My ways|בִדְרָכַ֗י\rb*, \rb nor done|לַעֲשׂ֨וֹת\rb* \rb what is right|הַיָּשָׁ֧ר\rb* \rb in My eyes|בְּעֵינַ֛י\rb*, \rb nor kept My statutes|וְחֻקֹּתַ֥י\rb* \rb and judgments|וּמִשְׁפָּטַ֖י\rb*, \rb as Solomon’s father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb David did|כְּדָוִ֥ד\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb Nevertheless, I will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb take|אֶקַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb out of Solomon’s hand|מִיָּד֑וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb I have made him|אֲשִׁתֶ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb ruler|נָשִׂ֣יא\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his life|חַיָּ֔יו\rb* \rb for the sake|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֤ד\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּי֙\rb*, \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I chose|בָּחַ֣רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he kept|שָׁמַ֖ר\rb* \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֥י\rb* \rb and statutes|וְחֻקֹּתָֽי׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb But I will take|וְלָקַחְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb tribes|הַשְּׁבָטִֽים׃\rb* \rb of the kingdom|הַמְּלוּכָ֖ה\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of his son|בְּנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and give them|וּנְתַתִּ֣יהָ\rb* \rb to you|לְּךָ֔\rb*.\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \v 36 \rb I will give|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb tribe|שֵֽׁבֶט־\rb* \rb to his son|וְלִבְנ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb My servant|עַ֠בְדִּי\rb* \rb David|לְדָֽוִיד־\rb* \rb will always|כָּֽל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֤ים׀\rb* \rb have|הֱיֽוֹת־\rb* \rb a lamp|נִ֣יר\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַי֙\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I chose|בָּחַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb to put|לָשׂ֥וּם\rb* \rb My Name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb But as for you|וְאֹתְךָ֣\rb*, \rb I will take you|אֶקַּ֔ח\rb*, \rb and you shall reign|וּמָ֣לַכְתָּ֔\rb* \rb over all|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your heart|נַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb desires|תְּאַוֶּ֖ה\rb*, \rb and you will be|וְהָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb king|מֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 38 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you listen to|תִּשְׁמַע֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I command you|אֲצַוֶּךָ֒\rb*, \rb walk|וְהָלַכְתָּ֣\rb* \rb in My ways|בִדְרָכַ֗י\rb*, \rb and do|וְעָשִׂ֨יתָ\rb* \rb what is right|הַיָּשָׁ֤ר\rb* \rb in My sight|בְּעֵינַי֙\rb* \rb in order to keep|לִשְׁמ֤וֹר\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקּוֹתַי֙\rb* \rb and commandments|וּמִצְוֺתַ֔י\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֑י\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*, \rb then I will be|וְהָיִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֗ךְ\rb*. \rb I will build|וּבָנִ֨יתִי\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֤\rb* \rb a lasting|נֶאֱמָן֙\rb* \rb dynasty|בַֽיִת־\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I built|בָּנִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb for David|לְדָוִ֔ד\rb*, \rb and I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*. \v 39 \rb Because|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb of this|זֹ֑את\rb*, \rb I will humble|וַֽאעַנֶּ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb David’s|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb descendants|זֶ֥רַע\rb* — \rb but|אַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb forever|כָל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃ס\rb*.’”
\p \v 40 \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb therefore sought|וַיְבַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb to kill|לְהָמִ֣ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֑ם\rb*. \rb But Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb arose|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and fled|וַיִּבְרַ֤ח\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shishak|שִׁישַׁ֣ק\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb where|בְמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb he remained|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the death|מ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Death of Solomon
\r (2 Chronicles 9:29–31)
\p \v 41 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֛ה\rb* — \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he did|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*, \rb as well as his wisdom|וְחָכְמָת֑וֹ\rb* — \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתֻבִ֔ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb of the Acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb*? \v 42 \rb Thus the time|וְהַיָּמִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֤ה\rb* \rb reigned|מָלַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb was forty|אַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb And Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּ֨קָּבֵ֔ר\rb* \rb in the city|בְּעִ֖יר\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*. \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃ס\rb*.
\c 12
\s1 Rebellion against Rehoboam
\r (2 Chronicles 10:1–15)
\p \v 1 \rb Then Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Shechem|שְׁכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb had gone|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb there|שְׁכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to make him king|לְהַמְלִ֥יךְ\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb When Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֗ט\rb* \rb heard about this|כִּשְׁמֹ֣עַ׀\rb*, \rb he was|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb still|עוֹדֶ֣נּוּ\rb*\f + \fr 12:2 \ft Or \fqa he remained\f* \rb in Egypt|בְמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had fled|בָּרַ֔ח\rb* \rb from King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb and had been|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb living ever since|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb*\rb |בְּמִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb So they sent for|וַֽיִּשְׁלְחוּ֙\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרְאוּ־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|ל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb and the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb assembly|קְהַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹאוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb and said|וַֽיְדַבְּר֔וּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 4 “\rb Your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb put a heavy|הִקְשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb yoke|עֻלֵּ֑נוּ\rb* \rb on us|אֶת־\rb*. \rb But now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb you|וְאַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb must lighten|הָקֵל֩\rb* \rb the burden|הַקָּשָׁ֗ה\rb* \rb of your father’s|אָבִ֜יךָ\rb* \rb service|מֵעֲבֹדַ֨ת\rb* \rb and the heavy|הַכָּבֵ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb yoke|וּמֵעֻלּ֧וֹ\rb* \rb he put|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb*, \rb and we will serve you|וְנַעַבְדֶֽךָּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Rehoboam answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go away|לְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb for|עֹ֛ד\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֥ה\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and then return|וְשׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*.” \rb So the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb consulted|וַיִּוָּעַ֞ץ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the elders|הַזְּקֵנִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb had served|עֹמְדִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb during|בִּֽהְיֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb his lifetime|חַ֖י\rb*. “\rb How|אֵ֚יךְ\rb* \rb do you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb advise me|נֽוֹעָצִ֔ים\rb* \rb to respond|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb to these|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people|הָֽעָם־\rb*?” \rb he asked|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb They replied|וַיְדַבֵּר\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you will be|תִּֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb a servant|עֶ֜בֶד\rb* \rb to these|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb people|לָעָ֤ם\rb* \rb and serve them|וַֽעֲבַדְתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb this day|הַ֠יּוֹם\rb*, \rb and if you will respond|וַעֲנִיתָ֕ם\rb* \rb by speaking|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb kind|טוֹבִ֑ים\rb* \rb words|דְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb they will be|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb your|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb servants|עֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb forever|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb But Rehoboam rejected|וַֽיַּעֲזֹ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the advice|עֲצַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |יְעָצֻ֑הוּ\rb*; \rb instead, he consulted|וַיִּוָּעַ֗ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the young men|הַיְלָדִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had grown up|גָּדְל֣וּ\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and served|הָעֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb He asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*, “\rb What|מָ֚ה\rb* \rb message|דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb do you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb advise|נֽוֹעָצִ֔ים\rb* \rb that we send back|וְנָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb to these|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb have spoken|דִּבְּר֤וּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Lighten|הָקֵל֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the yoke|הָעֹ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb put|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb on us|עָלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*’?”
\p \v 10 \rb The young men|הַיְלָדִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb had grown up|גָּדְל֣וּ\rb* \rb with him|אִתּוֹ֮\rb* \rb replied|וַיְדַבְּר֣וּ\rb*, “\rb This is how|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb you should answer|תֹאמַ֣ר\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֡ה\rb* \rb people|לָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb said|דִּבְּר֨וּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֜יךָ\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* ‘\rb Your father|אָבִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb made our yoke|עֻלֵּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb heavy|הִכְבִּ֣יד\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb but you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb must make it lighter|הָקֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |מֵעָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb*.’ \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb you should tell|תְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*: ‘\rb My little finger|קָֽטָנִּ֥י\rb* \rb is thicker|עָבָ֖ה\rb* \rb than my father’s|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb waist|מִמָּתְנֵ֥י\rb*! \v 11 \rb Whereas|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb my father|אָבִי֙\rb* \rb burdened|הֶעְמִ֤יס\rb* \rb you with a heavy|כָּבֵ֔ד\rb* \rb yoke|עֹ֣ל\rb*, \rb I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will add|אוֹסִ֣יף\rb*\rb |עַֽל־\rb* \rb to|עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb your yoke|עֻלְּכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Whereas my father|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb scourged|יִסַּ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb with whips|בַּשּׁוֹטִ֔ים\rb*, \rb I|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb will scourge|אֲיַסֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb with scorpions|בָּעַקְרַבִּֽים׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 12 \rb After three|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑י\rb* \rb days|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֧ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּבוֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb since|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb had said|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb*, “\rb Come back|שׁ֥וּבוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*.” \v 13 \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֧עַן\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb harshly|קָשָׁ֑ה\rb*. \rb He rejected|וַֽיַּעֲזֹ֛ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the advice|עֲצַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |יְעָצֻֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 14 \rb and spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb as the young men|הַיְלָדִים֙\rb* \rb had advised|כַּעֲצַ֤ת\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Whereas my father|אָבִי֙\rb* \rb made your yoke|עֻלְּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb heavy|הִכְבִּ֣יד\rb*,\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb will add|אֹסִ֣יף\rb* \rb to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb your yoke|עֻלְּכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Whereas my father|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb scourged|יִסַּ֤ר\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb with whips|בַּשּׁוֹטִ֔ים\rb*, \rb I|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb will scourge|אֲיַסֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb with scorpions|בָּעַקְרַבִּֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and indeed|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this turn of events|סִבָּה֙\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֣ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb to|לְמַ֜עַן\rb* \rb fulfill|הָקִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבָר֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb He|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָֽט׃\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the Shilonite|הַשִּׁילֹנִ֔י\rb*.
\s1 The Kingdom Divided
\r (2 Chronicles 10:16–19)
\p \v 16 \rb When all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֮\rb* \rb had refused|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to listen|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶם֒\rb*, \rb they|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|דָּבָ֣ר׀\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֡ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb portion|חֵ֨לֶק\rb* \rb do we have|לָּנוּ֩\rb* \rb in David|בְּדָוִ֜ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb and what|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb inheritance|נַחֲלָ֣ה\rb* \rb in the son|בְּבֶן־\rb* \rb of Jesse|יִשַׁ֗י\rb*?
\q1 \rb To your tents|לְאֹהָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*!
\q2 \rb Look|רְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb now|עַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb to your own house|בֵיתְךָ֖\rb*, \rb O David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*!”
\p \rb So the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb home|לְאֹהָלָֽיו׃\rb*, \v 17 \rb but Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָֽם׃פ\rb* \rb still reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb over|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb living|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb Adoram|אֲדֹרָם֙\rb*,\f + \fr 12:18 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts and Syriac \fqa Adoniram\ft ; see 1 Kings 4:6 and 1 Kings 5:14.\f* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was in charge|עַל־\rb* \rb of the forced labor|הַמַּ֔ס\rb*, \rb but all|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb stoned|וַיִּרְגְּמ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶ֖בֶן\rb* \rb him|בּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb to death|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb*. \rb And King|וְהַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb mounted|לַעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb his chariot|בַּמֶּרְכָּבָ֔ה\rb* \rb in haste|הִתְאַמֵּץ֙\rb* \rb and escaped|לָנ֖וּס\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb So to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb has been in rebellion|וַיִּפְשְׁע֤וּ\rb* \rb against the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*.
\s1 Shemaiah’s Prophecy
\r (2 Chronicles 11:1–4)
\p \v 20 \rb When all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb heard|כִּשְׁמֹ֤עַ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb had returned|שָׁ֣ב\rb*, \rb they summoned|וַֽיִּשְׁלְח֗וּ\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the assembly|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and made him king|וַיַּמְלִ֥יכוּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.\rb |הָיָה֙\rb* \rb Only|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |זוּלָתִ֥י\rb* \rb the tribe|שֵֽׁבֶט־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְבַדּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb followed|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb And when Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָם֮\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּבֹאוּ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַם֒\rb*, \rb he mobilized|וַיַּקְהֵל֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the tribe|שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֗ן\rb* — \rb 180,000|מֵאָ֨ה\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb* \rb chosen|בָּח֖וּר\rb*\rb |עֹשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb warriors|מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* — \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵם֙\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and restore|לְהָשִׁיב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמְּלוּכָ֔ה\rb* \rb to Rehoboam|לִרְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb But the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shemaiah|שְׁמַעְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 23 “\rb Tell|אֱמֹ֗ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֤ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹה֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Benjamin|וּבִנְיָמִ֑ין\rb*, \rb and the rest|וְיֶ֥תֶר\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 24 \rb that this is what|כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb You are not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to go up|תַעֲלוּ֩\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb and fight|תִלָּ֨חֲמ֜וּן\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb your brothers|אֲחֵיכֶ֣ם\rb*, \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*. \rb Each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of you must return|שׁ֚וּבוּ\rb* \rb home|לְבֵית֔וֹ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb is|נִהְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb My|מֵאִתִּ֛י\rb* \rb doing|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*.’”
\p \rb So they listened|וַיִּשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and turned back|וַיָּשֻׁ֥בוּ\rb*\rb |לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Jeroboam’s Idolatry
\p \v 25 \rb Then Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb built|וַיִּ֨בֶן\rb* \rb Shechem|שְׁכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and lived there|וַיֵּ֣שֶׁב\rb*. \rb And from|בָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb there|מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb he went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb and built|וַיִּ֖בֶן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Penuel|פְּנוּאֵֽל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 12:25 \fqa Penuel \ft is a variant of \fqa Peniel\ft ; see Genesis 32:30.\f*
\p \v 26 \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb in his heart|בְּלִבּ֑וֹ\rb*, “\rb Now|עַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb might revert|תָּשׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb If|אִֽם־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb go up|יַעֲלֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb to offer|לַעֲשׂ֨וֹת\rb* \rb sacrifices|זְבָחִ֤ים\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb at Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb their hearts|לֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |הָעָ֤ם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb will return|וְ֠שָׁב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their lord|אֲדֹ֣נֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*; \rb then they will kill me|וַהֲרָגֻ֕נִי\rb* \rb and return|וְשָׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 28 \rb After seeking advice|וַיִּוָּעַ֣ץ\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֕עַשׂ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb golden|זָהָ֑ב\rb* \rb calves|עֶגְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to the people|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb*,\f + \fr 12:28 \ft Hebrew \fqa to them\f* “\rb Going up|מֵעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb is too much|רַב־\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶם֙\rb*. \rb Here|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb are your gods|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb brought you up|הֶעֱל֖וּךָ\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 29 \rb One calf|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb he set up|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb in Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb the other|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb in Dan|בְּדָֽן׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb And this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb thing|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb became|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb a sin|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb*; \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb walked|וַיֵּלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb as far as|עַד־\rb* \rb Dan to worship|דָּֽן׃\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb one of the calves|הָאֶחָ֖ד\rb*.\f + \fr 12:30 \ft Likely reading of the original Hebrew text; MT \fqa the people walked to the one as far as Dan\ft ; LXX \fqa the people went to the one at Bethel and to the other as far as Dan\f*
\p \v 31 \rb Jeroboam also built|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shrines|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb on the high places|בָּמ֑וֹת\rb* \rb and appointed|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb from every class|מִקְצ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb priests|כֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were|הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb Levites|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |לֵוִֽי׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb And Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם׀\rb* \rb ordained|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb a feast|חָ֡ג\rb* \rb on the fifteenth|בַּחֲמִשָּֽׁה־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֩\rb* \rb day|י֨וֹם׀\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֜דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֣י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 12:32 \ft This feast was exactly one month after the annual Feast of Tabernacles in Judah; see Leviticus 23:34.\f* \rb like the feast|כֶּחָ֣ג׀\rb* \rb that was|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּיהוּדָ֗ה\rb*, \rb and he offered sacrifices|וַיַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*; \rb he made|עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb this|כֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb offering in Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to sacrifice|לְזַבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to the calves|לָעֲגָלִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had set up|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*, \rb and he installed|וְהֶעֱמִיד֙\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֥י\rb* \rb in Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the high places|הַבָּמ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had set up|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb*.
\p \v 33 \rb On the fifteenth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb day|יוֹם֙\rb* \rb of the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb a month|בַּחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of his own choosing|בָּדָ֣א\rb*\rb |מִלִּבַּד\rb*, \rb Jeroboam offered sacrifices|וַיַּ֜עַל\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֣חַ׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had set up|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb*\rb |בְּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb in Bethel|אֵ֗ל\rb*. \rb So he ordained|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a feast|חָג֙\rb* \rb for the Israelites|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb offered sacrifices|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*, \rb and burned incense|לְהַקְטִֽיר׃פ\rb*.
\c 13
\s1 Jeroboam’s Hand Withers
\r (2 Kings 23:4–20; 2 Chronicles 34:3–7)
\p \v 1 \rb Suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb as Jeroboam|וְיָרָבְעָ֛ם\rb* \rb was standing|עֹמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb to burn incense|לְהַקְטִֽיר׃\rb*, \rb there came|בָּ֧א\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb from Judah|מִיהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb by the word|בִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 2 \rb And he cried out|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb by the word|בִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, “\rb O altar|מִזְבֵּ֣חַ\rb*, \rb O altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*, \rb this is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*:\rb |הִנֵּֽה־\rb* ‘\rb A son|בֵ֞ן\rb* \rb named|שְׁמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb will be born|נוֹלָ֤ד\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִד֙\rb*, \rb and upon you|עָלֶ֗יךָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he will sacrifice|וְזָבַ֣ח\rb* \rb the priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the high places|הַבָּמוֹת֙\rb* \rb who burn incense|הַמַּקְטִרִ֣ים\rb* \rb upon you|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb and human|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb bones|וְעַצְמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb will be burned|יִשְׂרְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb upon you|עָלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.’”\f + \fr 13:2 \ft See 2 Kings 23:16.\f*
\p \v 3 \rb That|הַה֤וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb the man of God gave|וְנָתַן֩\rb* \rb a sign|מוֹפֵת֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb this|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb sign|הַמּוֹפֵ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*: ‘\rb Surely|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb will be split apart|נִקְרָ֔ע\rb*, \rb and the ashes|הַדֶּ֥שֶׁן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb upon it|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \rb will be poured out|וְנִשְׁפַּ֖ךְ\rb*.’”
\p \v 4 \rb Now when|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֧ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*, \rb who was at|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb in|בְּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֣ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb had cried out|קָרָ֤א\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb it|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*, \rb he stretched out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֛וֹ\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֣ר׀\rb*, “\rb Seize him|תִּפְשֻׂ֑הוּ\rb*!” \rb But the hand|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb he stretched out|שָׁלַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb toward him|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb withered|וַתִּיבַ֤שׁ\rb*, \rb so that he could|יָכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb pull it back|לַהֲשִׁיבָ֥הּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb And the altar|וְהַמִּזְבֵּ֣חַ\rb* \rb was split apart|נִקְרָ֔ע\rb*, \rb and the ashes|הַדֶּ֖שֶׁן\rb* \rb poured out|וַיִּשָּׁפֵ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*\rb |הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*, \rb according to the sign|כַּמּוֹפֵ֗ת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb had given|נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb by the word|בִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb* \rb responded|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb*, “\rb Intercede|חַל־\rb*\rb |נָ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with|פְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and pray|וְהִתְפַּלֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb for me|בַּעֲדִ֔י\rb* \rb that my hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb may be restored|וְתָשֹׁ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑י\rb*.”
\p \rb So the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb interceded|וַיְחַ֤ל\rb* \rb with|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and the king’s|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb hand|יַד־\rb* \rb was restored|וַתָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb as it was|וַתְּהִ֖י\rb* \rb before|כְּבָרִֽאשֹׁנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, “\rb Come|בֹּאָה־\rb* \rb home|הַבַּ֖יְתָה\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֥י\rb* \rb and refresh yourself|וּֽסְעָ֑דָה\rb*, \rb and I will give|וְאֶתְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb a reward|מַתָּֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb But the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you were to give|תִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb half|חֲצִ֣י\rb* \rb your possessions|בֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb I still would not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go|אָבֹ֖א\rb* \rb with you|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb nor|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb would I eat|אֹ֤כַל\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or drink|אֶשְׁתֶּה־\rb* \rb water|מַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֖וֹם\rb*. \v 9 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֵ֣ן׀\rb* \rb I was commanded|צִוָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb by the word|בִּדְבַ֤ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*: ‘\rb You must not|לֹא־\rb* \rb eat|תֹ֥אכַל\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֖חֶם\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or drink|תִשְׁתֶּה־\rb* \rb water|מָּ֑יִם\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or return|תָשׁ֔וּב\rb* \rb by the way|בַּדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you came|הָלָֽכְתָּ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 10 \rb So the man of God went|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb another|אַחֵ֑ר\rb* \rb way|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb return|שָׁ֣ב\rb* \rb by the way|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb he had come|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Old Prophet and the Man of God
\p \v 11 \rb Now a certain|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb old|זָקֵ֔ן\rb* \rb prophet|וְנָבִ֤יא\rb* \rb was living|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb*\rb |בְּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb in Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and his sons|בְנ֡וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 13:11 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa son\f* \rb came|וַיָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb and told|וַיְסַפֶּר־\rb* \rb him|ל֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the deeds|הַמַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֨ים׀\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂה֩\rb* \rb that day|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb in Bethel|אֵ֗ל\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb They also told|וַֽיְסַפְּר֖וּם\rb* \rb their father|לַאֲבִיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the man had spoken|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*.
\p \v 12 “\rb Which|אֵֽי־\rb*\rb |זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb way|הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb did he go|הָלָ֑ךְ\rb*?” \rb their father|אֲבִיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb asked|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb*.
\p \rb And his sons|בָנָ֗יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb showed him|וַיִּרְא֣וּ\rb*\f + \fr 13:12 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa had seen\f* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb taken|הָלַךְ֙\rb* \rb by the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had come|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb from Judah|מִיהוּדָֽה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb So the prophet said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Saddle|חִבְשׁוּ־\rb* \rb the donkey|הַחֲמ֑וֹר\rb* \rb for me|לִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \rb Then they saddled|וַיַּחְבְּשׁוּ־\rb* \rb the donkey|הַחֲמ֔וֹר\rb* \rb for him|ל֣וֹ\rb*, \rb and he mounted|וַיִּרְכַּ֖ב\rb* \rb it|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 14 \rb and went|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*. \rb He found him|וַיִּ֨מְצָאֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb sitting|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb an oak tree|הָאֵלָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 13:14 \ft Or \fqa a terebinth \ft or \fqa a great tree\f* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Are you|הַאַתָּ֧ה\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥אתָ\rb* \rb from Judah|מִֽיהוּדָ֖ה\rb*?”
\p “\rb I am|אָֽנִי׃\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb So the prophet said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to the man of God|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Come|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb home|הַבָּ֑יְתָה\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb and eat|וֶאֱכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb some bread|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb But the man replied|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I cannot|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אוּכַ֛ל\rb* \rb go home|לָשׁ֥וּב\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |וְלָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and I will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb eat|אֹ֣כַל\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֗חֶם\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb or drink|אֶשְׁתֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb water|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּךָ֙\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֖וֹם\rb*. \v 17 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb have been told|דָבָ֤ר\rb* \rb by the word|בִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*: ‘\rb You must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכַ֣ל\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֔חֶם\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb or drink|תִשְׁתֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb water|מָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb or return|תָשׁ֣וּב\rb*\rb |הָלַ֥כְתָּ\rb* \rb by the way|בַּדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you came|לָלֶ֔כֶת\rb*.’”
\p \v 18 \rb Then the prophet replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |ל֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb too am|גַּם־\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִיא֮\rb* \rb like you|כָּמוֹךָ֒\rb*, \rb and an angel|וּמַלְאָ֡ךְ\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֩\rb* \rb by the word|בִּדְבַ֨ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Bring him back|הֲשִׁבֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּךָ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your house|בֵּיתֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb so that he may eat|וְיֹ֥אכַל\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb and drink|וְיֵ֣שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb water|מָ֑יִם\rb*.’”
\p \rb The old prophet was lying|כִּחֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb to him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 19 \rb but the man of God went back|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb ate|וַיֹּ֥אכַל\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֛חֶם\rb* \rb in his house|בְּבֵית֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and drank|וַיֵּ֥שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb water|מָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb While they|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb were sitting|יֹשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֑ן פ\rb*,\rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had brought him back|הֱשִׁיבֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb and the prophet cried out|וַיִּקְרָ֞א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had come|בָּ֤א\rb* \rb from Judah|מִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*: ‘\rb Because|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you have defied|מָרִ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb the word|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and have not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb kept|שָׁמַ֙רְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandment|הַמִּצְוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb gave you|צִוְּךָ֖\rb*, \v 22 \rb but you went back|וַתָּ֗שָׁב\rb* \rb and ate|וַתֹּ֤אכַל\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb and drank|וַתֵּ֣שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb water|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb in the place|בַּמָּקוֹם֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He told|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb to do so|תֹּ֥אכַל\rb*\rb |לֶ֖חֶם\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb*\rb |תֵּ֣שְׁתְּ\rb*\rb |מָ֑יִם\rb*, \rb your body|נִבְלָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb shall never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb reach|תָב֥וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the tomb|קֶ֥בֶר\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 23 \rb And|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb the man of God had finished eating|אָכְל֥וֹ\rb*\rb |לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb and|וְאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb drinking|שְׁתוֹת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb the old prophet|לַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had brought him back|הֱשִׁיבֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb saddled|וַיַּחֲבָשׁ־\rb* \rb the donkey|הַחֲמ֔וֹר\rb* \rb for him|ל֣וֹ\rb*. \v 24 \rb As he went on his way|וַיֵּ֕לֶךְ\rb*, \rb a lion|אַרְיֵ֛ה\rb* \rb met him|וַיִּמְצָאֵ֧הוּ\rb* \rb on the road|בַּדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיְמִיתֵ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb and his body|נִבְלָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb left lying|מֻשְׁלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb in the road|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb*, \rb with the donkey|וְהַחֲמוֹר֙\rb*\rb |עֹמֵ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶצְלָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and the lion|וְהָ֣אַרְיֵ֔ה\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֥צֶל\rb* \rb it|הַנְּבֵלָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb And there were|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb passing by|עֹבְרִ֗ים\rb* \rb who saw|וַיִּרְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the body|הַנְּבֵלָה֙\rb* \rb lying|מֻשְׁלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb in the road|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lion|הָ֣אַרְיֵ֔ה\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb it|הַנְּבֵלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and they went|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb and reported this|וַיְדַבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb in the city|בָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the old|הַזָּקֵ֖ן\rb* \rb prophet|הַנָּבִ֥יא\rb* \rb lived|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb When the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֮\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had brought him back|הֱשִׁיב֣וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb his journey|הַדֶּרֶךְ֒\rb* \rb heard this|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb It is|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb disobeyed|מָרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the command|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Therefore the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb has delivered him|וַיִּתְּנֵ֨הוּ\rb* \rb to the lion|לָאַרְיֵ֗ה\rb*, \rb and it has mauled him|וַֽיִּשְׁבְּרֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיְמִתֵ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּר־\rb* \rb to him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 27 \rb Then the old prophet instructed|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָיו֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Saddle|חִבְשׁוּ־\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the donkey|הַחֲמ֑וֹר\rb* \rb for me|לִ֖י\rb*.” \rb So they saddled it|וַֽיַּחֲבֹֽשׁוּ׃\rb*, \v 28 \rb and he went|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb and found|וַיִּמְצָ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the body|נִבְלָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb lying|מֻשְׁלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb in the road|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb*, \rb with the donkey|וַֽחֲמוֹר֙\rb* \rb and the lion|וְהָ֣אַרְיֵ֔ה\rb* \rb standing|עֹמְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb it|הַנְּבֵלָ֑ה\rb*. \rb The lion|הָֽאַרְיֵה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb eaten|אָכַ֤ל\rb* \rb the body|הַנְּבֵלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or mauled|שָׁבַ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the donkey|הַחֲמֽוֹר׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb So the old prophet|הַנָּבִ֜יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lifted up|וַיִּשָּׂ֨א\rb* \rb the body|נִבְלַ֧ת\rb* \rb of the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*, \rb laid|וַיַּנִּחֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb it on|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the donkey|הַחֲמ֖וֹר\rb*, \rb and brought it back|וַיְשִׁיבֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb to his own|הַזָּקֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |הַנָּבִ֣יא\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb city|עִיר֙\rb* \rb to mourn for him|לִסְפֹּ֖ד\rb* \rb and bury him|וּלְקָבְרֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb Then he laid|וַיַּנַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the body|נִבְלָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in his own tomb|בְּקִבְר֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and they lamented|וַיִּסְפְּד֥וּ\rb* \rb over him|עָלָ֖יו\rb*, “\rb Oh|ה֥וֹי\rb*, \rb my brother|אָחִֽי׃\rb*!”
\p \v 31 \rb |וַיְהִי֮\rb* \rb After|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb he had buried him|קָבְר֣וֹ\rb*,\rb |אֹתוֹ֒\rb* \rb the prophet said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his sons|בָּנָיו֙\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb When I die|בְּמוֹתִי֙\rb*, \rb you must bury|וּקְבַרְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֔י\rb* \rb in the tomb|בַּקֶּ֕בֶר\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb is buried|קָב֣וּר\rb*. \rb Lay|הַנִּ֖יחוּ\rb* \rb my bones|עַצְמֹתָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֚צֶל\rb* \rb his bones|עַצְמֹתָֽי׃\rb*, \v 32 \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the message|הַדָּבָ֗ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb he cried out|קָרָא֙\rb* \rb by the word|בִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |בְּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb in Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and against|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the shrines|בָּתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb on the high places|הַבָּמ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃פ\rb* \rb will surely come to pass|הָיֹ֨ה\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֜ה\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb Even after|אַחַר֙\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb events|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*, \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb repent|שָׁ֥ב\rb* \rb of his evil|הָרָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb ways|מִדַּרְכּ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb but again|וַ֠יָּשָׁב\rb* \rb he appointed|וַיַּ֜עַשׂ\rb* \rb priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֣י\rb* \rb for the high places|בָמ֔וֹת\rb* \rb from every class|מִקְצ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of people|הָעָם֙\rb*. \rb He ordained|יְמַלֵּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb anyone who desired|הֶֽחָפֵץ֙\rb* \rb to be|וִיהִ֖י\rb* \rb a priest|כֹּהֲנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the high places|בָמֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb And this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִי֙\rb*\rb |בַּדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb the sin|לְחַטַּ֖את\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb that led to its extermination|וּלְהַכְחִיד֙\rb* \rb and destruction|וּלְהַשְׁמִ֔יד\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\c 14
\s1 Ahijah’s Prophecy against Jeroboam
\p \v 1 \rb At that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Abijah|אֲבִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָֽם׃\rb* \rb became ill|חָלָ֖ה\rb*, \v 2 \rb and Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֜ם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to his wife|לְאִשְׁתּ֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Now|נָא֙\rb* \rb get up|ק֤וּמִי\rb*, \rb disguise yourself|וְהִשְׁתַּנִּ֔ית\rb* \rb so they will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb recognize|יֵֽדְע֔וּ\rb* \rb you|אַתִּי\rb* \rb as my wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |יָרָבְעָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and go|וְהָלַ֣כְתְּ\rb* \rb to Shiloh|שִׁלֹ֗ה\rb*. \rb For|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb is there|שָׁם֙\rb*; \rb it was he|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb who spoke|דִבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb about my|עָלַ֛י\rb* \rb kingship|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֥ם\rb*. \v 3 \rb Take|וְלָקַ֣חַתְּ\rb* \rb with you|בְּ֠יָדֵךְ\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֨ה\rb* \rb loaves of bread|לֶ֧חֶם\rb*, \rb some cakes|וְנִקֻּדִ֛ים\rb*, \rb and a jar|וּבַקְבֻּ֥ק\rb* \rb of honey|דְּבַ֖שׁ\rb*, \rb and go|וּבָ֣את\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb He|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will tell|יַגִּ֣יד\rb* \rb you|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb will become|יִּֽהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb of the boy|לַנָּֽעַר׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb Jeroboam’s|יָרָבְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb did|וַתַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb as instructed|כֵּן֙\rb*; \rb she arose|וַתָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb and went|וַתֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Shiloh|שִׁלֹ֔ה\rb* \rb and arrived|וַתָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb at Ahijah’s|אֲחִיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb*. \rb Now Ahijah|וַאֲחִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb could|יָכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see|לִרְא֔וֹת\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb his eyes|עֵינָ֖יו\rb* \rb were dim|קָ֥מוּ\rb* \rb because of his age|מִשֵּׂיבֽוֹ׃ס\rb*. \v 5 \rb But the LORD|וַיהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb had said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֗הוּ\rb*, “\rb Behold|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb the wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֡ם\rb* \rb is coming|בָּאָ֣ה\rb* \rb to ask|לִדְרֹשׁ֩\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֨ר\rb* \rb you|מֵעִמְּךָ֤\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb her son|בְּנָהּ֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is ill|חֹלֶ֣ה\rb*. \rb You are to say|תְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb such|כָּזֹ֥ה\rb* \rb and such|וְכָזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֑יהָ\rb*, \rb because|וִיהִ֣י\rb* \rb when she arrives|כְבֹאָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb she|וְהִ֖יא\rb* \rb will be disguised|מִתְנַכֵּרָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb So|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb when Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֜הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb the sound|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of her feet|רַגְלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb entering|בָּאָ֣ה\rb* \rb the door|בַפֶּ֔תַח\rb*, \rb he said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Come in|בֹּ֖אִי\rb*, \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֑ם\rb*! \rb Why|לָ֣מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb are you|אַ֚תְּ\rb* \rb disguised|מִתְנַכֵּרָ֔ה\rb*? \rb For I|וְאָ֣נֹכִ֔י\rb* \rb have been sent|שָׁל֥וּחַ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלַ֖יִךְ\rb* \rb with bad news|קָשָֽׁה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Go|לְכִ֞י\rb*, \rb tell|אִמְרִ֣י\rb* \rb Jeroboam|לְיָרָבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֤ר\rb*:\rb |יַ֛עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* ‘\rb I raised you up|הֲרִימֹתִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from among|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb and appointed you|וָאֶתֶּנְךָ֣\rb* \rb ruler|נָגִ֔יד\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb I tore the kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָה֙\rb* \rb away|וָאֶקְרַ֤ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb* \rb and gave it|וָאֶתְּנֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb to you|לָ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb But you have not been|הָיִ֜יתָ\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb like My servant|כְּעַבְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֗ד\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb kept|שָׁמַ֨ר\rb* \rb My commandments|מִצְוֺתַ֜י\rb* \rb and|וַאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb followed Me|הָלַ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרַי֙\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֔וֹ\rb*, \rb doing|לַעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb* \rb only|רַ֖ק\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in My eyes|בְּעֵינָֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb You have done|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb more evil|וַתָּ֣רַע\rb* \rb than all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb You have proceeded|וַתֵּ֡לֶךְ\rb* \rb to make|וַתַּעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for yourself|לְּךָ֩\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֤ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֨ים\rb* \rb and molten images|וּמַסֵּכוֹת֙\rb* \rb to provoke|לְהַכְעִיסֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb Me|וְאֹתִ֥י\rb*, \rb and you have flung Me|הִשְׁלַ֖כְתָּ\rb* \rb behind|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb your back|גַוֶּֽךָ׃ס\rb*. \v 10 \rb Because of all this|לָכֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb behold|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I am bringing|מֵבִ֤יא\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָה֙\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֔ם\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb I will cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb from Jeroboam|לְיָֽרָבְעָם֙\rb* \rb every male|מַשְׁתִּ֣ין\rb*\rb |בְּקִ֔יר\rb*,\f + \fr 14:10 \ft Literally \fqa (all) those who urinate against a wall\f*
\q2 \rb both slave|עָצ֥וּר\rb* \rb and free|וְעָז֖וּב\rb*,
\q2 \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*;
\q1 \rb I will burn up|וּבִֽעַרְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb one burns up|יְבַעֵ֥ר\rb* \rb dung|הַגָּלָ֖ל\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb it is gone|תֻּמּֽוֹ׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 11 \rb Anyone belonging to Jeroboam|לְיָֽרָבְעָ֤ם\rb* \rb who dies|הַמֵּ֨ת\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִיר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb will be eaten|יֹאכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb by dogs|הַכְּלָבִ֔ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb and anyone who dies|וְהַמֵּת֙\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb will be eaten|יֹאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb by the birds|ע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb*.’
\qr \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֵּֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb As for you|וְאַ֥תְּ\rb*, \rb get up|ק֖וּמִי\rb* \rb and go|לְכִ֣י\rb* \rb home|לְבֵיתֵ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb When your feet|רַגְלַ֛יִךְ\rb* \rb enter|בְּבֹאָ֥ה\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖ירָה\rb*, \rb the child|הַיָּֽלֶד׃\rb* \rb will die|וּמֵ֥ת\rb*. \v 13 \rb All|כָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb will mourn|וְסָֽפְדוּ־\rb* \rb for him|ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb and bury|וְקָבְר֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֔וֹ\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this is|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the only one|לְבַדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb belonging to Jeroboam|לְיָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb who will receive a proper burial|יָבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |קָ֑בֶר\rb*,\f + \fr 14:13 \ft Literally \fqa who will come to the grave\f* \rb because|יַ֣עַן\rb* \rb only in him|ב֞וֹ\rb* \rb has the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb found|נִמְצָא־\rb* \rb any|דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb good|ט֗וֹב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Moreover , the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb will raise up|וְהֵקִים֩\rb* \rb for Himself|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb a king|מֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb will cut off|יַכְרִ֛ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb*. \rb This|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb is the day|הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* —\rb |וּמֶ֖ה\rb* \rb yes, even|גַּם־\rb* \rb today|עָֽתָּה׃\rb*! \v 15 \rb For the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will strike|וְהִכָּ֨ה\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb a reed|הַקָּנֶה֮\rb* \rb is shaken|יָנ֣וּד\rb* \rb in the water|בַּמַּיִם֒\rb*. \rb He will uproot|וְנָתַ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb from|מֵ֠עַל\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb good|הַטּוֹבָ֤ה\rb* \rb land|הָאֲדָמָ֨ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb He gave|נָתַן֙\rb* \rb their fathers|לַאֲב֣וֹתֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and He will scatter them|וְזֵרָ֖ם\rb* \rb beyond|מֵעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Euphrates|לַנָּהָ֑ר\rb*,\f + \fr 14:15 \ft Hebrew \fqa the River\f* \rb because|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they have made|עָשׂוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their Asherah poles|אֲשֵׁ֣רֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb provoking|מַכְעִיסִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD to anger|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb So He will give|וְיִתֵּ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel over|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb on account|בִּגְלַ֞ל\rb* \rb of the sins|חַטֹּ֤אות\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָֽרָבְעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has committed|חָטָ֔א\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and has caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to commit|הֶחֱטִ֖יא\rb*.”\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then Jeroboam’s|יָרָבְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb got up|וַתָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb and departed|וַתֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb for|וַתָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb Tirzah|תִרְצָ֑תָה\rb*, \rb and as soon as she|הִ֛יא\rb* \rb stepped over|בָּאָ֥ה\rb* \rb the threshold|בְסַף־\rb* \rb of the house|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*, \rb the boy|וְהַנַּ֥עַר\rb* \rb died|מֵֽת׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb And they buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb mourned|וַיִּסְפְּדוּ־\rb* \rb for him|ל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֤ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֔ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִֽיא׃\rb*.
\s1 Nadab Succeeds Jeroboam
\p \v 19 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָֽרָבְעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb how|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he waged war|נִלְחַ֖ם\rb* \rb and how|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he reigned|מָלָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb And the length|וְהַיָּמִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of Jeroboam’s|יָרָבְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb reign|מָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb was twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and he rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּב֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Nadab|נָדָ֥ב\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Rehoboam Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Chronicles 12:13–14)
\p \v 21 \rb Meanwhile, Rehoboam|וּרְחַבְעָם֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֔ה\rb* \rb reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He|רְחַבְעָ֨ם\rb* \rb was forty-one|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָה֩\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֜וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb seventeen|וּֽשֲׁבַ֨ע\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb*, \rb the city|הָ֠עִיר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb had chosen|בָּחַ֨ר\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb to put|לָשׂ֨וּם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His Name|שְׁמ֥וֹ\rb*\rb |שָׁם֙\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Naamah|נַעֲמָ֖ה\rb* \rb the Ammonite|הָעַמֹּנִֽית׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb And Judah|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and by the sins|בְּחַטֹּאתָ֖ם\rb* \rb they committed|חָטָֽאוּ׃\rb* \rb they provoked Him to jealous anger|וַיְקַנְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb more than all|מִכֹּל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb their fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb had done|עָשׂ֣וּ\rb*. \v 23 \rb They|הֵ֧מָּה\rb* \rb also|גַם־\rb* \rb built|וַיִּבְנ֨וּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb high places|בָּמ֥וֹת\rb*, \rb sacred pillars|וּמַצֵּב֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and Asherah poles|וַאֲשֵׁרִ֑ים\rb* \rb on|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb high|גְבֹהָ֔ה\rb* \rb hill|גִּבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb and under|וְתַ֖חַת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb green|רַעֲנָֽן׃\rb* \rb tree|עֵ֥ץ\rb*. \v 24 \rb There were|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb male shrine prostitutes|קָדֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb in the land|בָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb They imitated|עָשׂ֗וּ\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the abominations|הַתּוֹעֲבֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had driven out|הוֹרִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Shishak Raids Jerusalem
\r (2 Chronicles 12:1–12)
\p \v 25 \rb |וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb In the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁ֖ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Rehoboam’s|רְחַבְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb reign|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb Shishak|שׁוּשַׁק\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |עָלָ֛ה\rb* \rb attacked|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb He seized|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the treasures|אֹצְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֽוֹצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb*. \rb He took|לָקָ֑ח\rb* \rb everything|הַכֹּ֖ל\rb*, \rb including|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb* \rb shields|מָגִנֵּ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹֽה׃\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb Then King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָם֙\rb* \rb made|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb shields|מָגִנֵּ֖י\rb* \rb in their place|תַּחְתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and committed them|וְהִפְקִ֗יד\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the care|יַד֙\rb* \rb of the captains|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the guard|הָרָצִ֔ים\rb* \rb on duty|הַשֹּׁ֣מְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֥ית\rb*. \v 28 \rb And|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb whenever|מִדֵּי־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb entered|בֹ֥א\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb the guards|הָֽרָצִ֔ים\rb* \rb would bear the shields|יִשָּׂאוּם֙\rb*, \rb and later they would return them|וֶהֱשִׁיב֖וּם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the guardroom|הָרָצִֽים׃\rb*\rb |תָּ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he did|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*?
\p \v 30 \rb There was|הָיְתָ֧ה\rb* \rb war|וּמִלְחָמָ֨ה\rb* \rb between|בֵין־\rb* \rb Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb their days|הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb And Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֜ם\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֨ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb them|אֲבֹתָיו֙\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*; \rb his mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Naamah|נַעֲמָ֖ה\rb* \rb the Ammonite|הָעַמֹּנִ֑ית\rb*. \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Abijam|אֲבִיָּ֥ם\rb*\f + \fr 14:31 \fqa Abijam \ft is a variant of \fqa Abijah\ft ; some Hebrew manuscripts and LXX \fqa Abijah\ft ; see 2 Chronicles 12:16.\f* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\c 15
\s1 Abijam Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Chronicles 13:1–3)
\p \v 1 \rb In the eighteenth|שְׁמֹנֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֔ה\rb* \rb year|וּבִשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of the reign|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֑ט\rb*, \rb Abijam|אֲבִיָּ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 15:1 \fqa Abijam \ft is a variant of \fqa Abijah\ft ; some Hebrew manuscripts and LXX \fqa Abijah\ft ; also in verses 3, 6, 7, and 8; see 2 Chronicles 12:16.\f* \rb became king|מָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Maacah|מַעֲכָ֖ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Abishalom|אֲבִישָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 15:2 \fqa Abishalom \ft is a variant of \fqa Absalom\ft ; also in verse 10; see 2 Chronicles 11:20.\f*
\p \v 3 \rb And Abijam walked|וַיֵּ֕לֶךְ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the sins|חַטֹּ֥אות\rb* \rb that his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb had committed|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb*, \rb and his heart|לְבָב֤וֹ\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb as fully devoted|שָׁלֵם֙\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֔יו\rb* \rb as the heart|כִּלְבַ֖ב\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb* \rb his forefather had been|אָבִֽיו׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Nevertheless|כִּ֚י\rb*, \rb for the sake|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֔ד\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb his God|אֱלֹהָ֥יו\rb* \rb gave|נָתַן֩\rb* \rb him|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb a lamp|נִ֖יר\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb by raising up|לְהָקִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a son|בְּנוֹ֙\rb* \rb to succeed him|אַחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb and to make|וּֽלְהַעֲמִ֖יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jerusalem strong|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb For|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and had not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb turned aside|סָ֞ר\rb* \rb from anything|מִכֹּ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD commanded|צִוָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his life|חַיָּ֔יו\rb*, \rb except|רַ֕ק\rb* \rb in the matter|בִּדְבַ֖ר\rb* \rb of Uriah|אוּרִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Hittite|הַחִתִּֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb And there was|הָיְתָ֧ה\rb* \rb war|וּמִלְחָמָ֨ה\rb* \rb between|בֵין־\rb* \rb the houses of Rehoboam|רְחַבְעָ֛ם\rb*\f + \fr 15:6 \ft Literally \fqa war between Rehoboam \ft (most Hebrew manuscripts); some Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac \fqa war between Abijam \ft (that is, Abijah); most LXX texts do not contain this verse.\f*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Abijam’s life|חַיָּֽיו׃\rb*.\f + \fr 15:6 \ft Literally \fqa of his life\f*
\p \v 7 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Abijam|אֲבִיָּם֙\rb*, \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*? \rb And there was|הָיְתָ֛ה\rb* \rb war|וּמִלְחָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Abijam|אֲבִיָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And Abijam|אֲבִיָּם֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*, \rb and his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֥א\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Asa Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Chronicles 14:1–15; 2 Chronicles 15:8–19)
\p \v 9 \rb In the twentieth|עֶשְׂרִ֔ים\rb* \rb year|וּבִשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Jeroboam’s|לְיָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb Asa|אָסָ֖א\rb* \rb became king|מָלַ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb forty-one|וְאַרְבָּעִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַת֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb His grandmother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb*\f + \fr 15:10 \ft Or \fqa The queen mother’s\ft ; Hebrew \fqa His mother’s\ft ; see verses 2 and 13.\f* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Maacah|מַעֲכָ֖ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Abishalom|אֲבִישָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb And Asa|אָסָ֛א\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb as his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb David had done|כְּדָוִ֖ד\rb*. \v 12 \rb He banished|וַיַּעֲבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb the male shrine prostitutes|הַקְּדֵשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and removed|וַיָּ֙סַר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the idols|הַגִּלֻּלִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb had made|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb*. \v 13 \rb He also|וְגַ֣ם׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb removed|וַיְסִרֶ֙הָ֙\rb* \rb his grandmother|אִמּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Maacah|מַעֲכָ֣ה\rb* \rb from her position as queen mother|מִגְּבִירָ֔ה\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb she had made|עָשְׂתָ֥ה\rb* \rb a detestable|מִפְלֶ֖צֶת\rb* \rb Asherah pole|לָאֲשֵׁרָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Asa|אָסָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb chopped down|וַיִּכְרֹ֤ת\rb* \rb the pole|מִפְלַצְתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb and burned|וַיִּשְׂרֹ֖ף\rb* \rb it in the Kidron|קִדְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb Valley|בְּנַ֥חַל\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb The high places|וְהַבָּמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb were not|לֹא־\rb* \rb removed|סָ֑רוּ\rb*, \rb but|רַ֣ק\rb* \rb Asa’s|אָסָ֗א\rb* \rb heart|לְבַב־\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb fully devoted|שָׁלֵ֛ם\rb* \rb to|עִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his days|יָמָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And he brought|וַיָּבֵא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb the silver|כֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֖ב\rb* \rb and the articles|וְכֵלִֽים׃\rb* \rb that he|וְקָדְשׁוֹ\rb* \rb and his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb had dedicated|קָדְשֵׁ֣י\rb*.
\s1 War between Asa and Baasha
\r (2 Chronicles 16:1–6)
\p \v 16 \rb Now there was|הָיְתָ֜ה\rb* \rb war|וּמִלְחָמָ֨ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֗א\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֛ין\rb* \rb and Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֥א\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb their days|יְמֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֤א\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb went to war|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and fortified|וַיִּ֖בֶן\rb* \rb Ramah|הָרָמָ֑ה\rb*\rb |לְבִלְתִּ֗י\rb* \rb to prevent|תֵּ֚ת\rb* \rb anyone from leaving|יֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb or entering the territory of|וָבָ֔א\rb* \rb Asa|לְאָסָ֖א\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb So Asa|אָ֠סָא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb withdrew|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֨סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְהַזָּהָ֜ב\rb* \rb that remained|הַֽנּוֹתָרִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb in the treasuries|בְּאוֹצְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֽוֹצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb the royal|מֶלֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb*. \rb He entrusted it|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּיַד־\rb* \rb to his servants|עֲבָדָ֑יו\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אָסָ֗א\rb* \rb and sent them|וַיִּשְׁלָחֵ֞ם\rb* \rb with this message|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲ֠דַד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Tabrimmon|טַבְרִמֹּ֤ן\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hezion|חֶזְיוֹן֙\rb*, \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb*, \rb who was ruling|הַיֹּשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in Damascus|בְּדַמֶּ֖שֶׂק\rb*: \v 19 “\rb Let there be a treaty|בְּרִית֙\rb*\f + \fr 15:19 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft ; twice in this verse.\f* \rb between me and you|בֵּינִ֣י\rb* \rb as there was between|וּבֵינֶ֔ךָ\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb my father|אָבִ֖י\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and your father|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb See|הִנֵּה֩\rb*, \rb I have sent|שָׁלַ֨חְתִּֽי\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb a gift|שֹׁ֙חַד֙\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֔ב\rb*. \rb Now go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and break|הָפֵ֗רָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your treaty|בְּרִֽיתְךָ֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֣א\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb so that he will withdraw|וְיַעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from me|מֵעָלָֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb And Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֜ד\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֨ע\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֗א\rb* \rb and sent|וַ֠יִּשְׁלַח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of his armies|הַחֲיָלִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb conquering|וַיַּךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ijon|עִיּ֣וֹן\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Dan|דָּ֔ן\rb*,\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |אָבֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Abel-beth-maacah|מַעֲכָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִֽי׃\rb*, \rb including|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the region|כָּל־\rb* \rb of Chinnereth|כִּנְר֔וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb When|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֔א\rb* \rb learned of this|כִּשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb*, \rb he stopped|וַיֶּחְדַּ֕ל\rb* \rb fortifying|מִבְּנ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ramah|הָֽרָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and withdrew|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb to Tirzah|בְּתִרְצָֽה׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb Then King|וְהַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֜א\rb* \rb summoned|הִשְׁמִ֤יעַ\rb* \rb all the men|כָּל־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*,\f + \fr 15:22 \ft Or \fqa Then King Asa made a proclamation throughout all Judah\f* \rb with no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb exceptions|נָקִ֔י\rb*, \rb and they carried away|וַיִּשְׂא֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the stones|אַבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Ramah|הָֽרָמָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the timbers|עֵצֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֑א\rb* \rb had used for building|בָּנָ֖ה\rb*. \rb And with these materials|בָּם֙\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֔א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb built up|וַיִּ֤בֶן\rb* \rb Geba|גֶּ֥בַע\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֖ן\rb*, \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Jehoshaphat Succeeds Asa
\r (2 Chronicles 17:1–19)
\p \v 23 \rb Now the rest|וְיֶ֣תֶר\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Asa|אָ֠סָא\rb*, \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his might|גְּב֨וּרָת֜וֹ\rb*, \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֗ה\rb*, \rb and the cities|וְהֶֽעָרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he built|בָּנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹֽא־\rb* \rb written|כְתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*?\rb |לְעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb In his old age|זִקְנָת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb however|רַ֚ק\rb*, \rb he became diseased|חָלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in his feet|רַגְלָֽיו׃\rb*.
