\p \v 29 \rb As soon as|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb Baasha became king|כְמָלְכ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb he struck down|הִכָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֔ם\rb*. \rb He did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb leave|הִשְׁאִ֧יר\rb* \rb to Jeroboam|לְיָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb anyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb who breathed|נְשָׁמָ֛ה\rb*, \rb but destroyed them all|הִשְׁמִד֑וֹ\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֔ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Shilonite|הַשִּׁילֹנִֽי׃\rb*, \v 30 \rb because|עַל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of the sins|חַטֹּ֤אות\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָם֙\rb* \rb had committed|חָטָ֔א\rb* \rb and|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb to commit|הֶחֱטִ֖יא\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and because he had provoked|הִכְעִ֔יס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \rb to anger|בְּכַעְס֕וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*.
