\s1 Jehu’s Prophecy against Baasha
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵה֣וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Hanani|חֲנָ֔נִי\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֖א\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 2 “\rb Even|יַ֗עַן\rb* \rb though|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I lifted you|הֲרִימֹתִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb out|מִן־\rb* \rb of the dust|הֶ֣עָפָ֔ר\rb* \rb and made|וָאֶתֶּנְךָ֣\rb* \rb you ruler|נָגִ֔יד\rb* \rb over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb you have walked|וַתֵּ֣לֶךְ׀\rb* \rb in the way|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb and have caused My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to sin|וַֽתַּחֲטִא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and to provoke Me to anger|לְהַכְעִיסֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb by their sins|בְּחַטֹּאתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb So now|הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb I will consume|מַבְעִ֛יר\rb* \rb Baasha|בַעְשָׁ֖א\rb* \rb and his house|בֵית֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and I will make|וְנָֽתַתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your house|בֵּ֣יתְךָ֔\rb* \rb like that|כְּבֵ֖ית\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָֽט׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Anyone belonging to Baasha|לְבַעְשָׁא֙\rb* \rb who dies|הַמֵּ֤ת\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֔יר\rb*
