\q1 \rb and anyone who dies|וְהַמֵּ֥ת\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb will be eaten|יֹאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb by the birds|ע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Baasha|בַעְשָׁ֛א\rb*, \rb along with his accomplishments|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb and might|וּגְבֽוּרָת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*? \v 6 \rb And Baasha|בַּעְשָׁא֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in Tirzah|בְּתִרְצָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Elah|אֵלָ֥ה\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*.
