\s1 Elah Reigns in Israel
\p \v 8 \rb In the twenty-sixth|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וָשֵׁשׁ֙\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Asa’s|לְאָסָ֖א\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb Elah|אֵלָ֨ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֧א\rb* \rb became king|מָ֠לַךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*, \rb and he reigned in Tirzah|בְּתִרְצָ֖ה\rb* \rb two years|שְׁנָתָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb However, while Elah|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb was in Tirzah|בְתִרְצָה֙\rb* \rb getting drunk|שֹׁתֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |שִׁכּ֔וֹר\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Arza|אַרְצָ֔א\rb* \rb the steward|עַל־\rb* \rb of his household|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb there|בְּתִרְצָֽה׃\rb*, \rb Elah’s servant|עַבְדּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Zimri|זִמְרִ֔י\rb*, \rb the commander|שַׂ֖ר\rb* \rb of half|מַחֲצִ֣ית\rb* \rb his chariots|הָרָ֑כֶב\rb*, \rb conspired|וַיִּקְשֹׁ֤ר\rb* \rb against him|עָלָיו֙\rb*. \v 10 \rb So in the twenty-seventh|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וָשֶׁ֔בַע\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of Asa’s|לְאָסָ֖א\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb Zimri|זִמְרִי֙\rb* \rb went in|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb*, \rb struck Elah down|וַיַּכֵּ֣הוּ\rb*, \rb and killed him|וַיְמִיתֵ֔הוּ\rb*. \rb And Zimri reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb As soon as|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb Zimri began to reign|בְמָלְכ֜וֹ\rb* \rb and was seated|כְּשִׁבְתּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסְא֗וֹ\rb*, \rb he struck down|הִכָּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֔א\rb*. \rb He did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb leave|הִשְׁאִ֥יר\rb* \rb a single male|מַשְׁתִּ֣ין\rb*\rb |בְּקִ֑יר\rb*, \rb whether a kinsman|וְגֹאֲלָ֖יו\rb* \rb or friend|וְרֵעֵֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb So Zimri|זִמְרִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb destroyed|וַיַּשְׁמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֑א\rb*, \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֤ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֔א\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵה֥וּא\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִֽיא׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb This happened because of|אֶ֚ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the sins|חַטֹּ֣אות\rb* \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֔א\rb* \rb and|וְחַטֹּ֖אות\rb* \rb his son|בְנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Elah|אֵלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had committed|חָטְא֗וּ\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb and had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to commit|הֶחֱטִ֙יאוּ֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb provoking|לְהַכְעִ֗יס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel, to anger|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb with their worthless idols|בְּהַבְלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Elah|אֵלָ֖ה\rb*, \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*?
\s1 Zimri Reigns in Israel
\p \v 15 \rb In the twenty-seventh|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וָשֶׁ֜בַע\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֩\rb* \rb of Asa’s|לְאָסָא֙\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Zimri|זִמְרִ֛י\rb* \rb reigned|מָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in Tirzah|בְּתִרְצָ֑ה\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb*. \rb Now the troops|וְהָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb were encamped|חֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb against|עַֽל־\rb* \rb Gibbethon|גִּבְּת֖וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb of the Philistines|לַפְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb and the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb in the camp|הַחֹנִ֣ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb that Zimri|זִמְרִ֔י\rb* \rb had conspired|קָשַׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb and|וְגַ֖ם\rb* \rb struck him down|הִכָּ֣ה\rb*. \rb So there in the camp|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb* \rb that very|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*, \rb all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb proclaimed Omri|עָמְרִ֨י\rb*, \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of the army|צָבָ֧א\rb*, \rb king|וַיַּמְלִ֣כוּ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Then Omri|עָמְרִ֛י\rb* \rb and|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb marched up|וַיַּעֲלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb from Gibbethon|מִֽגִּבְּת֑וֹן\rb* \rb and besieged|וַיָּצֻ֖רוּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Tirzah|תִּרְצָֽה׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb When Zimri|זִמְרִי֙\rb* \rb saw|כִּרְא֤וֹת\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb was captured|נִלְכְּדָ֣ה\rb*, \rb he entered|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the citadel|אַרְמ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |מֶ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb and burned it down|וַיִּשְׂרֹ֨ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb upon himself|עָלָ֧יו\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb So he died|וַיָּמֹֽת׃\rb* \v 19 \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb the sins|חַטָּאתוֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had committed|חָטָ֔א\rb*, \rb doing|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and following|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb* \rb the example|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and the sin|וּבְחַטָּאתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had committed|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb and had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to commit|לְהַחֲטִ֖יא\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zimri|זִמְרִ֔י\rb* \rb and the treason|וְקִשְׁר֖וֹ\rb* \rb he committed|קָשָׁ֑ר\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹֽא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*?
\s1 Omri Reigns in Israel
\p \v 21 \rb At that time|אָ֧ז\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb were divided|יֵחָלֵ֛ק\rb*: \rb Half|לַחֵ֑צִי\rb*\rb |חֲצִ֨י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb supported|הָ֠יָה\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb Tibni|תִבְנִ֤י\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ginath|גִּינַת֙\rb* \rb as king|לְהַמְלִיכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and half|וְהַחֲצִ֖י\rb* \rb supported|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Omri|עָמְרִֽי׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb But the followers|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Omri|עָמְרִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb proved stronger|וַיֶּחֱזַ֤ק\rb* \rb than those|הָעָ֕ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Tibni|תִּבְנִ֣י\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ginath|גִּינַ֑ת\rb*. \rb So Tibni|תִּבְנִ֔י\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb and Omri|עָמְרִֽי׃פ\rb* \rb became king|וַיִּמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb In the thirty-first|שְׁלֹשִׁ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֜ת\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֩\rb* \rb of Asa’s|לְאָסָא֙\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Omri|עָמְרִי֙\rb* \rb became king|מָלַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and he reigned twelve|שְׁתֵּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |מָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb of them|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \rb in Tirzah|בְּתִרְצָ֖ה\rb*. \v 24 \rb He bought|וַיִּ֜קֶן\rb* \rb the hill|הָהָ֥ר\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְר֛וֹן\rb* \rb from|מֵ֥אֶת\rb* \rb Shemer|שֶׁ֖מֶר\rb* \rb for two talents|בְּכִכְּרַ֣יִם\rb* \rb of silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 16:24 \fqa 2 talents \ft is approximately 151 pounds or 68.4 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb and built a city|וַיִּ֙בֶן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb there|הָהָ֔ר\rb*, \rb calling|וַיִּקְרָ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb it|הָעִיר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |בָּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb Samaria|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb after|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the name|שֶׁם־\rb* \rb of Shemer|שֶׁ֔מֶר\rb*, \rb who had owned|אֲדֹנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the hill|הָהָ֥ר\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb But Omri|עָמְרִ֛י\rb* \rb did|וַיַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and acted more wickedly|וַיָּ֕רַע\rb* \rb than all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb For he walked|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the ways|דֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֔ט\rb* \rb and in his sins|וּבְחַטֹּאתָיו\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb to commit|הֶחֱטִ֖יא\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb provoking|לְהַכְעִ֗יס\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb to anger|אֶת־\rb* \rb with their worthless idols|בְּהַבְלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Omri|עָמְרִי֙\rb*, \rb along with his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb and the might|וּגְבוּרָת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he exercised|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹֽא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*?
\p \v 28 \rb And Omri|עָמְרִי֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֥ב\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Ahab Reigns in Israel, Marries Jezebel
\p \v 29 \rb In the thirty-eighth|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנֶה֙\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Asa’s|לְאָסָ֖א\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb Ahab|וְאַחְאָ֣ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Omri|עָמְרִ֗י\rb* \rb became king|מָלַךְ֙\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*,\rb |אַחְאָ֨ב\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |עָמְרִ֤י\rb* \rb and he reigned|וַ֠יִּמְלֹךְ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb However, Ahab|אַחְאָ֧ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Omri|עָמְרִ֛י\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb more than all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were before him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb And as if it were|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb not enough|הֲנָקֵ֣ל\rb* \rb for him to walk|לֶכְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb in the sins|בְּחַטֹּ֖אות\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֑ט\rb*, \rb he even married|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jezebel|אִיזֶ֗בֶל\rb* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Ethbaal|אֶתְבַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Sidonians|צִידֹנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and he then proceeded|וַיֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb to serve|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb and worship|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb Baal|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb First, Ahab set up|וַיָּ֥קֶם\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb for Baal|לַבָּ֑עַל\rb* \rb in the temple|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had built|בָּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 33 \rb Then he|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb set up|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb an Asherah pole|הָאֲשֵׁרָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Thus Ahab|אַחְאָ֜ב\rb* \rb did|לַעֲשׂ֗וֹת\rb* \rb more|וַיּ֨וֹסֶף\rb* \rb to provoke|לְהַכְעִיס֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהֹוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel, to anger|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb than all|מִכֹּ֨ל\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb In Ahab’s days|בְּיָמָ֞יו\rb*, \rb Hiel|חִיאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb the Bethelite|הָאֱלִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb rebuilt|בָּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb Jericho|יְרִיחֹ֑ה\rb*. \rb At the cost of Abiram|בַּאֲבִירָ֨ם\rb* \rb his firstborn|בְּכֹר֜וֹ\rb* \rb he laid its foundation|יִסְּדָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb and at the cost of Segub|וּבִשְׂגִיב\rb* \rb his youngest|צְעִירוֹ֙\rb* \rb he set up|הִצִּ֣יב\rb* \rb its gates|דְּלָתֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֔ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun|נֽוּן׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 16:34 \ft See Joshua 6:26.\f*
\c 17
\s1 The Ravens Feed Elijah
\p \v 1 \rb Now Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb the Tishbite|הַתִּשְׁבִּ֜י\rb*, \rb who was among the settlers|מִתֹּשָׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gilead|גִלְעָד֮\rb*,\f + \fr 17:1 \ft Or \fqa who was from Tishbe in Gilead\f* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָב֒\rb*, “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֞ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb lives|חַי־\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb before whom|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb* \rb I stand|עָמַ֣דְתִּי\rb*, \rb there will be|יִהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb neither|אִם־\rb* \rb dew|טַ֣ל\rb* \rb nor rain|וּמָטָ֑ר\rb* \rb in these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb years|הַשָּׁנִ֥ים\rb* \rb except|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb at|לְפִ֥י\rb* \rb my word|דְבָרִֽי׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 2 \rb Then a revelation|דְבַר־\rb* \rb from the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to Elijah|אֵלָ֥יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 3 “\rb Leave|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb here|מִזֶּ֔ה\rb*, \rb turn|וּפָנִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb eastward|קֵ֑דְמָה\rb*, \rb and hide yourself|וְנִסְתַּרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb by the Brook|בְּנַ֣חַל\rb* \rb of Cherith|כְּרִ֔ית\rb*, \rb east of|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*.\f + \fr 17:3 \ft Or \fqa the Cherith Ravine, near the Jordan\ft ; also in verse 5\f* \v 4 \rb And|וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb you are to drink|תִּשְׁתֶּ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb from the brook|מֵהַנַּ֣חַל\rb*, \rb and I have commanded|צִוִּ֔יתִי\rb* \rb the ravens|הָעֹרְבִ֣ים\rb* \rb to feed you|לְכַלְכֶּלְךָ֖\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb So Elijah did|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb* \rb what the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb had told him|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb*, \rb and he went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and lived|וַיֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb by the Brook|בְּנַ֣חַל\rb* \rb of Cherith|כְּרִ֔ית\rb*, \rb east of|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb The ravens|וְהָעֹרְבִ֗ים\rb* \rb would bring|מְבִיאִ֨ים\rb* \rb him|ל֜וֹ\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb and meat|וּבָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*\rb |וְלֶ֥חֶם\rb*\rb |וּבָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb and evening|בָּעָ֑רֶב\rb*, \rb and he would drink|יִשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb the brook|הַנַּ֖חַל\rb*. \v 7 \rb Some time later, however|וַיְהִ֛י\rb*\rb |מִקֵּ֥ץ\rb*\rb |יָמִ֖ים\rb*, \rb the brook|הַנָּ֑חַל\rb* \rb dried up|וַיִּיבַ֣שׁ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb there had been|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb rain|גֶ֖שֶׁם\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Widow of Zarephath
\p \v 8 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to Elijah|אֵלָ֥יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 9 “\rb Get up|ק֣וּם\rb* \rb and go|לֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb to Zarephath|צָרְפַ֙תָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of Sidon|לְצִיד֔וֹן\rb*, \rb and stay|וְיָשַׁבְתָּ֖\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*. \rb Behold|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I have commanded|צִוִּ֥יתִי\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb a widow|אַלְמָנָ֖ה\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb to provide for you|לְכַלְכְּלֶֽךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb So Elijah got up|וַיָּ֣קָם׀\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Zarephath|צָרְפַ֗תָה\rb*. \rb When he arrived|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb gate|פֶּ֣תַח\rb*, \rb there|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb was a widow|אַלְמָנָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb gathering|מְקֹשֶׁ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb sticks|עֵצִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Elijah called|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֨א\rb* \rb bring|קְחִי־\rb* \rb me|לִ֧י\rb* \rb a little|מְעַט־\rb* \rb water|מַ֛יִם\rb* \rb in a cup|בַּכְּלִ֖י\rb*, \rb so that I may drink|וְאֶשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb*.” \v 11 \rb And as she was going|וַתֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to get it|לָקַ֑חַת\rb*, \rb he called|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb bring|לִֽקְחִי־\rb* \rb me|לִ֛י\rb* \rb a piece|פַּת־\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֖חֶם\rb*\rb |בְּיָדֵֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb But she replied|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb I|לִ֣י\rb* \rb have|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb no|אִם־\rb* \rb bread|מָע֔וֹג\rb*— \rb only|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb a handful|מְלֹ֤א\rb*\rb |כַף־\rb* \rb of flour|קֶ֙מַח֙\rb* \rb in a jar|בַּכַּ֔ד\rb* \rb and a little|וּמְעַט־\rb* \rb oil|שֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb in a jug|בַּצַּפָּ֑חַת\rb*. \rb Look|וְהִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I am gathering|מְקֹשֶׁ֜שֶׁת\rb* \rb a couple of|שְׁנַ֣יִם\rb* \rb sticks|עֵצִ֗ים\rb* \rb to take home|וּבָ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb and prepare a meal|וַעֲשִׂיתִ֙יהוּ֙\rb* \rb for myself|לִ֣י\rb* \rb and my son|וְלִבְנִ֔י\rb*, \rb so that we may eat it|וַאֲכַלְנֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and die|וָמָֽתְנוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 13 “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּ֣ירְאִ֔י\rb*,” \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֤יהָ\rb*. “\rb Go|בֹּ֖אִי\rb* \rb and do|עֲשִׂ֣י\rb* \rb as you have said|כִדְבָרֵ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb But|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb first|בָרִאשֹׁנָה֙\rb* \rb make|עֲשִׂי־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb a small|קְטַנָּ֤ה\rb* \rb cake of bread|עֻגָ֨ה\rb* \rb from what you have|מִ֠שָּׁם\rb*, \rb and bring it out|וְהוֹצֵ֣אתְ\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb*. \rb Afterward|בָּאַחֲרֹנָֽה׃ס\rb*, \rb make some|תַּעֲשִׂ֖י\rb* \rb for yourself|וְלָ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and your son|וְלִבְנֵ֔ךְ\rb*, \v 14 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹה֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb says|אָמַ֨ר\rb*: ‘\rb The jar|כַּ֤ד\rb* \rb of flour|הַקֶּ֙מַח֙\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be exhausted|תִכְלָ֔ה\rb* \rb and the jug|וְצַפַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb of oil|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb run dry|תֶחְסָ֑ר\rb* \rb until|עַ֠ד\rb* \rb the day|י֧וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb sends|תִּתֶּן\rb* \rb rain|גֶּ֖שֶׁם\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 15 \rb So she went|וַתֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and did|וַתַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb and there was food|וַתֹּ֧אכַל\rb* \rb every day|יָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb for Elijah|וָהִיא\rb* \rb and the woman|הוּא־\rb* \rb and her household|וּבֵיתָ֖הּ\rb*. \v 16 \rb The jar|כַּ֤ד\rb* \rb of flour|הַקֶּ֙מַח֙\rb* \rb was not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb exhausted|כָלָ֔תָה\rb* \rb and the jug|וְצַפַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb of oil|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb run dry|חָסֵ֑ר\rb*, \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Elijah Raises the Widow’s Son
\p \v 17 \rb Later|אַחַר֙\rb*\rb |הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb who owned|בַּעֲלַ֣ת\rb* \rb the house|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb became ill|חָלָ֕ה\rb*, \rb and his sickness|חָלְיוֹ֙\rb* \rb grew worse|חָזָ֣ק\rb* \rb and worse|מְאֹ֔ד\rb*, \rb until|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb breath|נְשָׁמָֽה׃\rb* \rb remained|נֽוֹתְרָה־\rb* \rb in him|בּ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 18 “\rb O man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*,” \rb said the woman|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵ֣לִיָּ֔הוּ\rb*, “\rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb have you done|וָלָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb to me|לִּ֥י\rb*? \rb Have you come|בָּ֧אתָ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb to remind me|לְהַזְכִּ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of my iniquity|עֲוֺנִ֖י\rb* \rb and cause the death|וּלְהָמִ֥ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of my son|בְּנִֽי׃\rb*?”
\p \v 19 \rb But Elijah said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb*, “\rb Give|תְּנִֽי־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb your son|בְּנֵ֑ךְ\rb*.”
\p \rb So he took him|וַיִּקָּחֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb from her arms|מֵחֵיקָ֗הּ\rb*, \rb carried him|וַֽיַּעֲלֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the upper room|הָעֲלִיָּ֗ה\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he|הוּא֙\rb* \rb was staying|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb*,\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb and laid him|וַיַּשְׁכִּבֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his own bed|מִטָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb Then he cried out|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, “\rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָ֔י\rb*, \rb have You also|הֲ֠גַם\rb* \rb brought tragedy|הֲרֵע֖וֹתָ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb this widow|הָאַלְמָנָ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb who has opened her home to me|מִתְגּוֹרֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |עִמָּ֛הּ\rb*, \rb by causing|לְהָמִ֥ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her son to die|בְּנָֽהּ׃\rb*?” \v 21 \rb Then he stretched himself out|וַיִּתְמֹדֵ֤ד\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the child|הַיֶּ֙לֶד֙\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and cried out|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb*, “\rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb my God|אֱלֹהָ֔י\rb*, \rb please|נָ֛א\rb* \rb let this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb boy’s|הַיֶּ֥לֶד\rb* \rb life|נֶֽפֶשׁ־\rb* \rb return|תָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb him|קִרְבּֽוֹ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 22 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb and the child’s|הַיֶּ֛לֶד\rb* \rb life|נֶֽפֶשׁ־\rb* \rb returned|וַתָּ֧שָׁב\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb him|קִרְבּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and he lived|וַיֶּֽחִי׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb Then Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֜הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the child|הַיֶּ֗לֶד\rb*, \rb brought him down|וַיֹּרִדֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the upper room|הָעֲלִיָּה֙\rb* \rb into the house|הַבַּ֔יְתָה\rb*, \rb and gave him|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to his mother|לְאִמּ֑וֹ\rb*. “\rb Look|רְאִ֖י\rb*, \rb your son|בְּנֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb is alive|חַ֥י\rb*,” \rb Elijah|אֵ֣לִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Then the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵ֣לִיָּ֔הוּ\rb*, “\rb Now|עַתָּה֙\rb*\rb |זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you|אָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb are a man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and that the word|וּדְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb from your mouth|בְּפִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is truth|אֱמֶֽת׃פ\rb*.”
\c 18
\s1 Elijah’s Message to Ahab
\p \v 1 \rb After|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb a long|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb time|יָמִ֣ים\rb*, \rb in the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֖ית\rb* \rb year of the drought|בַּשָּׁנָ֥ה\rb*,\f + \fr 18:1 \ft Literally \fqa And the days were many, and in the third year,\f* \rb the word|וּדְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵ֣לִיָּ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: “\rb Go|לֵ֚ךְ\rb* \rb and present|הֵרָאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb yourself to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb and I will send|וְאֶתְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb rain|מָטָ֖ר\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאֲדָמָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb So Elijah|אֵֽלִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb to present himself|לְהֵרָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb*. \rb The famine|וְהָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb was severe|חָזָ֥ק\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb and Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb Obadiah|עֹבַדְיָ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the palace|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*.
\p (\rb Now Obadiah|וְעֹבַדְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb greatly|מְאֹֽד׃\rb*\rb |הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb feared|יָרֵ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \v 4 \rb for when|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb Jezebel|אִיזֶ֔בֶל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb had slaughtered|בְּהַכְרִ֣ית\rb* \rb the prophets|נְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb Obadiah|עֹבַדְיָ֜הוּ\rb* \rb had taken|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb prophets|נְבִאִ֗ים\rb* \rb and hidden them|וַֽיַּחְבִּיאֵ֞ם\rb*, \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb men|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb per cave|בַּמְּעָרָ֔ה\rb*, \rb providing them|וְכִלְכְּלָ֖ם\rb* \rb with food|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb and water|וָמָֽיִם׃\rb*.)
\p \v 5 \rb Then Ahab|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Obadiah|עֹ֣בַדְיָ֔הוּ\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb throughout the land|בָּאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb spring|מַעְיְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶ֖ל\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb valley|הַנְּחָלִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֣י׀\rb* \rb we will find|נִמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb grass|חָצִ֗יר\rb* \rb to keep the horses|ס֣וּס\rb* \rb and mules|וָפֶ֔רֶד\rb* \rb alive|וּנְחַיֶּה֙\rb* \rb so that we will not|וְל֥וֹא\rb* \rb have to destroy|נַכְרִ֖ית\rb* \rb any livestock|מֵהַבְּהֵמָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb So they divided|וַֽיְחַלְּק֥וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb to explore|לַֽעֲבָר־\rb*. \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֞ב\rb* \rb went|הָלַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb way|בְּדֶ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb by himself|לְבַדּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and Obadiah|וְעֹֽבַדְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb went|הָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb the other|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb way|בְּדֶרֶךְ־\rb* \rb by himself|לְבַדּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Now as Obadiah|עֹבַדְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb went|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb on his way|בַּדֶּ֔רֶךְ\rb*, \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb met him|לִקְרָאת֑וֹ\rb*. \rb When Obadiah recognized him|וַיַּכִּרֵ֙הוּ֙\rb*, \rb he fell|וַיִּפֹּ֣ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb facedown|פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is it|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb you|הַאַתָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 8 “\rb It is I|אָ֑נִי\rb*,” \rb he answered|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb*. “\rb Go|לֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb your master|לַאדֹנֶ֖יךָ\rb*, ‘\rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb is here|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*!’”
\p \v 9 \rb But Obadiah replied|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb How|מֶ֣ה\rb* \rb have I sinned|חָטָ֑אתִי\rb*, \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb are handing your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֛\rb* \rb over to|נֹתֵ֧ן\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb*\rb |בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb to put me to death|לַהֲמִיתֵֽנִי׃\rb*? \v 10 \rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb lives|חַ֣י׀\rb*, \rb there is|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb no|אִם־\rb* \rb nation|גּ֤וֹי\rb* \rb or kingdom|וּמַמְלָכָה֙\rb* \rb where|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb*\rb |שָׁם֙\rb* \rb has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb someone to search for you|לְבַקֶּשְׁךָ֔\rb*. \rb When they said|וְאָמְר֖וּ\rb*, ‘\rb He is not here|אָ֑יִן\rb*,’ \rb he made that kingdom|הַמַּמְלָכָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or nation|הַגּ֔וֹי\rb*\rb |כִּ֖י\rb* \rb swear|וְהִשְׁבִּ֤יעַ\rb* \rb that|אֶת־\rb* \rb they had not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb found you|יִמְצָאֶֽכָּה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb say|אֹמֵ֑ר\rb*, ‘\rb Go|לֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb your master that|לַאדֹנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb is here|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*!’
\p \v 12 \rb |וְהָיָ֞ה\rb* \rb I do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb know|אֵדָ֔ע\rb* \rb where|עַ֚ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the Spirit|וְר֨וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb may carry you off|יִֽשָּׂאֲךָ֙\rb* \rb when I|אֲנִ֣י׀\rb* \rb leave|אֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb you|מֵאִתָּ֗ךְ\rb*. \rb Then when I go|וּבָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb and tell|לְהַגִּ֧יד\rb* \rb Ahab|לְאַחְאָ֛ב\rb* \rb and he does not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb find you|יִֽמְצָאֲךָ֖\rb*, \rb he will kill me|וַהֲרָגָ֑נִי\rb*. \rb But I, your servant|וְעַבְדְּךָ֛\rb*, \rb have feared|יָרֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb from my youth|מִנְּעֻרָֽי׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Was it not|הֲלֹֽא־\rb* \rb reported|הֻגַּ֤ד\rb* \rb to my lord|לַֽאדֹנִי֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I did|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb* \rb when Jezebel|אִיזֶ֔בֶל\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb slaughtered|בַּהֲרֹ֣ג\rb* \rb the prophets|נְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*? \rb I hid|וָאַחְבִּא֩\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵ֣אָה\rb* \rb prophets|מִנְּבִיאֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*, \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֨ים\rb*\rb |חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb men|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb per cave|בַּמְּעָרָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and I provided them|וָאֲכַלְכְּלֵ֖ם\rb* \rb with food|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb and water|וָמָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb And now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb say|אֹמֵ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb Go|לֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֥ר\rb* \rb your lord|לַֽאדֹנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb that Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb is here|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*!’ \rb He will kill me|וַהֲרָגָֽנִי׃ס\rb*!”
\p \v 15 \rb Then Elijah|אֵֽלִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb lives|חַ֚י\rb*, \rb before|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I stand|עָמַ֖דְתִּי\rb*, \rb I will present myself|אֵרָאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to Ahab|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb*.”
\s1 Elijah on Mount Carmel
\p \v 16 \rb So Obadiah|עֹבַדְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb to|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb inform|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb*, \rb who|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb |וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb When Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|כִּרְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb he|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Is that|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb you|הַאַתָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb O troubler|עֹכֵ֥ר\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*?”
\p \v 18 “\rb I have not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb troubled|עָכַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*,” \rb Elijah replied|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb but|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and your father’s|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb house have|וּבֵ֣ית\rb*, \rb for you have forsaken|בַּֽעֲזָבְכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and have followed|וַתֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Baals|הַבְּעָלִֽים׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb summon|שְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to meet|קְבֹ֥ץ\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Carmel|הַכַּרְמֶ֑ל\rb*, \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּ֧ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb and fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֗ים\rb* \rb prophets|נְבִיאֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֜עַל\rb* \rb and the four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb prophets|וּנְבִיאֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Asherah|הָֽאֲשֵׁרָה֙\rb* \rb who eat|אֹכְלֵ֖י\rb* \rb at Jezebel’s|אִיזָֽבֶל׃\rb* \rb table|שֻׁלְחַ֥ן\rb*.”
\p \v 20 \rb So Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and assembled|וַיִּקְבֹּ֥ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb Carmel|הַכַּרְמֶֽל׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb Then Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֜הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּגַּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb How long|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַ֞י\rb* \rb will you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb waver|פֹּסְחִים֮\rb* \rb between|עַל־\rb* \rb two|שְׁתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb opinions|הַסְּעִפִּים֒\rb*? \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb is God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb*, \rb follow|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb Him|אַחֲרָ֔יו\rb*. \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb Baal is God|הַבַּ֖עַל\rb*, \rb follow|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אַחֲרָ֑יו\rb*.”
\p \rb But the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb answer|עָנ֥וּ\rb* \rb a word|דָּבָֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Then Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb am the only|לְבַדִּ֑י\rb* \rb remaining|נוֹתַ֧רְתִּי\rb* \rb prophet|נָבִ֛יא\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb but Baal has|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּע־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb and fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb* \rb prophets|וּנְבִיאֵ֣י\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb Get|וְיִתְּנוּ־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֣יִם\rb* \rb bulls|פָּרִ֗ים\rb* \rb for us|לָ֜נוּ\rb*. \rb Let the prophets of Baal choose|וְיִבְחֲר֣וּ\rb* \rb one|הָאֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb bull|הַפָּ֨ר\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶם֩\rb*, \rb cut it into pieces|וִֽינַתְּחֻ֗הוּ\rb*, \rb and place|וְיָשִׂ֙ימוּ֙\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wood|הָ֣עֵצִ֔ים\rb* \rb but not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb light|יָשִׂ֑ימוּ\rb* \rb the fire|וְאֵ֖שׁ\rb*. \rb And I|וַאֲנִ֞י\rb* \rb will prepare|אֶעֱשֶׂ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the other|הָאֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb bull|הַפָּ֣ר\rb* \rb and place|וְנָֽתַתִּי֙\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wood|הָ֣עֵצִ֔ים\rb* \rb but not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb light|אָשִֽׂים׃\rb* \rb the fire|וְאֵ֖שׁ\rb*. \v 24 \rb Then you may call|וּקְרָאתֶ֞ם\rb* \rb on the name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of your god|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb and I|וַֽאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will call|אֶקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb on the name|בְשֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb The God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb answers|יַעֲנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb by fire|בָאֵ֖שׁ\rb*, \rb He is|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*.”
\p \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |וַיַּ֧עַן\rb*, “\rb What you say|הַדָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb is good|ט֥וֹב\rb*.”
\p \v 25 \rb Then Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to the prophets|לִנְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֗עַל\rb*, “\rb Since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb are so numerous|הָרַבִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb choose|בַּחֲר֨וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb one|הָֽאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb bull|הַפָּ֤ר\rb* \rb and prepare|וַעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb it first|רִאשֹׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb Then call|וְקִרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb on the name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of your god|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb but do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb light|תָשִֽׂימוּ׃\rb* \rb the fire|וְאֵ֖שׁ\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb And they took|וַ֠יִּקְחוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|הַפָּ֨ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb was given|נָתַ֣ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֮\rb*, \rb prepared it|וַֽיַּעֲשׂוּ֒\rb*, \rb and called|וַיִּקְרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb on the name|בְשֵׁם־\rb* \rb of Baal|הַ֠בַּעַל\rb* \rb from morning|מֵהַבֹּ֨קֶר\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb noon|הַצָּהֳרַ֤יִם\rb*, \rb shouting|לֵאמֹר֙\rb*, “\rb O Baal|הַבַּ֣עַל\rb*, \rb answer us|עֲנֵ֔נוּ\rb*!”
\p \rb But there was no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb sound|ק֖וֹל\rb*, \rb and no one|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb answered|עֹנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb as they leaped|וַֽיְפַסְּח֔וּ\rb* \rb around|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they had made|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb |וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb At noon|בַֽצָּהֳרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb began to taunt|וַיְהַתֵּ֧ל\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶ֣ם\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Shout|קִרְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |בְקוֹל־\rb* \rb louder|גָּדוֹל֙\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he is|ה֔וּא\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb a god|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*! \rb Perhaps he is deep in thought|שִׂ֧יחַ\rb*\rb |וְכִֽי־\rb*, \rb or occupied|שִׂ֛יג\rb*,\rb |וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb or on a journey|דֶ֣רֶךְ\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֛י\rb* \rb he is|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb sleeping|יָשֵׁ֥ן\rb* \rb and must be awakened|וְיִקָֽץ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 28 \rb So they shouted louder|וַֽיִּקְרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |בְּק֣וֹל\rb*\rb |גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb and cut|וַיִּתְגֹּֽדְדוּ֙\rb* \rb themselves with knives|בַּחֲרָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb and lances|וּבָֽרְמָחִ֑ים\rb*, \rb as was their custom|כְּמִשְׁפָּטָ֔ם\rb*, \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the blood|דָּ֖ם\rb* \rb gushed|שְׁפָךְ־\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb Midday passed|כַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַֽצָּהֳרַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and they kept on raving|וַיִּֽתְנַבְּא֔וּ\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb the time|לַעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the evening sacrifice|הַמִּנְחָ֑ה\rb*. \rb But there was no|וְאֵֽין־\rb* \rb response|ק֥וֹל\rb*; \rb no|וְאֵין־\rb* \rb one answered|עֹנֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one paid attention|קָֽשֶׁב׃\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb Then Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb*, “\rb Come near|גְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*.” \rb So all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb approached him|וַיִּגְּשׁ֥וּ\rb*, \rb and he repaired|וַיְרַפֵּ֛א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb that had been torn down|הֶהָרֽוּס׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb And Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁתֵּ֤ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb stones|אֲבָנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb one for each|כְּמִסְפַּ֖ר\rb* \rb tribe|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַעֲקֹ֑ב\rb*, \rb to|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb had come|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb and said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb shall be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb your name|שְׁמֶֽךָ׃\rb*.” \v 32 \rb And with the stones|הָאֲבָנִ֛ים\rb*, \rb Elijah built|וַיִּבְנֶ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Then he dug|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb a trench|תְּעָלָ֗ה\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the altar|לַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \rb large enough to hold|כְּבֵית֙\rb* \rb two seahs|סָאתַ֣יִם\rb* \rb of seed|זֶ֔רַע\rb*.\f + \fr 18:32 \fqa 2 seahs \ft is approximately 13.2 dry quarts or 14.6 liters (probably about 25.4 pounds or 11.5 kilograms of seed).\f*
\p \v 33 \rb Next, he arranged|וַֽיַּעֲרֹ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wood|הָֽעֵצִ֑ים\rb*, \rb cut up|וַיְנַתַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bull|הַפָּ֔ר\rb*, \rb placed|וַיָּ֖שֶׂם\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wood|הָעֵצִֽים׃\rb*, \v 34 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Fill|מִלְא֨וּ\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֤ה\rb*\rb |כַדִּים֙\rb* \rb waterpots|מַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and pour the water|וְיִֽצְק֥וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the offering|הָעֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the wood|הָעֵצִ֑ים\rb*.”\f + \fr 18:34 \ft Some texts continue verse 33 to this point.\f*
\p “\rb Do it a second time|שְׁנוּ֙\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, \rb and they did it a second time|וַיִּשְׁנ֔וּ\rb*.
\p “\rb Do it a third time|שַׁלֵּ֖שׁוּ\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, \rb and they did it a third time|וַיְשַׁלֵּֽשׁוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb So the water|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb ran down|וַיֵּלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the altar|לַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb and even|וְגַ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb filled|מִלֵּא־\rb* \rb the trench|הַתְּעָלָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\s1 Elijah’s Prayer
\p \v 36 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb At the time of|בַּעֲל֣וֹת\rb* \rb the evening sacrifice|הַמִּנְחָ֗ה\rb*, \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֮\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּגַּ֞שׁ\rb* \rb the altar and said|וַיֹּאמַר֒\rb*, “\rb O LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of Abraham|אַבְרָהָם֙\rb*, \rb Isaac|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb*, \rb and Israel|וְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb let it be known|יִוָּדַ֗ע\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֧ה\rb* \rb are God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and that I am|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb Your servant|עַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and have done|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb things|וּבְדִבְרֶיךָ\rb* \rb at Your command|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb*. \v 37 \rb Answer me|עֲנֵ֤נִי\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*! \rb Answer me|עֲנֵ֔נִי\rb*, \rb so that this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb will know|וְיֵֽדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb are God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and that You|וְאַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb have turned|הֲסִבֹּ֥תָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their hearts|לִבָּ֖ם\rb* \rb back again|אֲחֹרַנִּֽית׃\rb*.”
\p \v 38 \rb Then the fire|אֵשׁ־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb fell|וַתִּפֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb and consumed|וַתֹּ֤אכַל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sacrifice|הָֽעֹלָה֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the wood|הָ֣עֵצִ֔ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the stones|הָאֲבָנִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the dust|הֶעָפָ֑ר\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and it licked up|לִחֵֽכָה׃\rb* \rb the water|הַמַּ֥יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the trench|בַּתְּעָלָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb When all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb saw this|וַיַּרְא֙\rb*, \rb they fell|וַֽיִּפְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb He|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*! \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb He|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*!”
\p \v 40 \rb Then Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb ordered|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb Seize|תִּפְשׂ֣וּ׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the prophets|נְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֗עַל\rb*! \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let a single one|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb escape|יִמָּלֵ֥ט\rb*.”\rb |מֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb So they seized them|וַֽיִּתְפְּשׂ֑וּם\rb*, \rb and Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb brought them down|וַיּוֹרִדֵ֤ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Kishon|קִישׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb Valley|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb and slaughtered them|וַיִּשְׁחָטֵ֖ם\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\s1 The LORD Sends Rain
\p \v 41 \rb And Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Ahab|לְאַחְאָ֔ב\rb*, “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֖ה\rb*, \rb eat|אֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb and drink|וּשְׁתֵ֑ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb there is the sound|ק֖וֹל\rb* \rb of a heavy|הֲמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb rain|הַגָּֽשֶׁם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 42 \rb So Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּעֲלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb and drink|וְלִשְׁתּ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb But Elijah|וְאֵ֨לִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb climbed|עָלָ֨ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the summit|רֹ֤אשׁ\rb* \rb of Carmel|הַכַּרְמֶל֙\rb*, \rb bent down|וַיִּגְהַ֣ר\rb* \rb on the ground|אַ֔רְצָה\rb*, \rb and put|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb his knees|בְּרָכוֹ׃\rb*. \v 43 “\rb Go|עֲלֵֽה־\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb* \rb and look|הַבֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb toward|דֶּֽרֶךְ־\rb* \rb the sea|יָ֔ם\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb his servant|נַעֲר֗וֹ\rb*.
\p \rb So the servant went|וַיַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb and looked|וַיַּבֵּ֔ט\rb*, \rb and he said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb There is nothing there|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |מְא֑וּמָה\rb*.”
\p \rb Seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִֽים׃\rb* \rb Elijah said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go back|שֻׁ֖ב\rb*.”
\p \v 44 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb On the seventh time|בַּשְּׁבִעִ֔ית\rb* \rb the servant reported|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb There is|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a cloud|עָ֛ב\rb* \rb as small|קְטַנָּ֥ה\rb* \rb as a man’s|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb hand|כְּכַף־\rb* \rb rising|עֹלָ֣ה\rb* \rb from the sea|מִיָּ֑ם\rb*.”
\p \rb And Elijah replied|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go|עֲלֵ֨ה\rb* \rb and tell|אֱמֹ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָב֙\rb*, ‘\rb Prepare your chariot|אֱסֹ֣ר\rb* \rb and go down|וָרֵ֔ד\rb* \rb before the rain|הַגָּֽשֶׁם׃\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb stops you|יַעַצָרְכָ֖ה\rb*.’”
\p \v 45 \rb Meanwhile|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb*\rb |כֹּ֗ה\rb*, \rb the sky|וְהַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb grew dark|הִֽתְקַדְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb with clouds|עָבִ֣ים\rb* \rb and wind|וְר֔וּחַ\rb*, \rb and a heavy|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb rain|גֶּ֣שֶׁם\rb* \rb began to fall|וַיְהִ֖י\rb*. \rb So Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb rode away|וַיִּרְכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶֽאלָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 46 \rb And the hand|וְיַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb came|הָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵ֣לִיָּ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and he tucked his cloak|וַיְשַׁנֵּ֖ס\rb* \rb into his belt|מָתְנָ֑יו\rb*\f + \fr 18:46 \ft Hebrew \fqa he girded up his loins\f* \rb and ran|וַיָּ֙רָץ֙\rb* \rb ahead of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb* \rb all the way to|עַד־\rb*\rb |בֹּאֲכָ֖ה\rb* \rb Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶֽאלָה׃\rb*.
\c 19
\s1 Elijah Flees from Jezebel
\p \v 1 \rb Now Ahab|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb Jezebel|לְאִיזֶ֔בֶל\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb and how|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had killed|הָרַ֛ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֖ים\rb* \rb with the sword|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So Jezebel|אִיזֶ֙בֶל֙\rb* \rb sent|וַתִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb a messenger|מַלְאָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb May the gods|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb deal with me|יַעֲשׂ֤וּן\rb*, \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely|יוֹסִפ֔וּן\rb*, \rb if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb by this time|כָעֵ֤ת\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָר֙\rb* \rb I have not made|אָשִׂ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֔\rb* \rb like the lives|כְּנֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of those you killed|אַחַ֥ד\rb*\rb |מֵהֶֽם׃\rb*!”
\p \v 3 \rb And Elijah was afraid|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb*\rb |וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb and ran|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֔וֹ\rb*. \rb When he came|וַיָּבֹ֕א\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb to Beersheba|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he left|וַיַּנַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb his servant|נַעֲר֖וֹ\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁם׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb while he himself|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb went|הָלַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb a day’s|י֔וֹם\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֕א\rb* \rb journey|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb into the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּר֙\rb*. \rb He sat down|וַיֵּ֕שֶׁב\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb a|אֶחָת\rb* \rb broom tree|רֹ֣תֶם\rb* \rb and prayed|וַיִּשְׁאַ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that he|נַפְשׁוֹ֙\rb* \rb might die|לָמ֔וּת\rb*. “\rb I have had enough|רַ֗ב\rb*\rb |עַתָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb*. “\rb Take|קַ֣ח\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֔י\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I am|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb better|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb than my fathers|מֵאֲבֹתָֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb Then he lay down|וַיִּשְׁכַּב֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the broom tree|רֹ֣תֶם\rb* \rb and fell asleep|וַיִּישַׁ֔ן\rb*.
\p \rb |אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb Suddenly|וְהִנֵּֽה־\rb*\rb |זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb an angel|מַלְאָךְ֙\rb* \rb touched|נֹגֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb him|בּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Get up|ק֥וּם\rb* \rb and eat|אֱכֽוֹל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb And he looked around|וַיַּבֵּ֕ט\rb*, \rb and there|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb by his head|מְרַאֲשֹׁתָ֛יו\rb* \rb was a cake of bread|עֻגַ֥ת\rb* \rb baked over hot coals|רְצָפִ֖ים\rb*, \rb and a jar|וְצַפַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb of water|מָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb So he ate|וַיֹּ֣אכַל\rb* \rb and drank|וַיֵּ֔שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb and lay down|וַיִּשְׁכָּֽב׃\rb* \rb again|וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb A second time|שֵׁנִית֙\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשָׁב֩\rb* \rb and touched|וַיִּגַּע־\rb* \rb him|בּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Get up|ק֣וּם\rb* \rb and eat|אֱכֹ֑ל\rb*,\rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb or the journey|הַדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb* \rb will be too much|רַ֥ב\rb* \rb for you|מִמְּךָ֖\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb So he got up|וַיָּ֖קָם\rb* \rb and ate|וַיֹּ֣אכַל\rb* \rb and drank|וַיִּשְׁתֶּ֑ה\rb*. \rb And strengthened|בְּכֹ֣חַ׀\rb* \rb by that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb food|הָאֲכִילָ֣ה\rb*, \rb he walked|וַיֵּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb days|יוֹם֙\rb* \rb and forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb nights|לַ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb until he reached|עַ֛ד\rb* \rb Horeb|חֹרֵֽב׃\rb*,\f + \fr 19:8 \ft That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai\f* \rb the mountain|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*.
\s1 The LORD Speaks to Elijah at Horeb
\p \v 9 \rb There|שָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb Elijah entered|וַיָּבֹא־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb a cave|הַמְּעָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and spent the night|וַיָּ֣לֶן\rb*. \rb And the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb came to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb saying|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |ל֔וֹ\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb are you doing|לְּךָ֥\rb* \rb here|פֹ֖ה\rb*, \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 10 “\rb I have been very zealous|קַנֹּ֨א\rb*\rb |קִנֵּ֜אתִי\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*, “\rb but|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have forsaken|עָזְב֤וּ\rb* \rb Your covenant|בְרִֽיתְךָ֙\rb*, \rb torn down|הָרָ֔סוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Your altars|מִזְבְּחֹתֶ֣יךָ\rb*, \rb and killed|הָרְג֣וּ\rb* \rb Your prophets|נְבִיאֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb with the sword|בֶחָ֑רֶב\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am the only one|לְבַדִּ֔י\rb* \rb left|וָֽאִוָּתֵ֤ר\rb*, \rb and they are seeking|וַיְבַקְשׁ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לְקַחְתָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb my life as well|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb*.”\f + \fr 19:10 \ft Cited in Romans 11:3; here and in verse 14\f*
\p \v 11 \rb Then the LORD said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go out|צֵ֣א\rb* \rb and stand|וְעָמַדְתָּ֣\rb* \rb on the mountain|בָהָר֮\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb*. \rb Behold|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb is about to pass by|עֹבֵ֗ר\rb*.”
\p \rb And a great|גְּדוֹלָ֡ה\rb* \rb and mighty|וְחָזָ֞ק\rb* \rb wind|וְר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb tore into|מְפָרֵק֩\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרִ֨ים\rb* \rb and shattered|וּמְשַׁבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb the rocks|סְלָעִים֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb was not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb in the wind|בָר֖וּחַ\rb*.
\p \rb After|וְאַחַ֤ר\rb* \rb the wind|הָר֨וּחַ\rb* \rb there was an earthquake|רַ֔עַשׁ\rb*, \rb but the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb was not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb in the earthquake|בָרַ֖עַשׁ\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb After|וְאַחַ֤ר\rb* \rb the earthquake|הָרַ֙עַשׁ֙\rb* \rb there was a fire|בָאֵ֖שׁ\rb*, \rb but the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb was not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb in the fire|אֵ֔שׁ\rb*.
\p \rb And after|וְאַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb came a still|דְּמָמָ֥ה\rb*, \rb small|דַקָּֽה׃\rb* \rb voice|ק֖וֹל\rb*. \v 13 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb When Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb heard it|כִּשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb*, \rb he wrapped|וַיָּ֤לֶט\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָיו֙\rb* \rb in his cloak|בְּאַדַּרְתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and went out|וַיֵּצֵ֕א\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb at the mouth|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the cave|הַמְּעָרָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb a voice came|ק֔וֹל\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb are you doing|לְּךָ֥\rb* \rb here|פֹ֖ה\rb*, \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 14 “\rb I have been very zealous|קַנֹּ֨א\rb*\rb |קִנֵּ֜אתִי\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה׀\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֗וֹת\rb*,” \rb he replied|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*, “\rb but|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have forsaken|עָזְב֤וּ\rb* \rb Your covenant|בְרִֽיתְךָ֙\rb*, \rb torn down|הָרָ֔סוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Your altars|מִזְבְּחֹתֶ֣יךָ\rb*, \rb and killed|הָרְג֣וּ\rb* \rb Your prophets|נְבִיאֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb with the sword|בֶחָ֑רֶב\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am the only one|לְבַדִּ֔י\rb* \rb left|וָאִוָּתֵ֤ר\rb*, \rb and they are seeking|וַיְבַקְשׁ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לְקַחְתָּֽהּ׃ס\rb* \rb my life as well|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb back|שׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb by the way you came|לְדַרְכְּךָ֖\rb*, \rb and go to the Desert|מִדְבַּ֣רָה\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַמָּ֑שֶׂק\rb*. \rb When you arrive|וּבָ֗אתָ\rb*, \rb you are to anoint|וּמָשַׁחְתָּ֧\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Hazael|חֲזָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb as king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Aram|אֲרָֽם׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb You are also to anoint|תִּמְשַׁ֥ח\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵה֣וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb*\f + \fr 19:16 \ft Or \fqa grandson\ft ; see 2 Kings 9:14.\f* \rb of Nimshi|נִמְשִׁ֔י\rb* \rb as king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֤ע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphat|שָׁפָט֙\rb*\rb |מֵאָבֵ֣ל\rb* \rb from Abel-meholah|מְחוֹלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |תִּמְשַׁ֥ח\rb* \rb to succeed you|תַּחְתֶּֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb as prophet|לְנָבִ֖יא\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Then|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵה֑וּא\rb* \rb will put to death|יָמִ֣ית\rb* \rb whoever escapes|הַנִּמְלָ֛ט\rb* \rb the sword|מֵחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb of Hazael|חֲזָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb and Elisha|אֱלִישָֽׁע׃\rb* \rb will put to death|יָמִ֥ית\rb* \rb whoever escapes|וְהַנִּמְלָ֛ט\rb* \rb the sword|מֵחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb of Jehu|יֵה֖וּא\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Nevertheless, I have reserved|וְהִשְׁאַרְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֑ים\rb* \rb in Israel|בְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*— \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb knees|הַבִּרְכַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb bowed|כָֽרְעוּ֙\rb* \rb to Baal|לַבַּ֔עַל\rb*\f + \fr 19:18 \ft Cited in Romans 11:4\f* \rb and whose|וְכָ֨ל־\rb* \rb mouths|הַפֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb kissed|נָשַׁ֖ק\rb* \rb him|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Call of Elisha
\p \v 19 \rb So Elijah departed|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |מִ֠שָּׁם\rb* \rb and found|וַיִּמְצָ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֤ע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphat|שָׁפָט֙\rb*. \rb He|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb was plowing|חֹרֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb with twelve|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֤ר\rb* \rb teams|צְמָדִים֙\rb* \rb of oxen|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb was with the twelfth team|בִּשְׁנֵ֣ים\rb*\rb |הֶעָשָׂ֑ר\rb*. \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb passed|וַיַּעֲבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb by him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and threw|וַיַּשְׁלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb his cloak|אַדַּרְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb around him|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb So Elisha left|וַיַּעֲזֹ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the oxen|הַבָּקָ֗ר\rb*, \rb ran|וַיָּ֙רָץ֙\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵֽלִיָּ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb and said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Please|נָּא֙\rb* \rb let me kiss|אֶשְּׁקָה־\rb* \rb my father|לְאָבִ֣י\rb* \rb and mother goodbye|וּלְאִמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb and then I will follow|וְאֵלְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb you|אַחֲרֶ֑יךָ\rb*.”
\p “\rb Go on|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb back|שׁ֔וּב\rb*,” \rb Elijah replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb what|מֶה־\rb* \rb have I done|עָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb* \rb to you|לָֽךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 21 \rb So Elisha turned back|וַיָּ֨שָׁב\rb* \rb from him|מֵאַחֲרָ֜יו\rb*, \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his pair|צֶ֧מֶד\rb* \rb of oxen|הַבָּקָ֣ר\rb*, \rb and slaughtered them|וַיִּזְבָּחֵ֗הוּ\rb*. \rb Using the oxen’s|הַבָּקָר֙\rb* \rb equipment for fuel|וּבִכְלִ֤י\rb*, \rb he cooked|בִּשְּׁלָ֣ם\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb and gave|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb it to the people|לָעָ֖ם\rb*, \rb and they ate|וַיֹּאכֵ֑לוּ\rb*. \rb Then he set out|וַיָּ֗קָם\rb* \rb to follow|וַיֵּ֛לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb and serve|וַיְשָׁרְתֵֽהוּ׃פ\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֖הוּ\rb*.
\c 20
\s1 Ben-hadad Attacks Samaria
\p \v 1 \rb |וּבֶן־\rb* \rb Now Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֣ד\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֗ם\rb* \rb assembled|קָבַץ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|חֵיל֔וֹ\rb*. \rb Accompanied by|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb thirty-two|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֨ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb kings|מֶ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb with their horses|וְס֣וּס\rb* \rb and chariots|וָרָ֑כֶב\rb*, \rb he marched up|וַיַּ֗עַל\rb*, \rb besieged|וַיָּ֙צַר֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Samaria|שֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb*, \rb and waged war|וַיִּלָּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb against it|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Then he sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֧ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֛ים\rb* \rb into the city|הָעִֽירָה׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֥ב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \v 3 \rb saying|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֔ד\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*:\f + \fr 20:3 \ft Some texts break verse 2 and begin verse 3 at this point.\f* ‘\rb Your silver|כַּסְפְּךָ֥\rb* \rb and gold|וּֽזְהָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb are|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb mine|לִֽי־\rb*, \rb and your best|הַטּוֹבִ֖ים\rb* \rb wives|וְנָשֶׁ֧יךָ\rb* \rb and children|וּבָנֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb are|הֵֽם׃\rb* \rb mine|לִי־\rb*!’”
\p \v 4 \rb And the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֤עַן\rb*, “\rb Just as you say|כִּדְבָרְךָ֖\rb*, \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*:\rb |לְךָ֥\rb* \rb I am yours|אֲנִ֖י\rb*, \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have|לִֽי׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb The messengers|הַמַּלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb came back|וַיָּשֻׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֖ד\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb*: ‘\rb I have sent|שָׁלַ֤חְתִּי\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb to demand|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |תִתֵּֽן׃\rb*\rb |לִ֥י\rb* \rb your silver|כַּסְפְּךָ֧\rb*, \rb your gold|וּזְהָבְךָ֛\rb*, \rb your wives|וְנָשֶׁ֥יךָ\rb*, \rb and your children|וּבָנֶ֖יךָ\rb*. \v 6 \rb But|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb about|אִם־\rb* \rb this time|כָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֗ר\rb* \rb I will send|אֶשְׁלַ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my servants|עֲבָדַי֙\rb* \rb to search|וְחִפְּשׂוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your palace|בֵּ֣יתְךָ֔\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the houses|בָּתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of your servants|עֲבָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb They will seize|יָשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb*\rb |בְיָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and carry away|וְלָקָֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb all that|כָּל־\rb* \rb is|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb precious|מַחְמַ֣ד\rb* \rb to you|עֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*.’”
\p \v 7 \rb Then the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb take note|דְּעֽוּ־\rb* \rb and see|וּרְא֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb this man|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb is looking for|מְבַקֵּ֑שׁ\rb* \rb trouble|רָעָ֖ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb when he demanded|שָׁלַ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֜י\rb* \rb my wives|לְנָשַׁ֤י\rb*, \rb my children|וּלְבָנַי֙\rb*, \rb my silver|וּלְכַסְפִּ֣י\rb*, \rb and my gold|וְלִזְהָבִ֔י\rb*, \rb I did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb deny|מָנַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb him|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb And the elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֛יו\rb*, “\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb listen to him|תִּשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb or|וְל֥וֹא\rb* \rb consent to his terms|תֹאבֶֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb So Ahab answered|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb the messengers|לְמַלְאֲכֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֗ד\rb*, “\rb Tell|אִמְר֞וּ\rb* \rb my lord|לַֽאדֹנִ֤י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*, ‘\rb All|כֹּל֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you demanded|שָׁלַ֨חְתָּ\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֤\rb* \rb the first time|בָרִֽאשֹׁנָה֙\rb* \rb I will do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb but this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb thing|וְהַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb I cannot|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb do|לַעֲשׂ֑וֹת\rb*.’”
\p \rb So the messengers|הַמַּלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb and relayed the message to Ben-hadad|דָּבָֽר׃\rb*\rb |וַיְשִׁבֻ֖הוּ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Then Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֔ד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb another message|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb to Ahab|אֵלָיו֙\rb*: “\rb May the gods|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb deal|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb with me|לִ֛י\rb*, \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely|יוֹסִ֑פוּ\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb enough dust|עֲפַ֣ר\rb* \rb remains|יִשְׂפֹּק֙\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb for each|לְכָל־\rb* \rb of my men|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |בְּרַגְלָֽי׃\rb* \rb to have a handful|לִשְׁעָלִ֕ים\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb And the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb replied|וַיַּ֤עַן\rb*, “\rb Tell him|דַּבְּר֔וּ\rb*: ‘\rb The one putting on his armor|חֹגֵ֖ר\rb* \rb should not|אַל־\rb* \rb boast|יִתְהַלֵּ֥ל\rb* \rb like one taking it off|כִּמְפַתֵּֽחַ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 12 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb Ben-hadad received|כִּשְׁמֹ֙עַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb message|הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb while he|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb and the kings|וְהַמְּלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb were drinking|שֹׁתֶ֛ה\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb in their tents|בַּסֻּכּ֑וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 20:12 \ft Or \fqa in Succoth\ft ; also in verse 16\f* \rb and he said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb*, “\rb Take your positions|שִׂ֔ימוּ\rb*.” \rb So they stationed themselves|וַיָּשִׂ֖ימוּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*.
\s1 Ahab Defeats Ben-hadad
\p \v 13 \rb Meanwhile|וְהִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb prophet|נָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb approached|נִגַּשׁ֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֣ב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb and declared|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb Do you see|הְֽרָאִ֔יתָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb army|הֶהָמ֥וֹן\rb*? \rb Behold|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I will deliver it|נֹתְנ֤וֹ\rb* \rb into your hand|בְיָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb this very day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*, \rb and you will know|וְיָדַעְתָּ֖\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 14 “\rb By whom|בְּמִ֔י\rb*?” \rb Ahab|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb And the prophet replied|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb By the young officers|בְּנַעֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the district|הַמְּדִינ֑וֹת\rb* \rb governors|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb*.’”
\p “\rb Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb will start|יֶאְסֹ֥ר\rb* \rb the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*?” \rb asked Ahab|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb*.
\p “\rb You will|אָֽתָּה׃\rb*,” \rb answered the prophet|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb So Ahab assembled|וַיִּפְקֹ֗ד\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the young officers|נַעֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the district|הַמְּדִינ֔וֹת\rb* \rb governors|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and there were|וַיִּהְי֕וּ\rb* \rb 232 men|מָאתַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |שְׁנַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֑ים\rb*. \rb And after them|וְאַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb he assembled|פָּקַ֧ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the rest of|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelite|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb troops|הָעָ֛ם\rb*, \rb 7,000|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִֽים׃\rb* \rb in all|כָּל־\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb They marched out|וַיֵּצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb at noon|בַּֽצָּהֳרָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |וּבֶן־\rb* \rb while Ben-hadad|הֲדַד֩\rb* \rb and the 32|שְׁלֹשִֽׁים־\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb kings|וְהַמְּלָכִ֛ים\rb* \rb allied|עֹזֵ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb were in their tents|בַּסֻּכּ֗וֹת\rb*\rb |ה֧וּא\rb* \rb getting|שֹׁתֶ֨ה\rb* \rb drunk|שִׁכּ֜וֹר\rb*. \v 17 \rb And the young officers|נַעֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb of the district|הַמְּדִינ֖וֹת\rb* \rb governors|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb marched out first|וַיֵּצְא֗וּ\rb*\rb |בָּרִֽאשֹׁנָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb Now Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֗ד\rb* \rb had sent out scouts|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb*, \rb who reported|וַיַּגִּ֤ידוּ\rb* \rb to him|לוֹ֙\rb*, “\rb Men|אֲנָשִׁ֕ים\rb* \rb are marching out|יָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb of Samaria|מִשֹּׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb they have marched out|יָצָ֖אוּ\rb* \rb in peace|לְשָׁל֥וֹם\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb*, “\rb take them|תִּפְשׂ֣וּם\rb* \rb alive|חַיִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb Even if|וְאִ֧ם\rb* \rb they have marched out|יָצָ֖אוּ\rb* \rb for war|לְמִלְחָמָ֛ה\rb*, \rb take them|תִּפְשֽׂוּם׃\rb* \rb alive|חַיִּ֥ים\rb*.”
\p \v 19 \rb Meanwhile, these|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb young officers|נַעֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the district|הַמְּדִינ֑וֹת\rb* \rb governors|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb marched out|יָצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb with the army|וְהַחַ֖יִל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb behind them|אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb and each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb one struck down|וַיַּכּוּ֙\rb* \rb his opponent|אִישׁ֔וֹ\rb*. \rb So the Arameans|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻ֣סוּ\rb*, \rb with the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb in pursuit|וַֽיִּרְדְּפֵ֖ם\rb*. \rb But Ben-hadad|הֲדַד֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb escaped|וַיִּמָּלֵ֗ט\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb horseback|ס֖וּס\rb* \rb with the cavalry|וּפָרָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Then the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb marched out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb and attacked|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the horses|הַסּ֖וּס\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and chariots|הָרָ֑כֶב\rb*, \rb inflicting|וְהִכָּ֥ה\rb* \rb a great|גְדוֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb slaughter|מַכָּ֥ה\rb* \rb on the Arameans|בַאֲרָ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Afterward, the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּגַּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and strengthen your position|הִתְחַזַּ֔ק\rb*, \rb and take note|וְדַ֥ע\rb*\rb |וּרְאֵ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb you must do|תַּעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb in the spring|לִתְשׁוּבַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 20:22 \ft Literally \fqa at the turn of the year\ft ; similarly in verse 26\f* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb will come up|עֹלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶֽיךָ׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb Meanwhile, the servants|וְעַבְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֜ם\rb* \rb said|אָמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Their gods are|אֱלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the hills|הָרִים֙\rb*. \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb they prevailed|חָזְק֣וּ\rb* \rb over us|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*. \rb Instead|וְאוּלָ֗ם\rb*, \rb we should fight|נִלָּחֵ֤ם\rb* \rb them|אִתָּם֙\rb* \rb on the plains|בַּמִּישׁ֔וֹר\rb*; \rb surely then|אִם־\rb* \rb we will prevail|נֶחֱזַ֖ק\rb*. \v 24 \rb So|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb do|עֲשֵׂ֑ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*: \rb Dismiss|הָסֵ֤ר\rb* \rb all|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb the kings|הַמְּלָכִים֙\rb* \rb from their positions|מִמְּקֹמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and replace them|וְשִׂ֥ים\rb*\rb |תַּחְתֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb with other officers|פַּח֖וֹת\rb*. \v 25 \rb And you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb must raise|תִֽמְנֶה־\rb* \rb an army|חַ֡יִל\rb* \rb like the one|כַּחַיִל֩\rb* \rb you have lost|הַנֹּפֵ֨ל\rb*—\rb |מֵאוֹתָ֜ךְ\rb* \rb horse|וְס֣וּס\rb* \rb for horse|כַּסּ֣וּס׀\rb* \rb and chariot|וְרֶ֣כֶב\rb* \rb for chariot|כָּרֶ֗כֶב\rb*— \rb so we can fight|וְנִֽלָּחֲמָ֤ה\rb* \rb the Israelites|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb on the plain|בַּמִּישׁ֔וֹר\rb*, \rb where we will surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb prevail|נֶחֱזַ֖ק\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֑ם\rb*.”
\p \rb And the king approved|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb their plan|לְקֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb and acted|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb accordingly|כֵּֽן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Another War with Ben-hadad
\p \v 26 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb In the spring|לִתְשׁוּבַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַשָּׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb mobilized|וַיִּפְקֹ֥ד\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֑ם\rb* \rb and went up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb to Aphek|אֲפֵ֔קָה\rb* \rb to fight|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb The Israelites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb also mobilized|הָתְפָּקְדוּ֙\rb*, \rb gathered supplies|וְכָלְכְּל֔וּ\rb*, \rb and marched out|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to meet them|לִקְרָאתָ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb The Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb camped|וַיַּחֲנ֨וּ\rb* \rb before them|נֶגְדָּ֗ם\rb* \rb like two|כִּשְׁנֵי֙\rb* \rb small flocks|חֲשִׂפֵ֣י\rb* \rb of goats|עִזִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb while the Arameans|וַאֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb covered|מִלְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the countryside|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb Then the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb approached|וַיִּגַּ֞שׁ\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb Because|יַ֠עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb have said that|אָמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is a god|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the hills|הָרִים֙\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the valleys|עֲמָקִ֖ים\rb*\rb |ה֑וּא\rb*, \rb I will deliver|וְ֠נָתַתִּי\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb great|הַגָּ֤דוֹל\rb* \rb army|הֶהָמ֨וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into your hand|בְּיָדֶ֔ךָ\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 29 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb the armies camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֧וּ\rb* \rb opposite each other|אֵ֦לֶּה\rb*\rb |נֹ֥כַח\rb*\rb |אֵ֖לֶּה\rb*, \rb and|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb on the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb ensued|וַתִּקְרַב֙\rb*, \rb and the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֧ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb struck down|וַיַּכּ֨וּ\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֛ם\rb*— \rb a hundred|מֵאָה־\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֥לֶף\rb* \rb foot soldiers|רַגְלִ֖י\rb* \rb in one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb*.
\p \v 30 \rb The rest of them|הַנּוֹתָרִ֥ים׀\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻ֨סוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִיר֒\rb* \rb of Aphek|אֲפֵקָה֮\rb*, \rb where the wall|הַחוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb fell|וַתִּפֹּל֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb twenty-seven|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעָ֥ה\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֛לֶף\rb* \rb of the remaining|הַנּוֹתָרִ֑ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*.\rb |וּבֶן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֣ד\rb* \rb also fled|נָ֔ס\rb* \rb to the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb and hid|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb an inner room|חֶ֥דֶר\rb*\rb |בְּחָֽדֶר׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Ahab Spares Ben-hadad
\p \v 31 \rb Then the servants of Ben-hadad|עֲבָדָיו֒\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֮\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb now|נָ֣א\rb*, \rb we have heard|שָׁמַ֔עְנוּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֗י\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵי֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb are merciful|חֶ֖סֶד\rb*\rb |הֵ֑ם\rb*\rb |מַלְכֵ֥י\rb*. \rb Let us go out|וְנֵצֵא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb with|נָשִׂ֣ימָה\rb*\rb |נָּא֩\rb* \rb sackcloth|שַׂקִּ֨ים\rb* \rb around our waists|בְּמָתְנֵ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb and ropes|וַחֲבָלִ֣ים\rb* \rb around our heads|בְּרֹאשֵׁ֗נוּ\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֖י\rb* \rb he will spare|יְחַיֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 32 \rb So with|וַיַּחְגְּרוּ֩\rb* \rb sackcloth|שַׂקִּ֨ים\rb* \rb around their waists|בְּמָתְנֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb and ropes|וַחֲבָלִ֣ים\rb* \rb around their heads|בְּרָאשֵׁיהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb they went|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb*, “\rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֧\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֛ד\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*, ‘\rb Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb spare|תְּחִֽי־\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֑י\rb*.’”
\p \rb And the king answered|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Is he still|הַעוֹדֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb alive|חַ֖י\rb*? \rb He|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is my brother|אָחִ֥י\rb*.”
\p \v 33 \rb Now the men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁים֩\rb* \rb were looking for a sign of hope|יְנַחֲשׁ֨וּ\rb*, \rb and they quickly|וַֽיְמַהֲר֜וּ\rb* \rb grasped at this word|וַיַּחְלְט֣וּ\rb*\rb |הֲמִמֶּ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb and replied|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Yes, your brother|אָחִ֣יךָ\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֔ד\rb*.”
\p “\rb Go|בֹּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb and get him|קָחֻ֑הוּ\rb*!” \rb said the king|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*.
\p \rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Then Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֔ד\rb* \rb came out|וַיֵּצֵ֤א\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb*, \rb and Ahab had him come up|וַֽיַּעֲלֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb his chariot|הַמֶּרְכָּבָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb Ben-hadad said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֡יו\rb*, “\rb I will restore|אָשִׁ֗יב\rb* \rb the cities|הֶעָרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִי֩\rb* \rb took|לָֽקַח־\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb your father|אָבִ֜יךָ\rb*; \rb you may set up|תָּשִׂ֨ים\rb* \rb your own|לְךָ֤\rb* \rb marketplaces|וְ֠חוּצוֹת\rb* \rb in Damascus|בְדַמֶּ֙שֶׂק֙\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb my father|אָבִי֙\rb* \rb did|שָׂ֤ם\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb*.”
\p “\rb By this treaty|בַּבְּרִ֣ית\rb*\f + \fr 20:34 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa berit \ft are translated in most passages as \fqa covenant\ft ; twice in this verse.\f* \rb I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb release you ,” Ahab replied|אֲשַׁלְּחֶ֑ךָּ\rb*. \rb So he made|וַיִּכְרָת־\rb* \rb a treaty|בְרִ֖ית\rb* \rb with him|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb and sent him away|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֵֽהוּ׃ס\rb*.
\s1 A Prophet Reproves Ahab
\p \v 35 \rb Meanwhile, by the word|בִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*,\rb |וְאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb of the sons|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֧ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his companion|רֵעֵ֛הוּ\rb*, “\rb Strike me|הַכֵּ֣ינִי\rb*, \rb please|נָ֑א\rb*!”
\p \rb But the man refused|וַיְמָאֵ֥ן\rb*\rb |הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb to strike him|לְהַכֹּתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb Then the prophet said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|ל֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Because|יַ֚עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb obeyed|שָׁמַ֙עְתָּ֙\rb* \rb the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb as soon as|הִנְּךָ֤\rb* \rb you depart|הוֹלֵךְ֙\rb* \rb from me|מֵֽאִתִּ֔י\rb* \rb a lion|הָאַרְיֵ֑ה\rb* \rb will kill you|וְהִכְּךָ֖\rb*.”
\p \rb And when he left|וַיֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽאֶצְל֔וֹ\rb*, \rb a lion|הָאַרְיֵ֖ה\rb* \rb found him|וַיִּמְצָאֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיַּכֵּֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb Then the prophet found|וַיִּמְצָא֙\rb* \rb another|אַחֵ֔ר\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Strike me|הַכֵּ֣ינִי\rb*, \rb please|נָ֑א\rb*!”
\p \rb So the man|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb struck him|וַיַּכֵּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb and wounded him|הַכֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּפָצֹֽעַ׃\rb*, \v 38 \rb and the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and waited|וַיַּעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the road|הַדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb* \rb for the king|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*, \rb disguising himself|וַיִּתְחַפֵּ֥שׂ\rb* \rb with a bandage|בָּאֲפֵ֖ר\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb his eyes|עֵינָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb As the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb passed by|עֹבֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb cried out|צָעַ֣ק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb*: “\rb Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֣׀\rb* \rb had marched out|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb into the middle|בְקֶֽרֶב־\rb* \rb of the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֗ה\rb*, \rb when suddenly|וְהִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb came over|סָ֜ר\rb* \rb with|וַיָּבֵ֧א\rb* \rb a captive|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֣י\rb*, ‘\rb Guard|שְׁמֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb*! \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb he goes missing|יִפָּקֵ֔ד\rb* \rb for any reason|הִפָּקֵד֙\rb*, \rb your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֙\rb* \rb will be exchanged|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb you will weigh out|תִּשְׁקֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb a talent|כִכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֖סֶף\rb*.\f + \fr 20:39 \fqa A talent \ft is approximately 75.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of silver.\f*’ \v 40 \rb But while your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֗\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb busy|עֹשֵׂ֥ה\rb* \rb here|הֵ֛נָּה\rb* \rb and there|וָהֵ֖נָּה\rb*, \rb the man|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb disappeared|אֵינֶ֑נּוּ\rb*.”
\p \rb And the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֧יו\rb*, “\rb So|כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb shall your judgment be|מִשְׁפָּטֶ֖ךָ\rb*; \rb you have pronounced it|חָרָֽצְתָּ׃\rb* \rb on yourself|אַתָּ֥ה\rb*.”
\p \v 41 \rb Then the prophet quickly|וַיְמַהֵ֕ר\rb* \rb removed|וַיָּ֙סַר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bandage|הָ֣אֲפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb from|מֵעַל\rb* \rb his eyes|עֵינָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb recognized|וַיַּכֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb as|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb one of the prophets|מֵֽהַנְּבִאִ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 42 \rb And the prophet said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to the king|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb Because|יַ֛עַן\rb* \rb you have let slip|שִׁלַּ֥חְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from your hand|מִיָּ֑ד\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb I had devoted to destruction|חֶרְמִ֖י\rb*,\f + \fr 20:42 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֙\rb* \rb will be exchanged|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb for|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and your people|וְעַמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb for|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb his people|עַמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 43 \rb Sullen|סַ֣ר\rb* \rb and angry|וְזָעֵ֑ף\rb*, \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֧לֶךְ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb home|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to Samaria|שֹׁמְרֽוֹנָה׃פ\rb*.
\c 21
\s1 Naboth’s Vineyard
\p \v 1 \rb Some time after|אַחַר֙\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb events|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb Naboth|לְנָב֥וֹת\rb* \rb the Jezreelite|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִ֖י\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb owned|הָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb a vineyard|כֶּ֧רֶם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Jezreel|בְּיִזְרְעֶ֑אל\rb* \rb next to|אֵ֚צֶל\rb* \rb the palace|הֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb* \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb So Ahab|אַחְאָ֣ב\rb* \rb said|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Naboth|נָב֣וֹת׀\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֩׀\rb*, “\rb Give|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your vineyard|כַּרְמְךָ֜\rb* \rb to use|וִֽיהִי־\rb* \rb as a vegetable|יָרָ֗ק\rb* \rb garden|לְגַן־\rb*, \rb since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb it|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb is next to|קָרוֹב֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb my palace|בֵּיתִ֔י\rb*. \rb I will give|וְאֶתְּנָ֤ה\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb a better|ט֣וֹב\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb vineyard|כֶּ֖רֶם\rb* \rb in its place|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb* — \rb or if|אִ֚ם\rb* \rb you prefer|ט֣וֹב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb I will give|אֶתְּנָה־\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb its|זֶֽה׃\rb* \rb value|מְחִ֥יר\rb* \rb in silver|כֶ֖סֶף\rb*.”
\p \v 3 \rb But Naboth|נָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אַחְאָ֑ב\rb*, “\rb The LORD|מֵֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb forbid|חָלִ֤ילָה\rb* \rb that I|לִּי֙\rb* \rb should give|מִתִּתִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֥ת\rb* \rb of my fathers|אֲבֹתַ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb So Ahab|אַחְאָ֨ב\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹא֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his palace|בֵּית֜וֹ\rb*, \rb sullen|סַ֣ר\rb* \rb and angry|וְזָעֵ֗ף\rb* \rb because|עַל־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Naboth|נָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb the Jezreelite|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִ֔י\rb* \rb had told him|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb give|אֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the inheritance|נַחֲלַ֣ת\rb* \rb of my fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֑י\rb*.” \rb He lay down|וַיִּשְׁכַּב֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his bed|מִטָּת֔וֹ\rb*, \rb turned his face|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb away|וַיַּסֵּ֥ב\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and refused|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb to eat|אָ֥כַל\rb*\rb |לָֽחֶם׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Soon his wife|אִשְׁתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb Jezebel|אִיזֶ֣בֶל\rb* \rb came in|וַתָּבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb and asked|וַתְּדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Why|מַה־\rb* \rb are you|רוּחֲךָ֣\rb* \rb so|זֶּה֙\rb* \rb sullen|סָרָ֔ה\rb* \rb that you refuse|וְאֵינְךָ֖\rb* \rb to eat|אֹכֵ֥ל\rb*\rb |לָֽחֶם׃\rb*?”
\p \v 6 \rb Ahab answered|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֗יהָ\rb*, “\rb Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I spoke|אֲ֠דַבֵּר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Naboth|נָב֨וֹת\rb* \rb the Jezreelite|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִ֜י\rb* \rb and told|וָאֹ֣מַר\rb* \rb him|ל֗וֹ\rb*, ‘\rb Give|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your vineyard|כַּרְמְךָ֙\rb* \rb for silver|בְּכֶ֔סֶף\rb*, \rb or|א֚וֹ\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb wish|חָפֵ֣ץ\rb*, \rb I will give|אֶתְּנָה־\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb another vineyard|כֶ֖רֶם\rb* \rb in its place|תַּחְתָּ֑יו\rb*.’ \rb And he replied|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb give|אֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my vineyard|כַּרְמִֽי׃\rb*!’”
\p \v 7 \rb But his wife|אִשְׁתּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb Jezebel|אִיזֶ֣בֶל\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb Do you not|עַתָּ֛ה\rb*\rb |תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb reign|מְלוּכָ֖ה\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*? \rb Get up|ק֤וּם\rb*, \rb eat|אֱכָל־\rb* \rb some food|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb*, \rb and be cheerful|וְיִטַ֣ב\rb*\rb |לִבֶּ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb for I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will get|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the vineyard|כֶּ֖רֶם\rb* \rb of Naboth|נָב֥וֹת\rb* \rb the Jezreelite|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִֽי׃\rb*.”
\s1 Jezebel’s Plot
\p \v 8 \rb Then Jezebel wrote|וַתִּכְתֹּ֤ב\rb* \rb letters|סְפָרִים֙\rb* \rb in Ahab’s|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb* \rb name|בְּשֵׁ֣ם\rb*, \rb sealed them|בְּחֹתָמ֑וֹ\rb* \rb with his seal|וַתַּחְתֹּ֖ם\rb*, \rb and sent|וַתִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb them|הַסְפָרִים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the elders|הַזְקֵנִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and nobles|הַֽחֹרִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb lived|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Naboth|נָבֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb in his city|בְּעִיר֔וֹ\rb*. \v 9 \rb In the letters|בַּסְּפָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb she wrote|וַתִּכְתֹּ֥ב\rb*:
\pmo “\rb Proclaim|קִֽרְאוּ־\rb* \rb a fast|צ֔וֹם\rb* \rb and give|וְהוֹשִׁ֥יבוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Naboth|נָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb a seat of honor|בְּרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb among the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb But seat|וְ֠הוֹשִׁיבוּ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֨יִם\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb scoundrels|בְלִיַּעַל֮\rb* \rb opposite him|נֶגְדּוֹ֒\rb* \rb and have them testify|וִיעִדֻ֣הוּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, ‘\rb You have cursed|בֵּרַ֥כְתָּ\rb* \rb both God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and the king|וָמֶ֑לֶךְ\rb*!’ \rb Then take him out|וְהוֹצִיאֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb and stone him|וְסִקְלֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to death|וְיָמֹֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb |אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb*\rb |עִיר֜וֹ\rb* \rb So the elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and nobles|וְהַחֹרִ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb lived|הַיֹּֽשְׁבִים֙\rb* \rb in Naboth’s city|בְּעִיר֔וֹ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּעֲשׂוּ֩\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb Jezebel|אִיזָ֑בֶל\rb* \rb had instructed|שָׁלְחָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |כָּתוּב֙\rb* \rb in the letters|בַּסְּפָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb she had written|שָׁלְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb They proclaimed|קָרְא֖וּ\rb* \rb a fast|צ֑וֹם\rb* \rb and gave|וְהֹשִׁ֥יבוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Naboth|נָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb a seat of honor|בְּרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb among the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And the two|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb scoundrels|בְלִיַּעַל֮\rb*\rb |הָאֲנָשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb came in|וַ֠יָּבֹאוּ\rb* \rb and sat|וַיֵּשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb opposite Naboth|נֶגְדּוֹ֒\rb*, \rb and these men|הַבְּלִיַּ֜עַל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb testified|וַיְעִדֻהוּ֩\rb* \rb against him|נָב֗וֹת\rb* \rb before|נֶ֤גֶד\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Naboth|נָב֛וֹת\rb* \rb has cursed|בֵּרַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb both God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and the king|וָמֶ֑לֶךְ\rb*!”
\p \rb So they took him|וַיֹּצִאֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb outside|מִח֣וּץ\rb* \rb the city|לָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and stoned him|וַיִּסְקְלֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb to death|וַיָּמֹֽת׃\rb*\rb |בָאֲבָנִ֖ים\rb*. \v 14 \rb Then they sent|וַֽיִּשְׁלְח֖וּ\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jezebel|אִיזֶ֣בֶל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*: “\rb Naboth|נָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb has been stoned|סֻקַּ֥ל\rb* \rb to death|וַיָּמֹֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb When Jezebel|אִיזֶ֔בֶל\rb* \rb heard|כִּשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Naboth|נָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb had been stoned|סֻקַּ֥ל\rb* \rb to death|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb*, \rb she|אִיזֶ֜בֶל\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֗ב\rb*, “\rb Get up|ק֣וּם\rb* \rb and take possession of|רֵ֞שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the vineyard|כֶּ֣רֶם׀\rb* \rb of Naboth|נָב֣וֹת\rb* \rb the Jezreelite|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִ֗י\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb refused|מֵאֵן֙\rb* \rb to give it|לָתֶת־\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb for silver|בְכֶ֔סֶף\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Naboth|נָב֛וֹת\rb* \rb is no longer|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb alive|חַ֖י\rb*, \rb but|כִּי־\rb* \rb dead|מֵֽת׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb And|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb when Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb heard|כִּשְׁמֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Naboth|נָב֑וֹת\rb* \rb was dead|מֵ֣ת\rb*, \rb he|אַחְאָ֗ב\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and went|לָרֶ֛דֶת\rb* \rb down|אֶל־\rb* \rb to take possession|לְרִשְׁתּֽוֹ׃ס\rb* \rb of the vineyard|כֶּ֛רֶם\rb* \rb of Naboth|נָב֥וֹת\rb* \rb the Jezreelite|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִ֖י\rb*.
\s1 Elijah Denounces Ahab and Jezebel
\p \v 17 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the Tishbite|הַתִּשְׁבִּ֖י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 18 “\rb Get up|ק֣וּם\rb* \rb and go down|רֵ֗ד\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֛את\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֥ב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is in Samaria|בְּשֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb*. \rb See, he is|הִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb in the vineyard|בְּכֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb of Naboth|נָב֔וֹת\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has gone|יָ֥רַד\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb to take possession of it|לְרִשְׁתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Tell|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֨\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb*: ‘\rb Have you not murdered a man|הֲרָצַ֖חְתָּ\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb seized his land|יָרָ֑שְׁתָּ\rb*?’
\p \rb Then tell him|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֨\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֜יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb that this is also what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb In the place|בִּמְק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the dogs|הַכְּלָבִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb licked up|לָקְק֤וּ\rb* \rb the blood|דַּ֣ם\rb* \rb of Naboth|נָב֔וֹת\rb*, \rb there also the dogs|הַכְּלָבִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will lick up|יָלֹ֧קּוּ\rb* \rb your blood|דָּמְךָ֖\rb* — \rb yes|גַּם־\rb*, \rb yours|אָֽתָּה׃\rb*!’\f + \fr 21:19 \ft See 1 Kings 22:38\f*”
\p \v 20 \rb When Elijah arrived|אֵ֣לִיָּ֔הוּ\rb*, \rb Ahab|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֶל־\rb*, “\rb So you have found me out|הַֽמְצָאתַ֖נִי\rb*, \rb my enemy|אֹיְבִ֑י\rb*.”
\p \rb He replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb I have found you out|מָצָ֔אתִי\rb* \rb because|יַ֚עַן\rb* \rb you have sold yourself|הִתְמַכֶּרְךָ֔\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb This is what the LORD says|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*:\f + \fr 21:21 \ft See LXX; the source of the quotation is clarified in verses 17 and 23; Hebrew \fqa Behold\ft .\f*
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb I will bring|מֵבִי\rb* \rb calamity|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb on you|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and consume|וּבִעַרְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb your descendants|אַחֲרֶ֑יךָ\rb*;
\q1 \rb I will cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb from Ahab|לְאַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb every male|מַשְׁתִּ֣ין\rb*\rb |בְּקִ֔יר\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*,
\q2 \rb both slave|וְעָצ֥וּר\rb* \rb and free|וְעָז֖וּב\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your house|בֵּיתְךָ֗\rb* \rb like that|כְּבֵית֙\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֔ט\rb*
\q2 \rb and like that|וּכְבֵ֖ית\rb* \rb of Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֣א\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahijah|אֲחִיָּ֑ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb because|אֶל־\rb* \rb you have provoked|הִכְעַ֔סְתָּ\rb* \rb My anger|הַכַּ֙עַס֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to sin|וַֽתַּחֲטִ֖א\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*’
\p \v 23 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb also|וְגַ֨ם־\rb* \rb speaks|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb concerning Jezebel|לְאִיזֶ֔בֶל\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb The dogs|הַכְּלָבִ֛ים\rb* \rb will devour|יֹאכְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jezebel|אִיזֶ֖בֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb by the wall|בְּחֵ֥ל\rb* \rb of Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶֽאל׃\rb*.’\f + \fr 21:23 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts; a few Hebrew manuscripts, Vulgate, and Syriac (see also 2 Kings 9:36) \fqa ‘The dogs will devour Jezebel at the plot of ground at Jezreel.’\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 24 \rb Anyone belonging to Ahab|לְאַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb who dies|הַמֵּ֤ת\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֔יר\rb*
\q2 \rb will be eaten|יֹאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb by dogs|הַכְּלָבִ֑ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb and anyone who dies|וְהַמֵּת֙\rb* \rb in the field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb will be eaten|יֹאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb by the birds|ע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*.”
\s1 Ahab’s Repentance
\p \v 25 (\rb Surely|רַ֚ק\rb* \rb there was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb one like Ahab|כְאַחְאָ֔ב\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb sold himself|הִתְמַכֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb incited|הֵסַ֥תָּה\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb by his wife|אִשְׁתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb Jezebel|אִיזֶ֥בֶל\rb*. \v 26 \rb He committed the most|מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb detestable acts|וַיַּתְעֵ֣ב\rb* \rb by going|לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb idols|הַגִּלֻּלִ֑ים\rb*, \rb just like|כְּכֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb*\rb |עָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had driven out|הוֹרִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.)
\p \v 27 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb When Ahab|אַחְאָ֜ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֤ים\rb*, \rb he tore|וַיִּקְרַ֣ע\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb*, \rb put|וַיָּֽשֶׂם־\rb* \rb on sackcloth|שַׂ֥ק\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בְּשָׂר֖וֹ\rb*, \rb and fasted|וַיָּצ֑וֹם\rb*. \rb He lay down|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb in sackcloth|בַּשָּׂ֔ק\rb* \rb and walked around|וַיְהַלֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb meekly|אַֽט׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb Then the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the Tishbite|הַתִּשְׁבִּ֖י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 29 “\rb Have you seen|הֲ‍ֽרָאִ֔יתָ\rb* \rb how|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb has humbled himself|נִכְנַ֥ע\rb* \rb before Me|מִלְּפָנָ֑י\rb*? \rb Because|יַ֜עַן\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he has humbled himself|נִכְנַ֣ע\rb* \rb before Me|מִפָּנַ֗י\rb*, \rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb bring|אָבִי\rb* \rb the calamity|הָֽרָעָה֙\rb* \rb during his days|בְּיָמָ֔יו\rb*, \rb but I will bring|אָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb it|הָרָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb his house|בֵּיתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his son|בְנ֔וֹ\rb*.”
\c 22
\s1 Ahab and the False Prophets
\r (2 Chronicles 18:1–11)
\p \v 1 \rb Then three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb passed|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb without|אֵ֚ין\rb* \rb war|מִלְחָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb However|וַיְהִ֖י\rb*, \rb in the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֑ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb*, \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּ֛רֶד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb visit the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb who|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb*, “\rb Do you not know|הַיְדַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֣ת\rb* \rb is ours|לָ֖נוּ\rb*,\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb* \rb but we|וַאֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb have failed|מַחְשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb to take|מִקַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb it|אֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָֽם׃\rb*?”
\p \v 4 \rb So he asked|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְה֣וֹשָׁפָ֔ט\rb*, “\rb Will you go|הֲתֵלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֛י\rb* \rb to fight|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֣ת\rb*?”
\p \rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהֽוֹשָׁפָט֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, “\rb I am|כָּמ֧וֹנִי\rb* \rb as you are|כָמ֛וֹךָ\rb*, \rb my people are|כְּעַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb your people|כְעַמֶּ֖ךָ\rb*, \rb and my horses are|כְּסוּסַ֥י\rb* \rb your horses|כְּסוּסֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb But Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb also said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, “\rb Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb inquire|דְּרָשׁ־\rb* \rb first|כַיּ֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the word|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 6 \rb So the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּקְבֹּ֨ץ\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִים֮\rb*, \rb about four|כְּאַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִישׁ֒\rb*, \rb and asked them|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb*, “\rb Should I go|הַאֵלֵ֞ךְ\rb* \rb to war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֛ד\rb*, \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb should I refrain|אֶחְדָּ֑ל\rb*?”
\p “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֔ה\rb*,” \rb they replied|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*, “\rb and the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֖י\rb* \rb will deliver it|וְיִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb But Jehoshaphat|יְה֣וֹשָׁפָ֔ט\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Is there not|הַאֵ֨ין\rb* \rb still|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִ֛יא\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb here|פֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb of whom we can inquire|וְנִדְרְשָׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |מֵאוֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 8 \rb The king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל׀\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |יְהוֹשָׁפָ֡ט\rb*, “\rb There is still|ע֣וֹד\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֡ד\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb through whom we can inquire of|לִדְרֹשׁ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb*,\rb |מֵאֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb but I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb hate him|שְׂנֵאתִ֗יו\rb* \rb because|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb he never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb prophesies|יִתְנַבֵּ֨א\rb* \rb anything good|טוֹב֙\rb* \rb for me|עָלַ֥י\rb*, \rb but only|אִם־\rb* \rb bad|רָ֔ע\rb*. \rb He is Micaiah|מִיכָ֖יְהוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Imlah|יִמְלָ֑ה\rb*.”
\p “\rb The king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb should not|אַל־\rb* \rb say|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb that|כֵּֽן׃\rb*!” \rb Jehoshaphat|יְה֣וֹשָׁפָ֔ט\rb* \rb replied|יֹאמַ֥ר\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb So the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb of his officials|סָרִ֖יס\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Bring|מַהֲרָ֖ה\rb* \rb Micaiah|מִיכָ֥יְהוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Imlah at once|יִמְלָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb Dressed|מְלֻבָּשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb in royal attire|בְּגָדִים֙\rb*, \rb the king|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb and Jehoshaphat|וִֽיהוֹשָׁפָ֣ט\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֡ה\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb were sitting|יֹשְׁבִים֩\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their thrones|כִּסְא֜וֹ\rb* \rb at the threshing floor|בְּגֹ֔רֶן\rb* \rb by the entrance|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb of the gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb with all|וְכָ֨ל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb* \rb prophesying|מִֽתְנַבְּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb before them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Now Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶֽן־\rb* \rb of Chenaanah|כְּנַעֲנָ֖ה\rb* \rb had made|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb for himself|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb iron|בַרְזֶ֑ל\rb* \rb horns|קַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb and declared|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb With these|בְּאֵ֛לֶּה\rb* \rb you shall gore|תְּנַגַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb they are finished off|כַּלֹּתָֽם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 12 \rb And all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִאִ֔ים\rb* \rb were prophesying|נִבְּאִ֥ים\rb* \rb the same|כֵּ֖ן\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֞ה\rb* \rb to Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֤ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָד֙\rb* \rb and triumph|וְהַצְלַ֔ח\rb*, \rb for the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will deliver it|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.”
\s1 Micaiah Prophesies against Ahab
\r (2 Chronicles 18:12–27)
\p \v 13 \rb Then the messenger|וְהַמַּלְאָ֞ךְ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had gone|הָלַ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb to call|לִקְרֹ֣א\rb* \rb Micaiah|מִיכָ֗יְהוּ\rb* \rb instructed him|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb*,\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* “\rb Behold|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb now|נָ֞א\rb*, \rb with one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb accord|פֶּֽה־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֛ים\rb* \rb are favorable|ט֖וֹב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*. \rb So please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb let your words|דִבְרֶיךָ\rb* \rb be|יְהִֽי־\rb* \rb like theirs|כִּדְבַ֛ר\rb*,\rb |אַחַ֥ד\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and speak|וְדִבַּ֥רְתָּ\rb* \rb favorably|טּֽוֹב׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb But Micaiah|מִיכָ֑יְהוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*, “\rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֕ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֠י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb*, \rb I will speak|אֲדַבֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb tells|יֹאמַ֧ר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb*.”
\p \v 15 \rb When Micaiah arrived|וַיָּבוֹא֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּלֶךְ֒\rb*, \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*, “\rb Micaiah|מִיכָ֙יְהוּ֙\rb*, \rb should we go|הֲנֵלֵ֞ךְ\rb* \rb to war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֥ת\rb*,\rb |גִּלְעָ֛ד\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb should we refrain|נֶחְדָּ֑ל\rb*?”
\p “\rb Go up|עֲלֵ֣ה\rb* \rb and triumph|וְהַצְלַ֔ח\rb*,” \rb Micaiah replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb for the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will deliver it|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb But the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb*, “\rb How many|עַד־\rb*\rb |כַּמֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb times|פְעָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb must I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb make you swear|מַשְׁבִּעֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to tell me|תְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb anything but|רַק־\rb* \rb the truth|אֱמֶ֖ת\rb* \rb in the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*?”
\p \v 17 \rb So Micaiah declared|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb I saw|רָאִ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb scattered|נְפֹצִ֣ים\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the hills|הֶהָרִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb like sheep|כַּצֹּ֕אן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb without|אֵין־\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a shepherd|רֹעֶ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb These people|לָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb have no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb master|אֲדֹנִ֣ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb let each one|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb return|יָשׁ֥וּבוּ\rb* \rb home|לְבֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb in peace|בְּשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 18 \rb Then the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֑ט\rb*, “\rb Did I not|הֲלוֹא֙\rb* \rb tell|אָמַ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb that he never|לֽוֹא־\rb* \rb prophesies|יִתְנַבֵּ֥א\rb* \rb good|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb for me|עָלַ֛י\rb*, \rb but only|כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb bad|רָֽע׃\rb*?”
\p \v 19 \rb Micaiah continued|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Therefore|לָכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb hear|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*: \rb I saw|רָאִ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb sitting|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb His throne|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֤א\rb* \rb of heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb by Him|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb on His right|מִימִינ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and on His left|וּמִשְּׂמֹאלֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb will entice|יְפַתֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb* \rb to march up|וְיַ֕עַל\rb* \rb and fall|וְיִפֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb at Ramoth-gilead|בְּרָמֹ֣ת\rb*?’\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*
\p \rb And one|זֶה֙\rb* \rb suggested|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb this|בְּכֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb and another|וְזֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹמֵ֖ר\rb* \rb that|בְּכֹֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb Then a spirit|הָר֗וּחַ\rb* \rb came forward|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb*, \rb stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb will entice him|אֲפַתֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*.’\f + \fr 22:21 \ft Some texts break verse 21 and begin verse 22 at this point.\f*
\p ‘\rb By what means|בַּמָּֽה׃\rb*?’ \rb asked|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb And he replied|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*, ‘\rb I will go out|אֵצֵא֙\rb* \rb and be|וְהָיִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb a lying|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \rb spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb in the mouths|בְּפִ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his prophets|נְבִיאָ֑יו\rb*.’
\p ‘\rb You will surely|וְגַם־\rb* \rb entice him|תְּפַתֶּה֙\rb* \rb and prevail|תּוּכָ֔ל\rb*,’ \rb said the LORD|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*. ‘\rb Go|צֵ֖א\rb* \rb and do|וַעֲשֵׂה־\rb* \rb it|כֵֽן׃\rb*.’
\p \v 23 \rb So|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb you see|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has put|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb a lying|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \rb spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb in the mouths|בְּפִ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb prophets of yours|נְבִיאֶ֣יךָ\rb*, \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has pronounced|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָֽה׃\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb*.”
\p \v 24 \rb Then Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶֽן־\rb* \rb of Chenaanah|כְּנַעֲנָ֔ה\rb* \rb went up|וַיִּגַּשׁ֙\rb*, \rb struck|וַיַּכֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Micaiah|מִיכָ֖יְהוּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|הַלֶּ֑חִי\rb*, \rb and demanded|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Which way|אֵי־\rb*\rb |זֶ֨ה\rb* \rb did the Spirit|רֽוּחַ־\rb* \rb of the LORD go|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb when He departed|עָבַ֧ר\rb* \rb from me|מֵאִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with you|אוֹתָֽךְ׃\rb*?”
\p \v 25 \rb Micaiah|מִיכָ֔יְהוּ\rb*\rb |הִנְּךָ֥\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb You will soon see|רֹאֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb on that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you go|תָּבֹ֛א\rb* \rb and hide|לְהֵחָבֵֽה׃\rb* \rb in an inner|חֶ֥דֶר\rb* \rb room|בְּחֶ֖דֶר\rb*.”
\p \v 26 \rb And the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb declared|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*, “\rb Take|קַ֚ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Micaiah|מִיכָ֔יְהוּ\rb* \rb and return him|וַהֲשִׁיבֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Amon|אָמֹ֣ן\rb* \rb the governor|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Joash|יוֹאָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb*, \v 27 \rb and tell them|וְאָמַרְתָּ֗\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb Put|שִׂ֥ימוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this man|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in prison|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַכֶּ֑לֶא\rb* \rb and feed him|וְהַאֲכִילֻ֨הוּ\rb* \rb only bread|לֶ֤חֶם\rb*\rb |לַ֙חַץ֙\rb* \rb and water|וּמַ֣יִם\rb*\rb |לַ֔חַץ\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb I return|בֹּאִ֥י\rb* \rb safely|בְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 28 \rb But Micaiah|מִיכָ֔יְהוּ\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you ever return|שׁ֤וֹב\rb*\rb |תָּשׁוּב֙\rb* \rb safely|בְּשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb spoken|דִבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb through me|בִּ֑י\rb*.” \rb Then he added|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Take heed|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb*, \rb all|כֻּלָּֽם׃\rb* \rb you people|עַמִּ֥ים\rb*!”
\s1 Ahab’s Defeat and Death
\r (2 Chronicles 18:28–34)
\p \v 29 \rb So the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and Jehoshaphat|וְיהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֧עַל\rb* \rb to Ramoth-gilead|רָמֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָֽד׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb And the king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט\rb*, “\rb I will disguise myself|הִתְחַפֵּשׂ֙\rb* \rb and go|וָבֹ֣א\rb* \rb into battle|בַמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb but you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb wear|לְבַ֣שׁ\rb* \rb your royal robes|בְּגָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*.” \rb So the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb disguised himself|וַיִּתְחַפֵּשׂ֙\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּב֖וֹא\rb* \rb into battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb Now the king|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֡ם\rb* \rb had ordered|צִוָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his thirty-two|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb chariot|הָרֶ֨כֶב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵי֩\rb*, “\rb Do not|לֹ֚א\rb* \rb fight|תִּלָּ֣חֲמ֔וּ\rb* \rb with anyone|אֶת־\rb*, \rb small|קָטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb or great|גָּד֑וֹל\rb*, \rb except|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִֽם־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לְבַדּֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 32 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb When the chariot|הָרֶ֜כֶב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb saw|כִּרְאוֹת֩\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט\rb*, \rb they|וְהֵ֤מָּה\rb* \rb said|אָֽמְרוּ֙\rb*, “\rb Surely|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb this|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb*!” \rb So they turned|וַיָּסֻ֥רוּ\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֑ם\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֖יו\rb*, \rb but Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָֽט׃\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּזְעַ֖ק\rb*. \v 33 \rb And|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb when the chariot|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb saw|כִּרְאוֹת֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb was not|לֹא־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb they turned back|וַיָּשׁ֖וּבוּ\rb* \rb from pursuing him|מֵאַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 34 \rb However, a certain man|וְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb drew|מָשַׁ֤ךְ\rb* \rb his bow|בַּקֶּ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb without taking special aim|לְתֻמּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he struck|וַיַּכֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the joints|הַדְּבָקִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of his armor|הַשִּׁרְיָ֑ן\rb*. \rb So the king said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to his charioteer|לְרַכָּב֗וֹ\rb*, “\rb Turn around|הֲפֹ֥ךְ\rb*\rb |יָדְךָ֛\rb*\f + \fr 22:34 \ft Literally \fqa Turn your hand\f* \rb and take me out|וְהוֹצִיאֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the battle|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I am badly wounded|הָחֳלֵֽיתִי׃\rb*!”
\p \v 35 \rb The battle|הַמִּלְחָמָה֙\rb* \rb raged|וַתַּעֲלֶ֤ה\rb* \rb throughout that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb and the king|וְהַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֧ה\rb* \rb propped up|מָעֳמָ֛ד\rb* \rb in his chariot|בַּמֶּרְכָּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb facing|נֹ֣כַח\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֑ם\rb*. \rb And the blood|דַּֽם־\rb* \rb from his wound|הַמַּכָּ֖ה\rb* \rb ran out|וַיִּ֥צֶק\rb* \rb onto|אֶל־\rb* \rb the floor|חֵ֥יק\rb* \rb of the chariot|הָרָֽכֶב׃\rb*, \rb and that evening|בָּעֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb he died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb*. \v 36 \rb As the sun|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb* \rb was setting|כְּבֹ֥א\rb*, \rb the cry|הָרִנָּה֙\rb* \rb rang out|וַיַּעֲבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb in the army|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Every man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own city|עִיר֖וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and every man|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own land|אַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 37 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb and was brought|וַיָּב֖וֹא\rb* \rb to Samaria|שֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb*, \rb where they buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |בְּשֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 38 \rb And the chariot|הָרֶ֜כֶב\rb* \rb was washed|וַיִּשְׁטֹ֨ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb at|עַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the pool|בְּרֵכַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְר֗וֹן\rb* \rb where the prostitutes|וְהַזֹּנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb bathed|רָחָ֑צוּ\rb*,\f + \fr 22:38 \ft Or \fqa the pool of Samaria, where they cleaned the weapons\f* \rb and the dogs|הַכְּלָבִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb licked up|וַיָּלֹ֤קּוּ\rb* \rb Ahab’s blood|דָּמ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb that the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֵּֽר׃\rb*.\f + \fr 22:38 \ft See 1 Kings 21:19.\f*
\p \v 39 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶתֶר֩\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֜ב\rb*, \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֗ה\rb* \rb and the ivory|הַשֵּׁן֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb palace|וּבֵ֤ית\rb*\rb |בָּנָ֔ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the cities|הֶעָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he built|בָּנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*?
\p \v 40 \rb And Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*.
\s1 Jehoshaphat Reigns in Judah
\r (2 Chronicles 20:31–34)
\p \v 41 \rb In the fourth|אַרְבַּ֔ע\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Ahab’s|לְאַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \rb Jehoshaphat|וִיהֽוֹשָׁפָט֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Asa|אָסָ֔א\rb* \rb became king|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \v 42 \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט\rb* \rb was thirty-five|שְׁלֹשִׁ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb old|בֶּן־\rb* \rb when he became king|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb twenty-five|וְעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*. \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Azubah|עֲזוּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Shilhi|שִׁלְחִֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb And Jehoshaphat walked|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the ways|דֶּ֛רֶךְ\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֥א\rb*; \rb he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֣ר\rb* \rb from them|מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb*, \rb but did|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \rb The high places|הַבָּמ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb however|אַ֥ךְ\rb*, \rb were not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb removed|סָ֑רוּ\rb*; \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb still|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb sacrificed|מְזַבְּחִ֥ים\rb* \rb and burned incense|וּֽמְקַטְּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb on the high places|בַּבָּמֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 44 \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb also made peace|וַיַּשְׁלֵ֥ם\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 45 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֛ט\rb*, \rb along with the might|וּגְבוּרָת֥וֹ\rb* \rb he exercised|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he waged war|נִלְחָ֑ם\rb*, \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹֽא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*? \v 46 \rb He banished|בִּעֵ֖ר\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb the|וְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb male shrine prostitutes|הַקָּדֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb remained|נִשְׁאַ֔ר\rb* \rb from the days|בִּימֵ֖י\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Asa|אָסָ֣א\rb*. \v 47 \rb And there was no|אֵ֛ין\rb* \rb king|וּמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Edom|בֶּאֱד֖וֹם\rb*; \rb a deputy|נִצָּ֥ב\rb* \rb served as king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 48 \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֡ט\rb* \rb built|עָשָׂר\rb* \rb ships|אֳנִיּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb of Tarshish|תַּרְשִׁ֜ישׁ\rb*\f + \fr 22:48 \ft Or \fqa a fleet of trading ships\f* \rb to go|לָלֶ֧כֶת\rb* \rb to Ophir|אוֹפִ֛ירָה\rb* \rb for gold|לַזָּהָ֖ב\rb*, \rb but they never|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb set sail|הָלָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they|אֳנִיּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |בְּעֶצְי֥וֹן\rb* \rb were wrecked|נִשְׁבְּרָה\rb* \rb at Ezion-geber|גָּֽבֶר׃\rb*. \v 49 \rb At that time|אָ֠ז\rb* \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְה֣וֹשָׁפָ֔ט\rb*, “\rb Let my servants|עֲבָדַ֛י\rb* \rb sail|יֵלְכ֧וּ\rb*\rb |בָּאֳנִיּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֖יךָ\rb*,” \rb but Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָֽט׃\rb* \rb refused|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |אָבָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 50 \rb And Jehoshaphat|יְהֽוֹשָׁפָט֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵר֙\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb them|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb in the city|בְּעִ֖יר\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֣ד\rb*. \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֥ם\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Ahaziah Reigns in Israel
\r (2 Kings 1:1–16)
\p \v 51 \rb In the seventeenth|שְׁבַ֣ע\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֔ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat’s|לִיהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֗ב\rb* \rb became king|מָלַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb and he reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb two years|שְׁנָתָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 52 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and walked|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדֶ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִיו֙\rb* \rb and|וּבְדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb mother|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and|וּבְדֶ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֔ט\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to sin|הֶחֱטִ֖יא\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 53 \rb Ahaziah served|וַֽיַּעֲבֹד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and worshiped|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb Baal|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb*, \rb provoking|וַיַּכְעֵ֗ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel, to anger|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*.
